/* Lecture 4 video lecture data: chapters, slide start times, timed bilingual transcript (generated). */
window.LEC = {"num":4,"videoBase":"https://wabyking.github.io/nlp2026-videos-1/lecture04/","parts":[{"n":1,"title":"NLP Tasks, Pre-training and Why Transformers","blurb":"From language-model recap and pre-training to classification, segmentation, span prediction and translation: the tasks a contextual encoder must serve.","file":"lecture04_part1.mp4","poster":"lecture04_part1.jpg","duration":1063.4,"first":1,"last":17,"slides":[{"n":1,"title":"Title: Lecture 4","t":0.8},{"n":2,"title":"Language Models: Recap","t":28.09},{"n":3,"title":"Example of a Bigram Language Model","t":48.22},{"n":4,"title":"Generating Shakespeare","t":95.27},{"n":5,"title":"Masked Language Models","t":137.63},{"n":6,"title":"Pre-training and Fine-tuning","t":167.75},{"n":7,"title":"Three Pre-training Architectures","t":289.45},{"n":8,"title":"Lecture Roadmap","t":327.3},{"n":9,"title":"Typical NLP Applications","t":364.07},{"n":10,"title":"Sentence-level Classification","t":430.22},{"n":11,"title":"Word Segmentation","t":486.97},{"n":12,"title":"Example:","t":569.67},{"n":13,"title":"Span Prediction","t":632.42},{"n":14,"title":"Translation: Generate One Token at a Time","t":793.22},{"n":15,"title":"Building a Contextual Encoder","t":900.41},{"n":16,"title":"Neural Network Architectures","t":976.57},{"n":17,"title":"Why Transformer?","t":1012.48}],"sents":[[0.8,3.19,1,"Hello everyone, and welcome back!","大家好，欢迎回来！"],[3.54,6.78,1,"This is Lecture four: Transformer and Beyond.","这是第四讲：Transformer 及其之后。"],[7.13,12.15,1,"Last lecture, we described language modeling as predicting words from context.","上一讲，我们把语言建模描述为根据上下文预测词。"],[12.5,17.64,1,"Today we ask a deeper question: how should a neural network organize that context?","今天我们问一个更深的问题：神经网络应该如何组织这些上下文？"],[17.99,25.26,1,"We will connect token interaction and feature transformation to the Transformer, and then examine scaling.","我们会把词元之间的交互和特征变换与 Transformer 联系起来，然后再讨论规模化。"],[25.61,26.69,1,"Let's get started!","我们开始吧！"],[27.94,32.42,2,"Before discussing architectures, let's recall the prediction problem they solve.","在讨论模型架构之前，我们先回顾一下它们要解决的预测问题。"],[32.77,39.23,2,"For each example, ask two questions: what context is available, and what is the output distribution?","对每个例子，都问两个问题：可用的上下文是什么？输出的分布又是什么？"],[39.58,46.82,2,"These two questions will help us compare statistical language models, masked models, and autoregressive models.","这两个问题能帮助我们比较统计语言模型、掩码模型和自回归模型。"],[48.07,53.02,3,"Let's use this short passage from Alice in Wonderland as our entire training corpus.","我们把这段《爱丽丝梦游仙境》的短文当作全部训练语料。"],[53.37,59.51,3,"We count a word only after its immediate predecessor. This is a bigram model.","我们只统计一个词紧跟在哪个前一个词之后出现。这就是二元语法模型，也就是 bigram 模型。"],[59.86,65.89,3,"After the word tired, the observed continuation is of, so its probability is one.","在 tired 之后，观察到的后续词是 of，所以它的概率是 1。"],[66.24,70.85,3,"After was, the words beginning and reading each receive one half.","在 was 之后，beginning 和 reading 各占二分之一。"],[71.2,76.22,3,"These are estimates from this tiny sample, not universal probabilities.","这些只是从这个很小的样本里得到的估计，并不是普遍成立的概率。"],[76.57,84.21,3,"After the word the, three observed continuations, bank, book and use, each receive one third.","在 the 之后，观察到三个后续词：bank、book 和 use，各占三分之一。"],[84.56,90.68,3,"A longer history might tell these situations apart, but our model deliberately throws that history away.","更长的历史也许能区分这些情况，但我们的模型刻意把这些历史丢掉了。"],[91.03,93.87,3,"So what does that mean for generation? Let's see.","那这对文本生成意味着什么？我们来看一看。"],[95.12,101.98,4,"These Shakespeare-style samples show what changes as a statistical language model sees more context.","这些莎士比亚风格的生成样例展示了：当统计语言模型看到更多上下文时，会发生什么变化。"],[102.33,107.18,4,"The unigram samples at the top read like a random bag of words.","最上面的 unigram 样例读起来就像一堆随机的词。"],[107.53,116.59,4,"Moving down through bigram, trigram and quadrigram, longer contexts tend to preserve more plausible local phrases.","往下看 bigram、trigram 和 quadrigram，上下文越长，越能保留看起来合理的局部短语。"],[116.94,123.77,4,"However, a sentence that resembles the source can still fail to express a coherent idea across the passage.","然而，一个看起来很像原文的句子，在整段话里仍然可能表达不出连贯的意思。"],[124.12,129.51,4,"Try it yourself: find one convincing local phrase, and one place where the meaning breaks.","大家自己试试：找出一个令人信服的局部短语，再找出一处意思断裂的地方。"],[129.86,136.23,4,"This distinction motivates representations that can use broader contextual information.","正是这种区别，促使我们去寻找能够利用更广泛上下文信息的表示。"],[137.48,142.89,5,"A masked language model hides selected input words and predicts them from the surrounding text.","掩码语言模型会遮住输入中的一些词，再根据周围的文本把它们预测出来。"],[143.24,147.65,5,"The familiar setup masks fifteen percent of the input words.","常见的做法是遮住百分之十五的输入词。"],[148.0,153.12,5,"In this example, both earlier and later words help recover store and gallon.","在这个例子里，前面的词和后面的词都能帮助恢复 store 和 gallon。"],[153.47,157.94,5,"The key architectural point is that the model can use both directions.","架构上的关键点是：模型可以同时利用两个方向的信息。"],[158.29,162.61,5,"This is different from predicting the next word with only a left context.","这和只用左侧上下文去预测下一个词是不同的。"],[162.96,166.35,5,"Keep that difference in mind when we compare attention masks later.","请记住这个区别，之后我们比较注意力掩码时还会用到。"],[167.6,172.59,6,"Now let's contrast two learning objectives, with the same encoder on both sides.","现在我们来对比两种学习目标，两边用的是同一个编码器。"],[172.94,176.39,6,"Pre-training reads text without task-specific labels.","预训练读的是没有任务标签的文本。"],[176.74,184.48,6,"A selected word is hidden, and the contextual state at that position predicts the original word through a vocabulary head.","某个词被遮住，该位置的上下文状态通过一个词表输出头来预测原来的词。"],[184.83,187.87,6,"In this teaching example, the original word is mat.","在这个教学例子里，原来的词是 mat。"],[188.22,195.46,6,"The distribution assigns seventy-two percent to mat, eighteen percent to floor, and ten percent to all other words together.","这个分布给 mat 百分之七十二，给 floor 百分之十八，其余所有词合起来占百分之十。"],[195.81,200.35,6,"These probabilities are hand-chosen illustrations, not measurements from BERT.","这些概率是为了示意而手工设定的，并不是 BERT 的实测结果。"],[200.7,206.33,6,"And the four colored squares are a compressed view of a much larger contextual vector.","这四个彩色方块，是一个大得多的上下文向量的压缩示意。"],[206.68,211.8,6,"Next, we copy the learned encoder parameters to initialize the downstream model.","接下来，我们把学到的编码器参数复制过去，用来初始化下游模型。"],[212.15,217.57,6,"This arrow transfers weights, not the current sentence or its hidden states.","这个箭头传递的是权重，而不是当前的句子或它的隐藏状态。"],[217.92,222.54,6,"At initialization, the two yellow encoders have the same architecture.","在初始化时，这两个黄色编码器的结构完全相同。"],[222.89,229.12,6,"Now a labeled sentiment example, A surprisingly good film, passes through the initialized encoder.","现在，一个带标签的情感样本 A surprisingly good film 经过这个初始化好的编码器。"],[229.47,234.93,6,"A classification head uses the CLS representation to predict the sentence label.","分类头利用 CLS 位置的表示来预测句子的标签。"],[235.28,242.9,6,"The illustrative class probabilities are positive eighty-five percent and negative fifteen percent, and the task label is positive.","示意的类别概率是正面百分之八十五、负面百分之十五，而任务标签是正面。"],[243.25,247.37,6,"Notice that this head has a different output space from the vocabulary head.","注意，这个分类头的输出空间和词表输出头是不同的。"],[247.72,254.16,6,"Finally, we compute the classification loss and backpropagate through both the task head and the encoder.","最后，我们计算分类损失，并通过任务头和编码器一起反向传播。"],[254.51,260.62,6,"Fine-tuning adapts all these parameters jointly. The reused encoder does not need to stay frozen.","微调会联合调整所有这些参数，复用的编码器并不需要冻结。"],[260.97,267.27,6,"The diagram shows the flow of one training step. It does not claim a measured change in accuracy.","这张图展示的是一步训练的流程，并不代表实测的准确率变化。"],[267.62,271.69,6,"This page isolates masked language modeling and sentence classification.","这一页只单独展示了掩码语言建模和句子分类。"],[272.04,280.51,6,"The original BERT also uses a next-sentence prediction objective during pre-training, and later BERT-style systems may modify that recipe.","原始的 BERT 在预训练时还使用了下一句预测目标，而后来的 BERT 类模型可能会修改这套方案。"],[280.86,288.05,6,"Next, an architecture comparison explains why bidirectional context is so useful for these encoders.","接下来，我们通过比较不同架构，来解释为什么双向上下文对这些编码器如此有用。"],[289.3,294.2,7,"Let's compare three pre-training architectures by the context each one can see.","我们按照每种架构能看到的上下文，来比较三种预训练架构。"],[294.55,301.85,7,"An encoder can read both sides of an input position, so it is useful for representation learning.","编码器可以读取某个输入位置两侧的内容，因此适合做表示学习。"],[302.2,307.64,7,"A decoder uses a causal context, which matches left-to-right generation.","解码器使用因果上下文，正好对应从左到右的生成。"],[307.99,315.29,7,"An encoder-decoder first represents a source sequence, and then generates a target conditioned on that source.","编码器-解码器先对源序列进行表示，再以这个源序列为条件生成目标序列。"],[315.64,320.83,7,"The lesson is that visibility constraints and learning objectives work together.","要点是：可见性约束和学习目标是相辅相成的。"],[321.18,325.9,7,"Later, we will find these same differences inside the Transformer diagram.","之后，我们会在 Transformer 的结构图里找到这些同样的区别。"],[327.15,329.12,8,"Here is our roadmap for today.","这是我们今天的路线图。"],[329.47,334.51,8,"We start with NLP tasks and representations, the topic shown in bold.","我们从 NLP 任务和表示开始，也就是加粗显示的这一部分。"],[334.86,339.91,8,"Then we look at inductive bias: semantic abstraction and composition.","然后我们讨论归纳偏置：语义抽象与语义组合。"],[340.26,349.24,8,"The architecture section groups four families: multilayer perceptrons, convolutional networks, recurrent networks, and the Transformer.","架构部分包含四类模型：多层感知机、卷积网络、循环网络和 Transformer。"],[349.59,354.89,8,"So we first establish the prediction tasks and the role of inductive bias.","所以，我们先明确预测任务以及归纳偏置的作用。"],[355.24,362.67,8,"Then we compare how these four families combine token information, before moving to scaling laws and emergence.","然后比较这四类模型如何整合词元信息，最后再讲规模定律和涌现。"],[363.92,369.47,9,"This overview uses four distinct examples, so each output structure is easy to recognize.","这张总览图用了四个不同的例子，让每种输出结构都容易辨认。"],[369.82,377.32,9,"In the middle sits a shared contextual encoder. It combines input words into context-sensitive features.","中间是一个共享的上下文编码器，它把输入的词组合成依赖上下文的特征。"],[377.67,383.89,9,"This is an architectural role. Different trained task systems need not share identical parameter values.","这里说的是一种架构上的角色，不同任务训练出来的系统并不需要共享完全相同的参数。"],[384.24,387.63,9,"Task one predicts one sentiment label for a sentence.","任务一：为一个句子预测一个情感标签。"],[387.98,395.22,9,"Task two partitions a Chinese character sequence into words, here Nanjing shi, and Changjiang daqiao.","任务二：把一串汉字切分成词，这里切成“南京市”和“长江大桥”。"],[395.57,402.06,9,"Task three extracts a contiguous answer from a passage, by predicting its start and end positions.","任务三：通过预测起始和结束位置，从一段文本中抽取出一个连续的答案。"],[402.41,404.76,9,"Task four produces new text.","任务四：生成新的文本。"],[405.11,411.82,9,"In translation, a decoder conditions on the encoded source and the target words already generated.","在翻译中，解码器以编码后的源句以及已经生成的目标词为条件。"],[412.17,417.61,9,"We will return to this exact translation when we discuss convolutional sequence-to-sequence models.","等讲到卷积序列到序列模型时，我们还会回到这个翻译例子。"],[417.96,424.49,9,"In every case, a task head or decoder turns contextual representations into the required output.","无论哪种情况，都是由任务头或解码器把上下文表示转换成所需的输出。"],[424.84,428.82,9,"Let's now open up each prediction interface, one at a time.","下面我们逐一打开每种预测接口来看。"],[430.07,436.08,10,"Task one: sentence-level classification. Take the sentence, This film feels warm.","任务一：句子级分类。看这个句子：This film feels warm。"],[436.43,439.91,10,"We want one sentiment decision for the entire sentence.","我们希望对整个句子做出一个情感判断。"],[440.26,444.56,10,"The shared contextual encoder produces a vector at every token.","共享的上下文编码器会在每个词元位置产生一个向量。"],[444.91,451.26,10,"The colored components visualize feature dimensions. We do not give them invented semantic names.","这些彩色分量表示特征维度，我们不会给它们编造什么语义名称。"],[451.61,456.09,10,"Then we average the four token vectors to obtain one sentence vector.","然后，我们把四个词元向量取平均，得到一个句子向量。"],[456.44,463.62,10,"Mean pooling is a simple example of aggregation. Other encoders may use a designated classification token instead.","平均池化是一种简单的聚合方式，其他编码器也可能使用一个专门的分类词元。"],[463.97,466.99,10,"The task head maps this vector to class scores.","任务头把这个向量映射成各个类别的分数。"],[467.34,473.18,10,"The number of output scores equals the number of classes, not some arbitrary hidden-layer width.","输出分数的个数等于类别数，而不是某个随意的隐藏层宽度。"],[473.53,477.32,10,"Here, Positive is the illustrative selected label.","这里，Positive 是示意中被选中的标签。"],[477.67,481.33,10,"So we have reduced several token vectors to one decision.","这样，我们就把多个词元向量归结成了一个决策。"],[481.68,485.57,10,"The next task keeps a decision aligned with every character.","下一个任务则要为每一个字都做出一个对应的决策。"],[486.82,490.99,11,"Task two predicts a structure over the input characters.","任务二要在输入的字上预测一种结构。"],[491.34,498.51,11,"Read the unsegmented example from left to right: Nanjing shi Changjiang daqiao, the Nanjing Yangtze River Bridge.","从左到右读这个未切分的例子：南京市长江大桥。"],[498.86,503.19,11,"The shared contextual encoder produces a vector for every character.","共享的上下文编码器为每个字都产生一个向量。"],[503.54,511.33,11,"A fixed copy of the input appears on the output row, so we can mark boundaries without moving or reassembling the characters.","输出行上放了一份固定的输入副本，这样我们就能标出边界，而不用移动或重新拼接这些字。"],[511.68,517.86,11,"Then a shared tag head predicts B, I, E, B, I, I, E.","然后，一个共享的标签预测头输出 B、I、E、B、I、I、E。"],[518.21,526.97,11,"B marks the beginning of a word, I an inside character, E the end, and S a word with only one character.","B 表示词的开头，I 表示词的中间，E 表示词的结尾，S 表示只有一个字的词。"],[527.32,532.02,11,"Other equivalent tag conventions exist. This slide uses BIES.","也存在其他等价的标注方案，这一页用的是 BIES。"],[532.37,540.18,11,"The first B, I, E group and its three characters form one word: Nanjing shi, Nanjing City.","第一组 B、I、E 及其对应的三个字构成一个词：南京市。"],[540.53,549.39,11,"The second B, I, I, E group and its four characters give Changjiang daqiao, the Yangtze River Bridge.","第二组 B、I、I、E 及其对应的四个字构成：长江大桥。"],[549.74,553.77,11,"So the final segmentation is Nanjing City, then Yangtze River Bridge.","所以最终的切分结果是：南京市 / 长江大桥。"],[554.12,558.21,11,"No character is added, removed, duplicated, or moved.","没有任何字被增加、删除、重复或移动。"],[558.56,563.83,11,"This is a boundary prediction problem, unlike the single sentence label in Task one.","这是一个边界预测问题，和任务一中整个句子只有一个标签不同。"],[564.18,568.27,11,"The next task selects a span from an evidence passage.","下一个任务是从一段证据文本中选出一个片段。"],[569.52,574.62,12,"Before we open up the mechanics of span prediction, here is a real example of the format.","在深入讲解片段预测的机制之前，先看一个这种格式的真实例子。"],[574.97,582.86,12,"The query is a sentence with a blank: an Imagist poem by blank, published in nineteen thirteen.","查询是一个带空格的句子：一首意象派诗歌，作者是某某，发表于 1913 年。"],[583.21,585.4,12,"The passage happens to contain the answer.","这段文本恰好包含了答案。"],[585.75,593.55,12,"The model's job is not to write a new answer, but to point at it: mark where Ezra Pound starts and where it ends in the passage.","模型的任务不是写出一个新答案，而是把它指出来：标出 Ezra Pound 在文本中从哪里开始、到哪里结束。"],[593.9,598.6,12,"The diagram on the left shows something nice about this paper's approach.","左边这张图展示了这篇论文方法的一个巧妙之处。"],[598.95,602.3,12,"You can build huge numbers of these instances automatically.","你可以自动构造出海量这样的训练样本。"],[602.65,608.66,12,"Take a sentence from a corpus, blank out a term, and retrieve passages that mention it.","从语料库中取一个句子，把某个词挖空，再检索出提到这个词的文本段落。"],[609.01,613.69,12,"Then you have a reading-comprehension exercise with no human labeling.","这样你就得到了一道阅读理解题，完全不需要人工标注。"],[614.04,619.25,12,"So span selection can serve as a pre-training task, not only as a downstream task.","所以，片段选择不仅可以作为下游任务，也可以作为预训练任务。"],[619.6,624.5,12,"Keep the output format in mind: two positions, a start and an end.","请记住这种输出格式：两个位置，一个起点和一个终点。"],[624.85,631.02,12,"Next, we will see exactly how a model scores those two positions and picks the best span.","接下来我们会看到，模型究竟如何给这两个位置打分，并选出最佳片段。"],[632.27,638.96,13,"Task three extracts an answer from evidence. The question is: Where was Marie Curie born?","任务三是从证据中抽取答案。问题是：居里夫人出生在哪里？"],[639.31,645.91,13,"In common extractive question answering systems, the question and the passage are encoded jointly.","在常见的抽取式问答系统中，问题和文本段落是一起编码的。"],[646.26,651.53,13,"The contextual encoder produces evidence features conditioned on the question.","上下文编码器产生以问题为条件的证据特征。"],[651.88,660.86,13,"The token positions are fixed: Marie is one, Curie two, and so on, up to Warsaw at six and Poland at seven.","词元的位置是固定的：Marie 是 1，Curie 是 2，依此类推，Warsaw 是 6，Poland 是 7。"],[661.21,665.94,13,"One prediction head assigns a probability to each possible start position.","一个预测头为每个可能的起始位置分配一个概率。"],[666.29,675.25,13,"For clarity, focus on two starts: position six has probability zero point six zero, and position seven has zero point two five.","为了清楚起见，只看两个起点：位置 6 的概率是 0.60，位置 7 是 0.25。"],[675.6,681.77,13,"The remaining start probability, zero point one five, is spread across positions one to five.","剩下的 0.15 的起点概率分布在位置 1 到 5 上。"],[682.12,685.98,13,"A separate prediction head assigns end probabilities.","另一个独立的预测头负责分配终点概率。"],[686.33,695.56,13,"Position six has zero point two five and position seven has zero point six five, and the remaining zero point one zero is spread over positions one to five.","位置 6 是 0.25，位置 7 是 0.65，剩下的 0.10 分布在位置 1 到 5 上。"],[695.91,701.22,13,"Start and end are two predictions, not a single categorical span label.","起点和终点是两个独立的预测，而不是一个单一的片段类别标签。"],[701.57,704.18,13,"Now pair start six with both ends.","现在把起点 6 和两个终点分别配对。"],[704.53,713.51,13,"The span from six to six is Warsaw, with score zero point six zero times zero point two five, which is zero point one five.","从 6 到 6 的片段是 Warsaw，得分是 0.60 乘 0.25，等于 0.15。"],[713.86,722.82,13,"The span from six to seven is Warsaw, Poland, with score zero point six zero times zero point six five, which is zero point three nine.","从 6 到 7 的片段是 Warsaw, Poland，得分是 0.60 乘 0.65，等于 0.39。"],[723.17,727.46,13,"The table holds the full set of combinations, not only the top candidate.","这张表包含了所有的组合，而不只是排名第一的候选。"],[727.81,730.64,13,"Next, pair start seven with both ends.","接着，把起点 7 和两个终点配对。"],[730.99,739.43,13,"The pair seven to six has a score of zero point zero six two five, but the start comes after the end, so we discard it.","7 到 6 这一对的得分是 0.0625，但起点在终点之后，所以要丢弃。"],[739.78,748.52,13,"The span from seven to seven is Poland, with score zero point two five times zero point six five, which is zero point one six two five.","从 7 到 7 的片段是 Poland，得分是 0.25 乘 0.65，等于 0.1625。"],[748.87,754.82,13,"Among all four displayed pairs, Warsaw, Poland is the highest-scoring valid span.","在这四对组合中，Warsaw, Poland 是得分最高的有效片段。"],[755.17,761.31,13,"Ranking valid pairs resolves conflicts between boundaries that each head favored independently.","对有效配对进行排序，可以解决两个预测头各自偏好的边界之间的冲突。"],[761.66,766.27,13,"In practice, implementations may also impose a maximum answer length.","在实际实现中，通常还会限制答案的最大长度。"],[766.62,775.25,13,"And the best omitted pair cannot exceed zero point one zero times zero point six five, so it cannot change the selected answer.","而被省略的配对中，得分最高的也不会超过 0.10 乘 0.65，所以不会改变选出的答案。"],[775.6,785.14,13,"A small historical note: Warsaw was within the Russian Empire when Curie was born in eighteen sixty-seven. The evidence gives its present-day country.","一个小小的历史注脚：居里夫人 1867 年出生时，华沙属于俄罗斯帝国；这段证据给出的是它现在所属的国家。"],[785.49,791.82,13,"Next, Task four generates an answer sequence, rather than selecting positions in the input.","接下来，任务四要生成一个答案序列，而不是在输入中选择位置。"],[793.07,802.55,14,"Task four is translation: the source is the Chinese sentence wo xihuan zhebu dianying, and the target will be I like this movie.","任务四是翻译：源句是“我 喜欢 这部 电影”，要生成的目标是 I like this movie。"],[802.9,806.55,14,"Prediction and copying are deliberately separate steps.","预测和复制被刻意分成了两个独立的步骤。"],[806.9,812.48,14,"First, we encode the Chinese source once, and prepare the start marker in the target prefix.","首先，我们对中文源句编码一次，并在目标前缀中放入起始标记。"],[812.83,818.18,14,"The decoder is conditioned on the encoded source and on the existing prefix.","解码器以编码后的源句和已有的前缀为条件。"],[818.53,823.82,14,"With only the start marker in the prefix, the decoder predicts I in the next-token box.","在前缀只有起始标记时，解码器在“下一个词元”框中预测出 I。"],[824.17,829.86,14,"This is a vocabulary prediction. I has not yet been appended to the prefix.","这是一个词表上的预测，此时 I 还没有被追加到前缀中。"],[830.21,836.27,14,"Then we follow the return arrow, append I to its prefix slot, and clear the output.","然后我们沿着回传箭头，把 I 追加到前缀的位置上，并清空输出。"],[836.62,844.4,14,"Now the prefix is start, I. We use it to predict like, and the prefix does not change during this prediction.","现在前缀是起始标记加 I，我们用它来预测 like，预测过程中前缀保持不变。"],[844.75,849.39,14,"We append like, and with that prefix unchanged, predict this.","我们把 like 追加进去，然后在前缀不变的情况下预测 this。"],[849.74,857.22,14,"We copy this into the next fixed slot, and then predict movie from the source and the prefix, start, I like this.","把 this 复制到下一个固定位置，再根据源句和前缀“起始标记 I like this”预测 movie。"],[857.57,863.29,14,"After movie is appended, the complete prefix is start, I like this movie.","movie 追加之后，完整的前缀就是“起始标记 I like this movie”。"],[863.64,870.05,14,"Finally, the decoder predicts the end-of-sequence marker, EOS, and generation stops.","最后，解码器预测出序列结束标记 EOS，生成停止。"],[870.4,873.64,14,"EOS is not appended as another content word.","EOS 不会作为另一个内容词被追加到前缀中。"],[873.99,879.34,14,"This illustrates autoregressive inference, using previously generated target tokens.","这展示的是自回归推理：利用之前已经生成的目标词元。"],[879.69,885.83,14,"Training with teacher forcing uses the reference prefix instead. We will develop that distinction later.","而用 teacher forcing 训练时，用的是参考答案的前缀。这个区别我们之后再展开。"],[886.18,890.75,14,"The decoder may be convolutional, recurrent, or attention-based.","解码器可以是卷积的、循环的，也可以是基于注意力的。"],[891.1,899.01,14,"And we will reuse this exact source and target pair in the convolutional sequence-to-sequence section.","在卷积序列到序列那一部分，我们还会用到这同一对源句和目标句。"],[900.26,907.81,15,"We have now seen four distinct tasks, and each one requires representations that include useful context.","我们已经看过了四种不同的任务，每一种都需要包含有用上下文的表示。"],[908.16,913.59,15,"So instead of introducing another task, let's open up the shared encoder.","所以，我们不再介绍新的任务，而是打开这个共享编码器看一看。"],[913.94,918.51,15,"First, embeddings turn vocabulary identities into vectors.","首先，词嵌入把词表中的身份标识变成向量。"],[918.86,923.52,15,"Second, an architecture specifies which tokens can exchange information.","其次，架构规定了哪些词元之间可以交换信息。"],[923.87,935.12,15,"A fixed-context MLP concatenates inputs, a CNN composes local windows, an RNN carries a recurrent state, and attention combines selected positions.","固定上下文的 MLP 把输入拼接起来，CNN 组合局部窗口，RNN 传递循环状态，而注意力则组合选定的位置。"],[935.47,941.38,15,"Third, learned nonlinear transformations turn the mixed information into useful features.","第三，学到的非线性变换把混合后的信息变成有用的特征。"],[941.73,948.28,15,"Mixing and transforming are a conceptual decomposition. Real layers may combine or interleave them.","混合与变换只是概念上的拆分，实际的网络层可能会把它们合并或交替进行。"],[948.63,953.54,15,"The resulting representations support the four interfaces, numbered one through four.","最终得到的表示支撑着编号为一到四的四种任务接口。"],[953.89,960.18,15,"A generative task additionally needs a decoder that respects the target-prefix visibility rule.","生成类任务还额外需要一个遵守目标前缀可见性规则的解码器。"],[960.53,968.15,15,"MLPs, CNNs, RNNs and Transformers use different rules for building these representations.","MLP、CNN、RNN 和 Transformer 用不同的规则来构建这些表示。"],[968.5,975.17,15,"We will first examine simple networks and their training, and then compare alternative sequence architectures.","我们先看简单的网络及其训练，再比较不同的序列架构。"],[976.42,980.84,16,"The same task interface can sit on top of very different networks.","同一个任务接口，可以架在非常不同的网络之上。"],[981.19,987.65,16,"It could be a multilayer perceptron, a convolutional network, a recurrent network, or a Transformer.","它可以是多层感知机、卷积网络、循环网络，也可以是 Transformer。"],[988.0,994.71,16,"To compare them, ask two questions: which input positions can influence a given output?","要比较它们，就问两个问题：哪些输入位置能够影响某个输出？"],[995.06,999.18,16,"And how many computational steps must that influence travel through?","这种影响又需要经过多少步计算才能传过去？"],[999.53,1002.53,16,"Names alone tell us very little about these paths.","光看名字，我们对这些路径几乎一无所知。"],[1002.88,1011.08,16,"So we will use token interaction as a common language for understanding the strengths and constraints of all four architectures.","所以我们将用词元交互作为共同的语言，来理解这四种架构各自的优势和局限。"],[1012.33,1016.7,17,"Let's pause on the question that drives this whole lecture: why the Transformer?","我们停下来思考一个贯穿整节课的问题：为什么是 Transformer？"],[1017.05,1019.2,17,"And no, not the robot on the left!","当然，不是左边这个机器人！"],[1019.55,1025.48,17,"Although the name fits: the model keeps transforming its token representations, layer after layer.","不过这个名字倒也贴切：这个模型一层接一层地不断变换词元的表示。"],[1025.83,1032.4,17,"The diagram on the right is the architecture from Attention Is All You Need, published in two thousand seventeen.","右边这张图，是 2017 年发表的论文 Attention Is All You Need 中的架构。"],[1032.75,1040.44,17,"Some version of it sits inside BERT, GPT, and essentially every large language model you will use in this course.","BERT、GPT，以及这门课里你会用到的几乎所有大语言模型，内部都有它的某种变体。"],[1040.79,1045.93,17,"If I just walked you through these boxes now, it would feel like memorizing a circuit diagram.","如果我现在就逐个讲解这些方框，感觉就像在死记一张电路图。"],[1046.28,1048.47,17,"So we will take a short detour first.","所以我们先绕一小段路。"],[1048.82,1056.23,17,"We will build two ideas, semantic abstraction and semantic composition, plus the notion of inductive bias.","我们要建立两个概念：语义抽象和语义组合，再加上归纳偏置这个概念。"],[1056.58,1061.51,17,"With those in hand, every box in this picture will have an obvious job.","有了这些概念，这张图里的每个方框的作用都会一目了然。"]]},{"n":2,"title":"Inductive Bias: Semantic Composition and Abstraction","blurb":"Two operations organise every architecture: composing tokens into larger meanings and abstracting features layer by layer, with different built-in assumptions about locality and order.","file":"lecture04_part2.mp4","poster":"lecture04_part2.jpg","duration":595.1,"first":18,"last":31,"slides":[{"n":18,"title":"Lecture Roadmap","t":0.8},{"n":19,"title":"Semantic Abstraction","t":31.07},{"n":20,"title":"Neural network layers","t":75.41},{"n":21,"title":"Semantic Composition","t":120.15},{"n":22,"title":"Composition and Abstraction","t":165.29},{"n":23,"title":"Combining Composition and Abstraction","t":206.55},{"n":24,"title":"Mean Pooling in CBOW","t":255.14},{"n":25,"title":"Inductive Bias in Composition","t":290.4},{"n":26,"title":"Local and Recurrent Composition","t":330.86},{"n":27,"title":"Limitations of CNNs and RNNs","t":360.34},{"n":28,"title":"Long-range Token Interaction","t":390.76},{"n":29,"title":"Weaker Inductive Bias","t":440.32},{"n":30,"title":"Global Token Interaction","t":500.83},{"n":31,"title":"Separating Composition and Abstraction","t":548.65}],"sents":[[0.8,7.82,18,"Back to our roadmap. We now move to part two: inductive bias, semantic abstraction and composition.","回到路线图。现在进入第二部分：归纳偏置、语义抽象与语义组合。"],[8.17,14.16,18,"We have just seen the prediction tasks. Now we ask what a good representation should be able to do.","我们刚刚看完了各种预测任务，现在要问：一个好的表示应该具备什么能力？"],[14.51,24.65,18,"These ideas will then guide how we compare the four architecture families: multilayer perceptrons, convolutional networks, recurrent networks, and the Transformer.","这些概念将指导我们比较四类架构：多层感知机、卷积网络、循环网络和 Transformer。"],[25.0,29.67,18,"And at the end, we will move to scaling laws and emergence.","最后，我们会讲到规模定律和涌现。"],[30.92,35.44,19,"Let's start with semantic abstraction, using a picture from computer vision.","我们先从语义抽象讲起，借用一张计算机视觉的图。"],[35.79,42.62,19,"This visual hierarchy moves from the raw input through deeper and deeper convolutional layers.","这个视觉层级从原始输入开始，经过越来越深的卷积层。"],[42.97,49.81,19,"The features move from pixels and textures toward regions, objects, relations and semantics.","特征从像素、纹理，逐步走向区域、物体、关系和语义。"],[50.16,55.89,19,"It is a useful illustration of why multiple layers can build increasingly complex features.","这很好地说明了，为什么多层网络能够构建越来越复杂的特征。"],[56.24,61.17,19,"However, language does not necessarily follow exactly the same hierarchy as vision.","不过，语言不一定遵循和视觉完全相同的层级结构。"],[61.52,69.94,19,"So use this figure as an analogy for repeated changes of representation, not as a literal map of linguistic processing.","所以，把这张图当作表示被反复变换的一个类比，而不是语言处理过程的字面写照。"],[70.29,74.01,19,"Now let's apply that idea to a next-word prediction example.","现在，我们把这个思路用到一个预测下一个词的例子上。"],[75.26,84.16,20,"Here, the input context is, I think therefore I, and the output is a prediction such as am.","这里的输入上下文是 I think therefore I，输出是一个预测，比如 am。"],[84.51,90.97,20,"Successive network layers repeatedly transform the context representation before the final prediction.","在做出最终预测之前，一层层的网络会反复变换上下文的表示。"],[91.32,100.95,20,"You can loosely compare these stages with the classic pipeline, from lexical and syntactic analysis up to discourse and pragmatics.","你可以粗略地把这些阶段和经典的分析流程相对应：从词法、句法分析，一直到篇章和语用。"],[101.3,104.3,20,"Depth can provide more expressive functions.","深度可以提供表达能力更强的函数。"],[104.65,112.0,20,"But this diagram alone does not tell us which tokens interact within each layer, and that missing detail matters.","但仅凭这张图，我们看不出每一层里哪些词元之间在交互，而这个缺失的细节很关键。"],[112.35,118.75,20,"Next, we separate the effect of transforming features from the effect of bringing different words together.","接下来，我们要把“变换特征”的作用和“把不同的词结合起来”的作用区分开。"],[120.0,123.37,21,"Let's begin with two separate images and words.","我们先看两张独立的图片和两个词。"],[123.72,127.42,21,"Ivory names a material, while tower names a structure.","Ivory，象牙，指的是一种材料；tower，塔，指的是一种建筑。"],[127.77,130.5,21,"Now put them together: ivory tower.","现在把它们放在一起：ivory tower，象牙塔。"],[130.85,137.41,21,"And here the picture is our own campus gate, because a university is the classic ivory tower.","这里的图片就是我们自己的校门，因为大学正是最典型的象牙塔。"],[137.76,142.81,21,"A phrase can acquire a conventional meaning that goes beyond a simple list of its component meanings.","一个短语可以获得一种约定俗成的含义，远远超出其组成部分含义的简单罗列。"],[143.16,150.4,21,"This is the general operation: semantic composition combines word meanings to interpret a larger expression.","这就是一般性的操作：语义组合把词义组合起来，用以理解更大的表达。"],[150.75,154.29,21,"The architectural implication is token interaction.","这在架构上的含义是：需要词元交互。"],[154.64,159.61,21,"A network needs some route by which one word can affect how another word is represented.","网络需要某种途径，让一个词能够影响另一个词的表示方式。"],[159.96,163.89,21,"Next, we contrast that route with feature transformation.","接下来，我们把这种途径和特征变换做个对比。"],[165.14,169.4,22,"Here, each vertical bar represents the feature vector of one token.","这里，每一根竖条代表一个词元的特征向量。"],[169.75,173.84,22,"We start with five separate input words: I think therefore I am.","我们从五个独立的输入词开始：I think therefore I am。"],[174.19,183.38,22,"The bracket and the resulting vector illustrate composition: information crosses token positions to form a combined representation.","括号和下面得到的向量展示的是组合：信息跨越不同词元位置，形成一个组合后的表示。"],[183.73,191.64,22,"The example on the right illustrates abstraction: a nonlinear transformation changes the features within one representation.","右边的例子展示的是抽象：一个非线性变换改变单个表示内部的特征。"],[191.99,196.6,22,"These operations can happen together, but they are conceptually different.","这两种操作可以同时发生，但在概念上是不同的。"],[196.95,205.15,22,"Keeping them separate will make the roles of attention and feed-forward layers easier to recognize when we reach the Transformer.","把它们区分开，等讲到 Transformer 时，我们就更容易认清注意力层和前馈层各自的作用。"],[206.4,217.49,23,"So how can a network do both composition and abstraction? One direct approach concatenates the context vectors and passes the result through an MLP.","那么，网络如何同时完成组合与抽象？一种直接的做法是把上下文向量拼接起来，再送进一个 MLP。"],[217.84,222.85,23,"This mixes token positions and feature dimensions together, in a single transformation.","这样，词元位置和特征维度就在同一个变换里被混合在一起。"],[223.2,228.34,23,"This is the idea behind the neural probabilistic language model of Bengio and colleagues.","这正是 Bengio 等人提出的神经概率语言模型背后的思想。"],[228.69,235.15,23,"The complexity shown here is order D squared times L squared, where D is the vector size and L is the context length.","这里给出的复杂度是 D 的平方乘以 L 的平方，其中 D 是向量维度，L 是上下文长度。"],[235.5,243.53,23,"This reflects the dense construction assumed on the slide. It is not a universal cost for every language model implementation.","这对应的是图中假设的全连接构造，并不是所有语言模型实现的通用开销。"],[243.88,248.5,23,"Concatenation also ties the input organization to a fixed context window.","拼接还会把输入的组织方式绑定在一个固定的上下文窗口上。"],[248.85,253.74,23,"Next, consider a cheaper alternative: averaging the context first.","接下来，我们看一个更省计算的替代方案：先对上下文取平均。"],[254.99,263.92,24,"CBOW, a variant of the MLP, first pools the context vectors, so token interaction happens through a simple average.","CBOW 是 MLP 的一种变体，它先对上下文向量做池化，所以词元交互只是通过一个简单的平均来完成。"],[264.27,270.39,24,"The following layers mainly transform the resulting features, rather than repeatedly exchanging token-specific information.","后面的各层主要是对得到的特征做变换，而不再反复交换各个词元特有的信息。"],[270.74,276.27,24,"This reduces the cost to order D squared, compared with a large concatenated input.","和巨大的拼接输入相比，这把复杂度降到了 D 的平方量级。"],[276.62,281.2,24,"But it loses fine-grained word order and positional distinctions.","但它丢失了细粒度的词序和位置区别。"],[281.55,289.0,24,"So this is a design tradeoff: a simpler interaction rule can be efficient, while restricting what the representation can preserve.","所以这是一种设计上的权衡：更简单的交互规则可以很高效，但也限制了表示所能保留的信息。"],[290.25,293.79,25,"This brings us to the key idea of inductive bias.","这就引出了一个关键概念：归纳偏置。"],[294.14,301.85,25,"An inductive bias is an assumption that helps a learning algorithm connect inputs to outputs.","归纳偏置是帮助学习算法把输入和输出联系起来的一种假设。"],[302.2,308.88,25,"In sequence modeling, one such assumption is about which tokens are allowed to interact, and along what paths.","在序列建模中，其中一种假设就是：哪些词元允许交互，以及沿着什么路径交互。"],[309.23,314.24,25,"And we want to decide this while also considering semantic abstraction at the same time.","而且在做这个决定时，我们还要同时考虑语义抽象。"],[314.59,320.73,25,"A local window, a recurrent state, and global attention encode different answers to this question.","局部窗口、循环状态和全局注意力，对这个问题给出了不同的答案。"],[321.08,329.46,25,"These are not merely implementation details. They influence which patterns a model can learn efficiently from the available data.","这些并不只是实现细节，它们会影响模型能从现有数据中高效学到哪些模式。"],[330.71,332.83,26,"Let's look at two classic answers.","我们来看两种经典的答案。"],[333.18,338.4,26,"First, the convolutional window: neighboring tokens are combined through a local operation.","首先是卷积窗口：相邻的词元通过一个局部操作被组合在一起。"],[338.75,344.74,26,"Then the recurrent state: the current token is combined with a summary carried from earlier positions.","然后是循环状态：当前词元与从前面位置传递过来的摘要信息组合在一起。"],[345.09,352.25,26,"Both perform composition, but one emphasizes locality, and the other emphasizes sequence order.","两者都在做组合，但一个强调局部性，另一个强调序列顺序。"],[352.6,358.94,26,"Next, we ask what happens when the decisive information lies far away from the word being predicted.","接下来我们要问：如果关键信息离要预测的词很远，会发生什么？"],[360.19,368.18,27,"A local CNN needs additional layers, wider windows, or another mechanism to connect distant positions.","局部的 CNN 需要更多的层、更宽的窗口，或者其他机制，才能把相距很远的位置联系起来。"],[368.53,374.75,27,"An RNN can carry information from far back, but that information must survive repeated state updates.","RNN 可以把很早之前的信息传递下来，但这些信息必须在一次次状态更新中存活下来。"],[375.1,379.2,27,"Neither statement means the architecture cannot model long-range dependencies.","这两点都不意味着这些架构无法建模长距离依赖。"],[379.55,383.13,27,"The issue is the length and difficulty of the information path.","问题在于信息路径的长度和传递的难度。"],[383.48,389.36,27,"The next examples make clear why language prediction sometimes depends on evidence far beyond the nearest few words.","接下来的例子会清楚地说明，为什么语言预测有时依赖于远在最近几个词之外的证据。"],[390.61,396.7,28,"Here are two Chinese examples from a dataset built to test word prediction with long-range context.","这里有两个中文例子，来自一个专门测试长距离上下文词预测的数据集。"],[397.05,401.48,28,"Before reading on, try to predict the missing word in each one yourself.","在往下看之前，大家先自己试着预测一下每个例子里缺失的词。"],[401.83,407.12,28,"In the first example, the earlier context establishes the character's fear and anger.","在第一个例子中，前面的上下文交代了人物的恐惧和愤怒。"],[407.47,412.86,28,"The target sentence then recalls that emotional state, and the answer is qifen, angry.","目标句再次唤起这种情绪，答案是“气愤”。"],[413.21,418.89,28,"In the second example, an earlier event identifies the role that the princess rejects.","在第二个例子中，前面发生的事件决定了公主要废掉的是哪个角色。"],[419.24,425.29,28,"She saw the prospective consort's bad behaviour, so the missing word is fuma, the prince consort.","她亲眼见到了准驸马的丑态，所以缺失的词是“驸马”。"],[425.64,431.01,28,"The real exercise is to point to the decisive sentence, not just to supply the answer.","真正的练习是指出起决定作用的那句话，而不只是给出答案。"],[431.36,438.92,28,"This makes the need for long-range context concrete, before we introduce more flexible token interactions.","这让我们在引入更灵活的词元交互之前，先具体地感受到对长距离上下文的需求。"],[440.17,445.73,29,"The previous slides compared fixed local and recurrent patterns of token interaction.","前面几页比较了固定的局部交互模式和循环交互模式。"],[446.08,452.08,29,"Here the question is: how can we compose tokens freely, with fewer structural constraints?","这里的问题是：我们如何在更少结构约束的情况下，自由地组合词元？"],[452.43,456.49,29,"The answer is to let data determine more of the token interactions.","答案是：让数据来决定更多的词元交互方式。"],[456.84,465.48,29,"Rich Sutton argues that general methods benefit from increasing computation, and can surpass methods built around detailed human knowledge.","Rich Sutton 认为，通用方法能从不断增长的算力中获益，并最终超越那些围绕精细人类知识构建的方法。"],[465.83,473.95,29,"In The Bitter Lesson, he writes that general methods that leverage computation are ultimately the most effective, and by a large margin.","在《苦涩的教训》中，他写道：利用算力的通用方法最终是最有效的，而且优势巨大。"],[474.3,478.49,29,"This motivates a preference for scalable learning mechanisms.","这促使我们更偏好可扩展的学习机制。"],[478.84,486.0,29,"But it does not mean every inductive bias is harmful, or that attention has no inductive bias.","但这并不意味着所有的归纳偏置都是有害的，也不意味着注意力机制没有归纳偏置。"],[486.35,490.98,29,"Weaker constraints still leave design choices about representation and learning.","约束更弱，依然需要在表示和学习上做出设计选择。"],[491.33,499.43,29,"So we will compare architectures by the constraints they impose, and by the computation their learning rules can exploit.","所以，我们会根据架构施加的约束，以及其学习规则能利用的计算量，来比较这些架构。"],[500.68,502.62,30,"Here is global token interaction.","这就是全局词元交互。"],[502.97,508.59,30,"The dense connections represent direct interactions between every pair of token positions.","这些稠密的连接表示每一对词元位置之间的直接交互。"],[508.94,515.48,30,"The n by n grid of attention scores on the left is the same picture, written as a matrix.","左边这个 n 乘 n 的注意力分数网格，是同一张图的矩阵写法。"],[515.83,523.29,30,"Self-attention assigns these weights based on content, but a mask still controls which connections are allowed.","自注意力根据内容来分配这些权重，但仍然由掩码来控制哪些连接是允许的。"],[523.64,528.24,30,"So how does the attention mask differ between BERT and GPT?","那么，BERT 和 GPT 的注意力掩码有什么不同？"],[528.59,539.16,30,"A bidirectional encoder like BERT can access both sides, whereas an autoregressive decoder like GPT must block future target positions.","像 BERT 这样的双向编码器可以看到两侧，而像 GPT 这样的自回归解码器必须屏蔽未来的目标位置。"],[539.51,547.25,30,"Thus, global interaction does not imply unrestricted visibility. The prediction task determines the allowed context.","因此，全局交互并不意味着可见性不受限制，允许看到的上下文是由预测任务决定的。"],[548.5,552.35,31,"Now let's read this diagram from the input tokens upward.","现在，我们从输入词元开始，自下而上地读这张图。"],[552.7,562.61,31,"Self-attention, labeled SAN, mixes information across positions and produces contextual vectors. This is the composition step.","自注意力，也就是图中的 SAN，在不同位置之间混合信息，产生上下文向量，这就是组合这一步。"],[562.96,569.55,31,"The feed-forward stage, FFN, then transforms each contextual vector independently, with shared parameters.","接着，前馈层 FFN 用共享的参数，独立地变换每一个上下文向量。"],[569.9,575.95,31,"It changes features without mixing positions at this stage. This is abstraction.","在这一步，它只改变特征，不混合位置。这就是抽象。"],[576.3,582.66,31,"The SAN and FFN blocks then repeat, alternating these two operations through depth.","然后 SAN 和 FFN 模块不断重复，在网络深度上交替进行这两种操作。"],[583.01,588.75,31,"This separation is the central connection between our conceptual framework and the Transformer architecture.","这种分离，正是我们的概念框架和 Transformer 架构之间最核心的联系。"],[589.1,593.22,31,"Next, we place it alongside the earlier alternatives.","接下来，我们把它和前面的几种替代方案放在一起比较。"]]},{"n":3,"title":"Multilayer Perceptrons and Neural Language Models","blurb":"Fully-connected layers, a word-embedding classifier trained from prediction error, training challenges, and Bengio's neural probabilistic language model as a first sequence model.","file":"lecture04_part3.mp4","poster":"lecture04_part3.jpg","duration":713.5,"first":32,"last":41,"slides":[{"n":32,"title":"Lecture Roadmap","t":0.8},{"n":33,"title":"Multilayer Perceptron","t":27.34},{"n":34,"title":"Fully-connected (FC) layers: All the units from one layer are fully connected to every unit of the next layer.","t":71.31},{"n":35,"title":"From Word Embeddings to a Classifier","t":139.02},{"n":36,"title":"Learning from Prediction Error","t":244.15},{"n":37,"title":"Challenges in Neural Network Training","t":357.57},{"n":38,"title":"Why Sequence Models?","t":455.35},{"n":39,"title":"A Neural Probabilistic Language Model","t":552.0},{"n":40,"title":"A neural network models a distribution over the next word. P(w | I am a good …) P(w | I am a great …)","t":602.74},{"n":41,"title":"From MLPs to Sequence Architectures","t":638.44}],"sents":[[0.8,5.09,32,"Now we reach part three: architectures for neural representations.","现在进入第三部分：神经表示的架构。"],[5.44,14.66,32,"This section groups four families under one heading: multilayer perceptrons, convolutional networks, recurrent networks, and the Transformer.","这一部分把四类模型放在同一个标题下：多层感知机、卷积网络、循环网络和 Transformer。"],[15.01,19.65,32,"We have established the prediction tasks and the role of inductive bias.","我们已经明确了预测任务以及归纳偏置的作用。"],[20.0,25.94,32,"Now we compare how each family combines token information, starting with the multilayer perceptron.","现在我们来比较每一类模型如何整合词元信息，先从多层感知机开始。"],[27.19,33.45,33,"An MLP stacks learned linear transformations and nonlinear activations.","MLP 把可学习的线性变换和非线性激活函数堆叠在一起。"],[33.8,41.02,33,"A perceptron can be seen as a single neuron: one output unit computed from a vector of input units.","感知机可以看作一个单独的神经元：由一组输入单元计算出一个输出单元。"],[41.37,50.14,33,"In a multilayer network, each unit combines features from the preceding layer, and multiple layers can represent more complex functions.","在多层网络中，每个单元组合前一层的特征，多层叠加就能表示更复杂的函数。"],[50.49,56.08,33,"Connect this diagram to semantic abstraction: the model repeatedly transforms its features.","把这张图和语义抽象联系起来：模型在不断地变换它的特征。"],[56.43,61.83,33,"But its ability to combine tokens depends on how those tokens are arranged in the input.","但它组合词元的能力，取决于这些词元在输入中是如何排列的。"],[62.18,69.91,33,"Next, let's distinguish two terms: fully connected and feed-forward, which describe different aspects of a network.","接下来，我们区分两个术语：全连接和前馈，它们描述的是网络的不同方面。"],[71.16,77.18,34,"A feed-forward neural network is one where the connections between units do not form any cycles.","前馈神经网络是指单元之间的连接不构成任何环路的网络。"],[77.53,86.1,34,"Information flows in one direction, layer by layer, from the input layer to the output layer. No outputs are passed back to lower layers.","信息沿一个方向逐层流动，从输入层流向输出层，不会有输出被传回更低的层。"],[86.45,94.02,34,"Fully connected describes something different: every unit in one layer connects to every unit in the next layer.","而“全连接”描述的是另一回事：一层中的每个单元都连接到下一层的每个单元。"],[94.37,101.28,34,"An MLP is a specific type of feed-forward network, while feed-forward network is the more general term.","MLP 是前馈网络的一种具体类型，而前馈网络是一个更宽泛的术语。"],[101.63,105.32,34,"The code shows a forward pass through a three-layer network.","下面的代码展示了一个三层网络的前向传播。"],[105.67,112.25,34,"Each hidden layer multiplies by a weight matrix, adds a bias, and applies a sigmoid activation.","每个隐藏层都乘以一个权重矩阵，加上偏置，再经过 sigmoid 激活函数。"],[112.6,120.4,34,"The activation functions introduce non-linearity, which lets MLPs learn complex relationships in data.","激活函数引入了非线性，使 MLP 能够学习数据中复杂的关系。"],[120.75,129.66,34,"Such networks are trained with supervised learning for classification and regression, by learning the weights and biases on each connection.","这类网络通过监督学习来做分类和回归，学习的是每条连接上的权重和偏置。"],[130.01,137.62,34,"And MLPs have been applied in image recognition, natural language processing, and recommendation systems.","MLP 已经被成功应用于图像识别、自然语言处理和推荐系统等领域。"],[138.87,146.25,35,"Now let's build a sentiment classifier from an MLP, using our familiar sentence, This film feels warm.","现在我们用 MLP 来搭建一个情感分类器，用的还是熟悉的句子：This film feels warm。"],[146.6,152.97,35,"The diagram separates three operations: embedding lookup, concatenation, and learned transformations.","这张图把三种操作分开：查嵌入表、拼接，以及可学习的变换。"],[153.32,156.37,35,"First, each token receives an embedding vector.","首先，每个词元得到一个嵌入向量。"],[156.72,164.7,35,"The four colors identify the tokens, and the small cells represent vector components, not scalar token identities.","四种颜色区分不同的词元，小格子表示向量的分量，而不是词元的标量编号。"],[165.05,173.44,35,"Next, we place the embedding of This in the first segment of the long vector x. The matching colors show the exact correspondence.","接着，把 This 的嵌入放进长向量 x 的第一段，颜色一一对应。"],[173.79,180.12,35,"Then we append the embeddings of film, feels and warm, each directly below the previous segment.","然后依次追加 film、feels 和 warm 的嵌入，每个都紧接在上一段的下面。"],[180.47,188.3,35,"Concatenation keeps every component and its order. No averaging, multiplication, or learned projection is involved.","拼接保留了每一个分量及其顺序，其中不涉及任何平均、乘法或可学习的投影。"],[188.65,195.19,35,"If each of the four embeddings had dimension d, the concatenated vector would have dimension four d.","如果四个嵌入的维度都是 d，拼接后的向量维度就是 4d。"],[195.54,200.65,35,"The small diagram uses four components per token only to show the grouping.","图中每个词元只画了四个分量，仅仅是为了展示分组。"],[201.0,209.09,35,"The first hidden layer applies an affine transformation followed by a nonlinearity, and outputs the vector h one.","第一个隐藏层先做仿射变换，再经过非线性函数，输出向量 h1。"],[209.44,214.0,35,"The second hidden layer transforms h one into a new vector, h two.","第二个隐藏层把 h1 变换成一个新的向量 h2。"],[214.35,219.43,35,"Notice that the information passed between layers is a whole vector, not a single number.","注意，层与层之间传递的是一整个向量，而不是一个数。"],[219.78,229.58,35,"Finally, the classification head converts h two into class scores, and then a prediction. Here, the prediction is Positive.","最后，分类头把 h2 转换成类别分数，再给出预测。这里的预测是 Positive。"],[229.93,237.34,35,"This architecture uses a fixed input layout. Sequence models will later handle variable lengths and contextual structure more directly.","这种架构使用固定的输入布局，之后的序列模型会更直接地处理可变长度和上下文结构。"],[237.69,242.75,35,"Next, let's see how the training error changes the parameters along this computation.","接下来，我们看看训练误差如何沿着这条计算路径去改变参数。"],[244.0,248.69,36,"This slide shows one gradient descent update of a small two-class MLP.","这一页展示的是一个小型二分类 MLP 的一次梯度下降更新。"],[249.04,254.34,36,"We use the same input and the same target, Positive, throughout.","自始至终，我们使用同样的输入和同样的目标：Positive。"],[254.69,259.49,36,"Learning changes the model parameters. It does not change the training example.","学习改变的是模型参数，而不是训练样本。"],[259.84,265.94,36,"Step one: forward propagation gives a probability of Positive of about zero point four zero.","第一步：前向传播得到 Positive 的概率约为 0.40。"],[266.29,274.25,36,"Because Positive is the target, the cross-entropy loss is minus the natural log of this probability, about zero point nine three.","因为目标是 Positive，交叉熵损失就是这个概率取自然对数再取负，约为 0.93。"],[274.6,281.13,36,"Step two: backpropagation applies the chain rule from the loss through the output and hidden layers.","第二步：反向传播运用链式法则，从损失出发，经过输出层和隐藏层往回传。"],[281.48,286.65,36,"It computes g, the gradient of the loss with respect to the trainable parameters theta.","它计算出 g，也就是损失对可训练参数 theta 的梯度。"],[287.0,292.73,36,"Each gradient component tells us how a small change to that parameter would change the loss locally.","梯度的每个分量告诉我们：这个参数的微小变化会在局部如何改变损失。"],[293.08,298.62,36,"These colored cells are just a schematic of the gradient vector, not actual values.","这些彩色格子只是梯度向量的示意，并不是实际数值。"],[298.97,304.42,36,"Note that backpropagation computes gradients. It is distinct from the optimizer update.","注意，反向传播负责计算梯度，它和优化器的更新是两回事。"],[304.77,310.34,36,"Step three: gradient descent sets theta to theta minus the learning rate eta times g.","第三步：梯度下降把 theta 更新为 theta 减去学习率 eta 乘以 g。"],[310.69,316.75,36,"All gradients are computed from the original forward pass, and then all parameters are updated together.","所有梯度都基于最初那次前向传播计算，然后所有参数一起更新。"],[317.1,322.83,36,"A small enough step against the gradient should lower this example's loss locally.","沿着梯度的反方向迈出足够小的一步，应该能在局部降低这个样本的损失。"],[323.18,330.23,36,"But a decrease is not guaranteed for an arbitrary learning rate, or for every other example.","但对于任意的学习率，或者对其他每一个样本，损失下降都是没有保证的。"],[330.58,334.89,36,"Step four: we recompute the same example with the updated parameters.","第四步：用更新后的参数重新计算同一个样本。"],[335.24,342.64,36,"Now the probability of Positive is about zero point eight one, and the loss drops to about zero point two one.","现在 Positive 的概率约为 0.81，损失降到了约 0.21。"],[342.99,347.99,36,"The bars use the same scale, so the improvement is easy to see.","两个进度条用的是同一个刻度，所以改进一目了然。"],[348.34,356.17,36,"We have moved the prediction closer to the target. This is one worked optimization step, not evidence about generalization.","我们让预测更接近了目标。这只是一步演算的优化过程，并不能说明泛化能力。"],[357.42,364.18,37,"Training neural networks can fail in different ways, and different failures call for different interventions.","神经网络训练可能以不同的方式失败，而不同的失败需要不同的应对措施。"],[364.53,372.93,37,"First, gradients can shrink or grow through repeated transformations, so earlier layers get tiny or unstable learning signals.","第一，梯度在反复的变换中可能变小或变大，导致前面的层只得到极小或不稳定的学习信号。"],[373.28,380.75,37,"The remedy depends on the mechanism: residual paths, suitable activations, normalization, and gradient clipping.","应对方法取决于具体机制：残差连接、合适的激活函数、归一化以及梯度裁剪。"],[381.1,387.47,37,"Clipping limits exploding gradients, but it does not by itself repair vanishing gradients.","梯度裁剪可以限制梯度爆炸，但它本身并不能解决梯度消失。"],[387.82,395.26,37,"Second, initialization determines the starting scale of signals, so choose it together with the activation and the layer type.","第二，初始化决定了信号的初始尺度，所以要结合激活函数和层的类型来选择。"],[395.61,400.8,37,"Third, optimization dynamics depend strongly on the learning rate and the optimizer.","第三，优化动态很大程度上取决于学习率和优化器。"],[401.15,405.28,37,"Examine training curves and gradient behavior, rather than guessing.","要去检查训练曲线和梯度的表现，而不是靠猜。"],[405.63,413.63,37,"Fourth, overfitting concerns held-out performance. A lower training loss alone does not mean better generalization.","第四，过拟合关乎在留出数据上的表现，仅仅训练损失更低，并不代表泛化更好。"],[413.98,419.17,37,"Validation, regularization, more data and early stopping address this problem.","验证、正则化、更多数据以及提前停止，都可以应对这个问题。"],[419.52,423.53,37,"Fifth, compute and memory place practical limits on training.","第五，算力和内存给训练设定了实际的上限。"],[423.88,429.44,37,"Efficient implementations and suitable architectures increase the experiment budget we can afford.","高效的实现和合适的架构，可以扩大我们能负担的实验规模。"],[429.79,435.35,37,"So architecture, optimization and generalization require separate diagnoses.","所以，架构、优化和泛化需要分别诊断。"],[435.7,445.1,37,"Next, we separate these training issues from representation issues: how a model handles variable-length sequences and shares information across positions.","接下来，我们把这些训练问题和表示问题区分开：模型如何处理变长序列，并在不同位置之间共享信息。"],[445.45,453.95,37,"Sequence architectures help structure that computation, but they do not automatically remove optimization problems or overfitting.","序列架构有助于组织这种计算，但并不会自动消除优化问题或过拟合。"],[455.2,464.75,38,"A concatenation MLP takes an input of fixed width, but language asks for more structure. Here is why we need sequence architectures.","拼接式 MLP 的输入宽度是固定的，但语言需要更多的结构。这就是我们需要序列架构的原因。"],[465.1,470.45,38,"First, sentences have different lengths, from good, to a surprisingly good film.","第一，句子长短不一，可以只是 good，也可以是 a surprisingly good film。"],[470.8,478.43,38,"Reusing a computation over positions allows variable-length processing, within an architecture's implementation limits.","在各个位置上重复使用同一种计算，就能在架构实现允许的范围内处理变长输入。"],[478.78,482.42,38,"Padding, batching and masking still matter, of course.","当然，填充、批处理和掩码依然很重要。"],[482.77,489.7,38,"Second, useful patterns can occur at different positions, like not good, or the ending was not good.","第二，有用的模式可能出现在不同位置，比如 not good，或者 the ending was not good。"],[490.05,498.16,38,"So we share parameters across token positions, rather than assigning unrelated parameters to every absolute slot.","所以我们在不同词元位置之间共享参数，而不是给每个绝对位置分配互不相关的参数。"],[498.51,505.08,38,"This covers shared filters, recurrent transformations, and token-wise transformations in attention architectures.","这包括共享的卷积核、循环变换，以及注意力架构中逐词元的变换。"],[505.43,513.68,38,"Third, some dependencies reach beyond one local window, as in, The film was not, despite its beautiful images, good.","第三，有些依赖关系超出了一个局部窗口，比如：The film was not, despite its beautiful images, good。"],[514.03,517.75,38,"So we must choose how information travels between words.","所以我们必须选择信息在词与词之间如何传递。"],[518.1,529.01,38,"CNNs enlarge their receptive fields through depth or dilation, recurrent models pass state through time, and attention builds content-dependent links.","CNN 通过加深层数或空洞卷积来扩大感受野，循环模型随时间传递状态，而注意力则建立依赖内容的连接。"],[529.36,533.01,38,"Each choice has its own computational and modeling tradeoffs.","每种选择在计算和建模上都有各自的权衡。"],[533.36,543.58,38,"These mechanisms help organize sequence representations, but they do not automatically solve initialization, exploding gradients, overfitting or training cost.","这些机制有助于组织序列表示，但并不会自动解决初始化、梯度爆炸、过拟合或训练开销等问题。"],[543.93,550.6,38,"Next, we connect the MLP to language modeling, and then compare these information-flow rules.","接下来，我们把 MLP 和语言建模联系起来，然后比较这些信息流动的规则。"],[551.85,561.92,39,"This historical example connects the feed-forward network to language modeling: the neural probabilistic language model of Bengio and colleagues, from two thousand three.","这个历史性的例子把前馈网络和语言建模联系了起来：Bengio 等人 2003 年提出的神经概率语言模型。"],[562.27,567.65,39,"Its first idea: word embeddings let similar words share statistical strength.","它的第一个思想是：词嵌入让相似的词可以共享统计信息。"],[568.0,572.78,39,"Words with nearby learned representations can support similar predictions.","学到的表示相近的词，可以支撑相似的预测。"],[573.13,584.54,39,"Its second idea: concatenate the embeddings of a fixed window of previous words, apply an MLP, and normalize the scores into a distribution over the next word.","它的第二个思想是：把固定窗口内前面几个词的嵌入拼接起来，送进 MLP，再把分数归一化成下一个词的概率分布。"],[584.89,589.47,39,"The embeddings and the predictor are trained together, by maximizing likelihood.","词嵌入和预测器通过最大化似然一起训练。"],[589.82,594.79,39,"Unlike a recurrent model, this architecture receives a fixed-length context directly.","和循环模型不同，这种架构直接接收一个固定长度的上下文。"],[595.14,601.34,39,"This motivates us to examine how later architectures represent and combine context.","这促使我们去研究后来的架构如何表示和组合上下文。"],[602.59,608.11,40,"Why do embeddings help? Compare, I am a good, with, I am a great.","为什么嵌入有用？比较一下 I am a good 和 I am a great。"],[608.46,617.52,40,"If good and great have similar embeddings, the network can map these related contexts to related next-word distributions.","如果 good 和 great 的嵌入相近，网络就能把这两个相关的上下文映射到相关的下一个词的分布上。"],[617.87,622.81,40,"It does not have to relearn each context from scratch, as an isolated count table.","它不必像孤立的计数表那样，对每个上下文都从头重新学习。"],[623.16,629.23,40,"Similar vectors do not force identical predictions, but they make statistical sharing possible.","相似的向量并不会强制产生相同的预测，但它们让统计信息的共享成为可能。"],[629.58,637.04,40,"This is the central advantage of learning continuous representations jointly with the language modeling objective.","这就是把连续表示和语言建模目标一起学习的核心优势。"],[638.29,642.63,41,"A connection rule determines how information moves between tokens.","连接规则决定了信息如何在词元之间流动。"],[642.98,651.62,41,"Forward computation and backpropagation are common to MLPs, CNNs and RNNs. What differs is their structural assumptions.","前向计算和反向传播对 MLP、CNN 和 RNN 都是通用的，区别在于它们的结构假设。"],[651.97,656.34,41,"And this is not a claim that an MLP cannot represent sequences.","这也并不是说 MLP 无法表示序列。"],[656.69,664.99,41,"A basic concatenation MLP receives a fixed input layout, with no built-in local filter or recurrent memory.","基本的拼接式 MLP 接收固定的输入布局，没有内置的局部滤波器，也没有循环记忆。"],[665.34,674.25,41,"Token order and context width come from how the input is arranged, and padding or truncation must be specified when lengths vary.","词序和上下文宽度取决于输入如何排列，长度不一时还必须规定如何填充或截断。"],[674.6,683.18,41,"A CNN reuses a local filter across positions, which shares parameters and makes local pattern detection explicit.","CNN 在不同位置重复使用同一个局部滤波器，从而共享参数，并让局部模式的检测变得显式。"],[683.53,687.54,41,"Depth or dilation can enlarge its receptive field.","加深层数或使用空洞卷积可以扩大它的感受野。"],[687.89,695.96,41,"An RNN reuses one state update over time, passing a summary of earlier context on to the next token.","RNN 随时间重复使用同一个状态更新，把前面上下文的摘要传给下一个词元。"],[696.31,698.77,41,"This introduces a sequential dependency.","这就引入了顺序上的依赖。"],[699.12,707.72,41,"Architecture changes the information path and parameter sharing, while initialization, optimization and pre-training still matter.","架构改变的是信息路径和参数共享方式，而初始化、优化和预训练依然重要。"],[708.07,711.69,41,"Next, we open up the convolution operation.","接下来，我们来打开卷积操作看一看。"]]},{"n":4,"title":"Convolutional Networks and ConvS2S","blurb":"Convolution as multiply-then-sum over a sliding window, from 2D images to 1D text, and how ConvS2S generates translations by predicting and appending tokens.","file":"lecture04_part4.mp4","poster":"lecture04_part4.jpg","duration":498.3,"first":42,"last":48,"slides":[{"n":42,"title":"Lecture Roadmap","t":0.8},{"n":43,"title":"Convolution: Multiply, Then Sum","t":23.04},{"n":44,"title":"Convolution: Multiply, Then Sum","t":67.53},{"n":45,"title":"2D and 1D Convolution: Move the Window","t":182.27},{"n":46,"title":"From Classification to Autoregressive Generation","t":246.95},{"n":47,"title":"ConvS2S: Predict, Append, Repeat","t":333.86},{"n":48,"title":"ConvS2S in the Original Paper","t":418.83}],"sents":[[0.8,7.97,42,"Back to the roadmap. We have covered multilayer perceptrons, and now we move to convolutional networks.","回到路线图。我们已经讲完了多层感知机，现在进入卷积网络。"],[8.32,13.39,42,"Keep our guiding question in mind: how does each architecture combine token information?","请记住我们的核心问题：每种架构是如何整合词元信息的？"],[13.74,21.64,42,"After convolution, we will turn to recurrent networks and then the Transformer, before scaling laws and emergence.","讲完卷积之后，我们会依次讲循环网络和 Transformer，最后是规模定律和涌现。"],[22.89,25.34,43,"Let's open up the convolution operation.","我们来打开卷积操作看一看。"],[25.69,32.89,43,"A convolutional layer slides a small window over its input. Here, a three by three window moves over the raw image.","卷积层在输入上滑动一个小窗口。这里，一个三乘三的窗口在原始图像上移动。"],[33.24,41.18,43,"The blue window produces one value in the first convolutional layer, and the green window, shifted along, produces the next.","蓝色窗口在第一个卷积层产生一个值，向右移动后的绿色窗口产生下一个值。"],[41.53,45.58,43,"Then a window over Conv one produces a value in Conv two.","接着，在 Conv1 上的一个窗口又产生了 Conv2 中的一个值。"],[45.93,49.7,43,"At each step, a unit only perceives part of the input.","每一步，一个单元只感知输入的一部分。"],[50.05,59.17,43,"But the unit in Conv two depends, through Conv one, on a larger region of the raw image. Stacking layers grows the receptive field.","但 Conv2 中的单元通过 Conv1，依赖于原始图像中更大的一片区域。层数叠加，感受野就会变大。"],[59.52,66.13,43,"So how is each value actually computed? Multiply, then sum. Let's work through a real example.","那么每个值究竟是怎么算出来的？先相乘，再求和。我们来算一个真实的例子。"],[67.38,78.82,44,"Here, a real photograph is converted to grayscale, resized to sixteen by sixteen, and quantized to integer levels from zero to nine.","这里，一张真实照片被转成灰度图，缩放到十六乘十六，并量化成零到九的整数等级。"],[79.17,83.95,44,"This keeps the arithmetic readable, while still using a real image.","这样既能让计算清晰易读，又仍然使用的是真实图像。"],[84.3,87.23,44,"The yellow square selects one three by three patch.","黄色方框选出了一个三乘三的图像块。"],[87.58,93.57,44,"Its values are two, two, three; one, three, two; and three, two, one.","它的数值是：2、2、3；1、3、2；3、2、1。"],[93.92,101.96,44,"The filter weights are minus one, zero, one; minus two, zero, two; and minus one, zero, one. This is a Sobel-style edge filter.","滤波器权重是：-1、0、1；-2、0、2；-1、0、1。这是一个 Sobel 风格的边缘滤波器。"],[102.31,109.29,44,"Strictly speaking, this is cross-correlation, but that is the operation normally called convolution in CNNs.","严格来说这是互相关运算，但在 CNN 里通常就把它叫作卷积。"],[109.64,116.4,44,"The grid is one grayscale channel. A color CNN would also sum the contributions across channels.","这个网格只是一个灰度通道，彩色图像的 CNN 还要把各个通道的贡献加起来。"],[116.75,127.35,44,"Now multiply matching entries. The products are minus two, zero, three; minus two, zero, four; and minus three, zero, one.","现在把对应位置的数相乘，得到的乘积是：-2、0、3；-2、0、4；-3、0、1。"],[127.7,134.58,44,"These are just products, not another learned filter. Notice that negative weights can subtract evidence.","这些只是乘积，而不是另一个学到的滤波器。注意，负权重可以抵消证据。"],[134.93,143.12,44,"Adding up the rows gives one, two and minus two, so the total response is one. With zero bias, that is our output.","每行相加分别是 1、2 和 -2，所以总响应是 1。偏置为零时，这就是输出。"],[143.47,146.26,44,"A nonzero learned bias would be added here.","如果有非零的可学习偏置，就在这一步加上。"],[146.61,152.51,44,"In a CNN, the filter is learned. This hand-chosen filter is only for teaching the operation.","在 CNN 中，滤波器是学出来的，这个手工选定的滤波器只是为了讲解运算过程。"],[152.86,160.5,44,"Then we apply the identical operation at every valid position. The same filter is reused everywhere.","然后在每一个有效位置上做完全相同的运算，同一个滤波器到处重复使用。"],[160.85,165.06,44,"With stride one and no padding, we get a fourteen by fourteen response map.","步长为一、不做填充，我们就得到一个十四乘十四的响应图。"],[165.41,170.15,44,"Blue indicates positive responses, and red negative responses.","蓝色表示正响应，红色表示负响应。"],[170.5,180.87,44,"Each filter in a filter bank produces a different feature channel. ReLU or pooling may follow, but here we isolate the multiply-and-sum step.","滤波器组中的每个滤波器都会产生一个不同的特征通道。后面可能还有 ReLU 或池化，但这里只单独看相乘再求和这一步。"],[182.12,186.31,45,"Now let's compare two-dimensional and one-dimensional convolution.","现在我们来比较二维卷积和一维卷积。"],[186.66,192.58,45,"Both reuse one filter. Only the axes that represent position are different.","两者都重复使用同一个滤波器，区别只在于表示位置的坐标轴不同。"],[192.93,196.86,45,"An image has two spatial axes, width and height.","图像有两个空间轴：宽和高。"],[197.21,202.08,45,"A text array has one token-position axis, plus a feature-channel axis.","文本数组只有一个词元位置轴，外加一个特征通道轴。"],[202.43,209.25,45,"A text filter spans the full embedding width. The colored cells are schematic features, not measured coordinates.","文本滤波器覆盖整个嵌入宽度。这些彩色格子只是示意的特征，并不是实测的坐标。"],[209.6,220.6,45,"In the image, the window moves to the right, while the text window moves from The, movie, was, to movie, was, really.","在图像中，窗口向右移动；在文本中，窗口从 The、movie、was 移到 movie、was、really。"],[220.95,226.67,45,"Then the image window moves down, while the text window moves to was, really, very.","接着图像窗口向下移动，文本窗口移到 was、really、very。"],[227.02,233.5,45,"Finally, the image window reaches another position, and the text window covers really, very, good.","最后图像窗口到达另一个位置，文本窗口覆盖 really、very、good。"],[233.85,241.14,45,"Only token positions move on the text side. In a typical text convolution, we do not slide across embedding coordinates.","在文本这一侧，移动的只是词元位置。在典型的文本卷积中，我们不会沿着嵌入维度滑动。"],[241.49,245.55,45,"And in both cases, the filter weights are shared across positions.","在这两种情况下，滤波器的权重都是在各个位置之间共享的。"],[246.8,255.99,46,"So far, convolution has been used to classify. Now let's use it to generate: predict one word, append it, then compute the next prediction.","到目前为止，卷积都用于分类。现在我们用它来生成：预测一个词，把它追加进去，然后计算下一个预测。"],[256.34,263.0,46,"The classification row stays as a reference: the CNN reads a complete sentence, pools, and returns one label.","分类这一行作为参照：CNN 读入一个完整的句子，做池化，再输出一个标签。"],[263.35,268.52,46,"The generation row separates predicting a word from appending it to the available prefix.","生成这一行把“预测一个词”和“把它追加到已有前缀中”分成了两步。"],[268.87,275.75,46,"The decoding head is a vocabulary projection and selection step, not a second sequence model.","解码头只是一个在词表上做投影和选择的环节，而不是第二个序列模型。"],[276.1,283.06,46,"First, from the prefix, The movie was, the model predicts good. The prefix has not changed yet.","首先，模型根据前缀 The movie was 预测出 good，此时前缀还没有改变。"],[283.41,289.43,46,"Then we copy good into the prefix along the green feedback route, and clear the output box.","然后我们沿着绿色的反馈路线把 good 复制到前缀中，并清空输出框。"],[289.78,297.71,46,"Next, the causal CNN recomputes with the extended prefix and predicts a period, which is appended in the same way.","接着，因果 CNN 基于延长后的前缀重新计算，预测出一个句号，并同样追加进去。"],[298.06,305.34,46,"Finally, it predicts the end-of-sequence token and stops. Future words never enter the earlier prefix.","最后，它预测出序列结束标记并停止，未来的词永远不会进入之前的前缀。"],[305.69,309.87,46,"These words are a teaching trajectory, not measured model outputs.","这些词只是教学用的示例过程，并不是模型的实测输出。"],[310.22,318.25,46,"Causal convolution reads only the target tokens that are already available, and the same decoding head is reused each time.","因果卷积只读取已经生成的目标词元，并且每次都复用同一个解码头。"],[318.6,327.71,46,"During teacher-forced training, many target positions can be computed in parallel. But that does not make generation non-autoregressive.","在 teacher forcing 训练中，许多目标位置可以并行计算，但这并不意味着生成过程不再是自回归的。"],[328.06,332.46,46,"The following translation example adds conditioning on a source sentence.","接下来的翻译例子会加入对源句的条件依赖。"],[333.71,341.38,47,"Let's return to our translation example: from the Chinese sentence wo xihuan zhebu dianying, to I like this movie.","我们回到翻译的例子：从中文句子“我 喜欢 这部 电影”翻译成 I like this movie。"],[341.73,347.24,47,"This is ConvS2S. The source stays fixed while the target prefix grows.","这就是 ConvS2S：源句保持不变，而目标前缀不断增长。"],[347.59,356.0,47,"The convolutional encoder processes the source once, and the source representations can be attended to at every decoder step.","卷积编码器只处理一次源句，而解码器在每一步都可以对源表示做注意力。"],[356.35,364.02,47,"Given only the start token and the source context, the decoder predicts I. Then we copy I into the target prefix.","只给定起始标记和源上下文，解码器预测出 I，然后把 I 复制到目标前缀中。"],[364.37,372.1,47,"Now, using start and I plus the source context, it recomputes and predicts like, and like is appended.","现在，利用起始标记、I 以及源上下文重新计算，预测出 like，并把 like 追加进去。"],[372.45,379.84,47,"Next, it predicts this from the available prefix, and appends it. Then it predicts movie, and appends that too.","接着，它根据已有前缀预测出 this 并追加，然后预测出 movie，也追加进去。"],[380.19,386.02,47,"Finally, the completed prefix predicts the end token, and translation stops.","最后，完整的前缀预测出结束标记，翻译停止。"],[386.37,393.9,47,"Prediction and appending are separate actions. The network cannot use a word until that word has entered the prefix.","预测和追加是两个独立的动作，一个词在进入前缀之前，网络都无法使用它。"],[394.25,402.78,47,"This diagram abstracts a stack of causal convolutions, with positional embeddings, gated linear units and residual paths.","这张图是一个抽象：它代表一叠因果卷积，带有位置嵌入、门控线性单元和残差连接。"],[403.13,407.44,47,"In the original paper, each decoder layer has its own source attention.","在原论文中，解码器的每一层都有自己的源端注意力。"],[407.79,417.43,47,"The next slide shows the original Figure one, which depicts batched teacher-forced training. Don't mistake it for simultaneous generation.","下一页展示原论文的图 1，它画的是批量化的 teacher forcing 训练，不要把它误认为是同时生成。"],[418.68,424.4,48,"This is the original Figure one from the ConvS2S paper by Gehring and colleagues.","这是 Gehring 等人 ConvS2S 论文中的原始图 1。"],[424.75,433.48,48,"The colored outlines are teaching overlays. The English source is, They agree, and the German target is, Sie stimmen zu.","彩色框是为教学加上的标注。英文源句是 They agree，德文目标句是 Sie stimmen zu。"],[433.83,441.17,48,"Notice the key point: this figure illustrates parallel teacher-forced training, not simultaneous generation.","注意关键点：这张图展示的是并行的 teacher forcing 训练，而不是同时生成。"],[441.52,451.64,48,"First, read the source encoder at the top. Embeddings enter convolutional blocks and gated linear units, and the output provides source context.","首先看顶部的源编码器：嵌入进入卷积模块和门控线性单元，输出提供源上下文。"],[451.99,460.16,48,"Next, the target decoder at the lower left. During teacher-forced training, the shifted gold target tokens are already available.","接着看左下角的目标解码器。在 teacher forcing 训练中，右移后的标准答案目标词元都是现成的。"],[460.51,470.06,48,"So causal convolutions can compute representations for several positions together, and padding ensures that no future target information leaks in.","所以因果卷积可以同时计算多个位置的表示，而填充保证了不会有未来的目标信息泄露进来。"],[470.41,475.24,48,"Third, the attention matrix combines target-context and source representations.","第三，注意力矩阵把目标上下文和源表示结合在一起。"],[475.59,482.25,48,"The weighted source reads join the decoder states, which predict the target words at the lower right.","加权读取的源信息与解码器状态结合，预测出右下角的目标词。"],[482.6,489.11,48,"Parallel training positions do not remove the dependence on previously generated words at inference time.","训练时位置可以并行，但这并没有消除推理时对之前已生成词的依赖。"],[489.46,496.41,48,"Generation still follows the predict-and-append loop from the previous slide. That is why both views are useful.","生成过程仍然遵循上一页的“预测再追加”循环，所以这两种视角都很有用。"]]},{"n":5,"title":"Recurrent Networks: RNN, LSTM and GRU","blurb":"Hidden states carried across time, training RNN language models with teacher forcing, and how LSTM and GRU gates decide what memory to keep, write and expose.","file":"lecture04_part5.mp4","poster":"lecture04_part5.jpg","duration":793.5,"first":49,"last":58,"slides":[{"n":49,"title":"Lecture Roadmap","t":0.8},{"n":50,"title":"hidden states","t":21.15},{"n":51,"title":"A Simple RNN Language Model","t":130.58},{"n":52,"title":"RNN Language Models","t":194.07},{"n":53,"title":"Training an RNN Language Model","t":254.6},{"n":54,"title":"Training an RNN Language Model","t":299.45},{"n":55,"title":"RNN: A New Context Vector at Every Step","t":349.37},{"n":56,"title":"Teacher Forcing and Free-Running Generation","t":449.17},{"n":57,"title":"LSTM: Keep, Write and Expose Memory","t":528.89},{"n":58,"title":"GRU: Reset, Then Blend","t":669.7}],"sents":[[0.8,8.28,49,"Back to the roadmap. We have seen multilayer perceptrons and convolutional networks. Now we move to recurrent networks.","回到路线图。我们已经讲了多层感知机和卷积网络，现在进入循环网络。"],[8.63,13.85,49,"Remember the comparison we are building: how does each architecture combine token information?","记住我们正在做的比较：每种架构是如何整合词元信息的？"],[14.2,19.75,49,"After recurrent networks, we will reach the Transformer, and then scaling laws and emergence.","讲完循环网络，我们就会讲到 Transformer，然后是规模定律和涌现。"],[21.0,29.3,50,"So what is an RNN? A recurrent neural network is designed to handle sequential data and capture temporal dependencies.","那么什么是 RNN？循环神经网络是专门用来处理序列数据、捕捉时间上依赖关系的网络。"],[29.65,38.16,50,"It suits sequences such as time series, natural language, audio and video, and it can process inputs of varying length.","它适合处理时间序列、自然语言、音频和视频等序列数据，并且可以处理不同长度的输入。"],[38.51,42.35,50,"Here is the core idea: apply the same weights W repeatedly.","核心思想是：反复使用同一组权重 W。"],[42.7,51.3,50,"Recurrent layers maintain hidden states. A hidden state captures information from previous time steps and influences future predictions.","循环层维护着隐藏状态，隐藏状态捕捉之前时间步的信息，并影响之后的预测。"],[51.65,57.74,50,"We usually draw an RNN unrolled in time, like this, to visualize its sequential processing.","我们通常像这样把 RNN 按时间展开来画，以便直观地看到它的顺序处理过程。"],[58.09,66.27,50,"At each step, the input x and the previous hidden state produce a new hidden state, and optionally an output y hat.","每一步，输入 x 和前一个隐藏状态共同产生新的隐藏状态，并可选地产生一个输出 y hat。"],[66.62,72.69,50,"Because the hidden states evolve over time, RNNs can learn temporal patterns and dependencies.","由于隐藏状态会随时间演化，RNN 能够学习时间上的模式和依赖。"],[73.04,81.75,50,"But during training, RNNs can suffer from vanishing or exploding gradients, which hurts their ability to capture long-range dependencies.","但在训练中，RNN 可能出现梯度消失或梯度爆炸，从而影响它捕捉长距离依赖的能力。"],[82.1,90.18,50,"Several variants exist: bidirectional RNNs read the sequence in both directions, to capture past and future context.","RNN 有几种变体：双向 RNN 从两个方向读取序列，以捕捉过去和未来的上下文。"],[90.53,97.16,50,"LSTMs introduce gating mechanisms to mitigate vanishing gradients, and GRUs are similar but simpler.","LSTM 引入门控机制来缓解梯度消失，GRU 与之类似但结构更简单。"],[97.51,108.64,50,"RNNs have been used for language modeling, machine translation, sentiment analysis, speech recognition, time series forecasting, video analysis, and even music generation.","RNN 被用于语言建模、机器翻译、情感分析、语音识别、时间序列预测、视频分析，甚至音乐生成。"],[108.99,115.33,50,"Their limitations: they may struggle with very long-term dependencies, and they can be expensive to train.","它们的局限在于：难以捕捉非常长期的依赖，而且训练开销可能很大。"],[115.68,123.15,50,"So some hybrid models combine RNNs with CNNs or Transformers, to capture both local and global dependencies.","因此，一些混合模型把 RNN 与 CNN 或 Transformer 结合起来，同时捕捉局部和全局的依赖。"],[123.5,129.18,50,"In short, RNNs are a fundamental architecture for processing sequential data.","总之，RNN 是处理序列数据的一种基础架构。"],[130.43,136.83,51,"Here is the classic RNN language model, and it is worth reading from the bottom up.","这是经典的 RNN 语言模型，值得我们自下而上地读一遍。"],[137.18,145.23,51,"Each word starts as a one-hot vector x, and the embedding matrix E turns it into a dense vector e.","每个词最开始是一个独热向量 x，嵌入矩阵 E 把它变成一个稠密向量 e。"],[145.58,155.87,51,"The hidden state at step t mixes two things: the previous hidden state through W h, and the current word through W e, followed by a nonlinearity.","第 t 步的隐藏状态混合了两样东西：经过 W_h 的前一个隐藏状态，以及经过 W_e 的当前词，再经过一个非线性函数。"],[156.22,158.05,51,"That is the recurrence.","这就是循环。"],[158.4,165.61,51,"At the top, U and a softmax turn the last hidden state into a distribution over the whole vocabulary.","在顶部，U 和 softmax 把最后一个隐藏状态变成整个词表上的概率分布。"],[165.96,170.12,51,"The horizontal axis of that histogram runs from a to zoo.","这个直方图的横轴从 a 一直排到 zoo。"],[170.47,176.59,51,"After, the students opened their, words like books and laptops get high probability.","在 the students opened their 之后，books 和 laptops 这样的词得到了很高的概率。"],[176.94,180.95,51,"It is the same task as Bengio's model a few slides ago.","这和几页之前 Bengio 的模型是同一个任务。"],[181.3,185.12,51,"But notice the pink note: there is no fixed window anymore.","但请注意粉色的提示：这里不再有固定的窗口了。"],[185.47,192.67,51,"Because the same W h and W e are reused at every step, the input can be as long as you like.","因为每一步都重复使用同样的 W_h 和 W_e，输入想要多长都可以。"],[193.92,196.44,52,"So what did we gain with recurrence?","那么，循环结构给我们带来了什么？"],[196.79,199.58,52,"On the plus side, any input length works.","好处是，任意长度的输入都能处理。"],[199.93,205.11,52,"The prediction at step t can, in theory, use information from many steps back.","第 t 步的预测在理论上可以利用很多步之前的信息。"],[205.46,212.73,52,"And the model does not grow when the context grows, because the same weights are applied at every time step.","而且上下文变长时模型并不会变大，因为每个时间步都使用同样的权重。"],[213.08,218.26,52,"That sharing also means a word is processed the same way wherever it appears.","这种共享还意味着，一个词无论出现在哪里，都会被以同样的方式处理。"],[218.61,222.44,52,"The two minuses are the ones that shape the rest of today.","而两个缺点，将决定我们今天剩下的内容。"],[222.79,234.14,52,"First, recurrent computation is slow. You cannot compute h four until you have finished h three, so the steps cannot run in parallel along the sequence.","第一，循环计算很慢。在算完 h3 之前你没法计算 h4，所以沿着序列的各步无法并行。"],[234.49,244.35,52,"Second, in theory is doing a lot of work in that second advantage. In practice, information from many steps back is hard to use.","第二，前面那条优势里的“理论上”其实分量很重。实际上，很多步之前的信息是很难利用的。"],[244.7,246.37,52,"Hold on to both problems.","请记住这两个问题。"],[246.72,253.2,52,"The vanishing gradient slides will explain the second one, and the Transformer is largely an answer to both.","梯度消失那几页会解释第二个问题，而 Transformer 在很大程度上就是对这两个问题的回答。"],[254.45,259.86,53,"So how do we train this? Take a big corpus and feed it in, word by word.","那么怎么训练它呢？拿一个大语料库，一个词一个词地输入进去。"],[260.21,266.5,53,"At every step, the model outputs a full distribution over the vocabulary for the next word.","在每一步，模型都会输出下一个词在整个词表上的完整分布。"],[266.85,273.71,53,"The loss at that step is simply the negative log probability it gave to the word that actually came next.","这一步的损失就是模型给实际出现的下一个词所分配概率的负对数。"],[274.06,283.96,53,"So at step one, the input is the, the true next word is students, and J one is minus log of the probability assigned to students.","所以在第一步，输入是 the，真实的下一个词是 students，J1 就是分配给 students 的概率取负对数。"],[284.31,291.84,53,"If the model was confident and right, that is close to zero. If it put almost no mass on students, the loss is large.","如果模型很有把握而且猜对了，损失就接近零；如果它几乎没给 students 分配概率，损失就会很大。"],[292.19,298.05,53,"It is the same cross-entropy you met in the classification example, now applied at every position.","这和你在分类例子里见过的交叉熵是一样的，只不过现在用在了每一个位置上。"],[299.3,307.83,54,"We do that at every position and average. The total loss J of theta is the mean of the per-step losses over the sequence.","我们在每个位置都这样做，然后取平均：总损失 J(θ) 就是整个序列上各步损失的平均值。"],[308.18,314.48,54,"In practice, we compute it over a batch of sentences, backpropagate, and take a gradient step.","实际中，我们在一批句子上计算这个损失，做反向传播，然后走一步梯度下降。"],[314.83,317.49,54,"Notice the pink label: teacher forcing.","注意这个粉色标签：teacher forcing。"],[317.84,324.86,54,"The input at each step is always the true word from the corpus, not whatever the model predicted a step earlier.","每一步的输入始终是语料库中真实的词，而不是模型上一步预测出来的词。"],[325.21,330.73,54,"Even if the model guessed something else after the, we still feed students as the next input.","即使模型在 the 之后猜了别的词，我们下一步输入的仍然是 students。"],[331.08,337.13,54,"That gives every position a clean learning signal, and lets training run on gold prefixes.","这样每个位置都能得到干净的学习信号，训练也可以在标准答案的前缀上进行。"],[337.48,343.86,54,"We will come back to what changes when the model has to feed on its own predictions at test time.","当模型在测试时必须以自己的预测作为输入时会发生什么变化，我们之后再回来讨论。"],[344.21,347.97,54,"First, let's put actual numbers into those hidden states.","首先，我们先给这些隐藏状态填上具体的数字。"],[349.22,357.87,55,"Here the state is visible as a vector at every time step: each step combines a token embedding with the previous hidden vector.","这里，每个时间步的状态都以向量的形式呈现出来：每一步都把一个词元嵌入和前一个隐藏向量结合起来。"],[358.22,363.29,55,"The blue triplets are word embeddings, and the purple triplets are hidden states.","蓝色的三元组是词嵌入，紫色的三元组是隐藏状态。"],[363.64,375.62,55,"The weights are invented for teaching: W x is the identity, b is zero, and W h is a small fixed matrix. This is not a trained semantic model.","这些权重是为教学编造的：W_x 是单位矩阵，b 为零，W_h 是一个固定的小矩阵。这不是一个训练好的语义模型。"],[375.97,381.93,55,"The hidden values are computed with this tanh recurrence and rounded to one decimal for display.","隐藏状态的数值按这个 tanh 递推公式计算，并四舍五入到一位小数显示。"],[382.28,394.23,55,"The initial hidden vector h zero is all zeros. Combine it with the embedding of The to obtain h one: zero point two, zero point five, minus zero point one.","初始隐藏向量 h0 全为零。把它和 The 的嵌入结合，得到 h1：0.2、0.5、-0.1。"],[394.58,404.4,55,"The next cell receives the embedding of movie together with h one, so its output, h two, can carry information from both tokens.","下一个单元接收 movie 的嵌入和 h1，所以它的输出 h2 可以同时携带这两个词元的信息。"],[404.75,414.78,55,"Then we add was. The same W h, W x and b operate again, but new inputs create a different hidden vector, h three.","然后加入 was。同样的 W_h、W_x 和 b 再次运算，但新的输入产生了一个不同的隐藏向量 h3。"],[415.13,420.81,55,"Finally we add good. The final h four summarizes the whole prefix consumed so far.","最后加入 good，最终的 h4 概括了到目前为止读入的整个前缀。"],[421.16,427.24,55,"A classification head could read h four, while a next-word head could read every state.","分类头可以读取 h4，而预测下一个词的输出头则可以读取每一个状态。"],[427.59,434.67,55,"The arrow from each purple vector into the next RNN box is the serial dependence that makes an RNN recurrent.","从每个紫色向量指向下一个 RNN 方框的箭头，就是让 RNN 成为“循环”网络的顺序依赖。"],[435.02,447.77,55,"All four boxes depict repeated use of one cell: the same W h, W x and b at every step. The hidden values change, while the parameters stay shared.","这四个方框画的都是同一个单元的重复使用：每一步都是同样的 W_h、W_x 和 b。隐藏值在变化，而参数始终共享。"],[449.02,454.31,56,"Now let's make teacher forcing concrete. The target sentence begins, I like this movie.","现在我们把 teacher forcing 讲具体一些。目标句子以 I like this movie 开头。"],[454.66,459.16,56,"Training appends the gold token, whether the prediction is correct or wrong.","训练时，无论预测对还是错，追加的都是标准答案词元。"],[459.51,467.28,56,"The diagram isolates where the appended token comes from, and leaves out the hidden-state arrows, which continue in every case.","这张图只突出被追加的词元从哪里来，省略了隐藏状态的箭头，而这些箭头在每种情况下都是存在的。"],[467.63,471.31,56,"In the first training case, the model correctly predicts like.","在第一种训练情况下，模型正确地预测出 like。"],[471.66,479.33,56,"We copy like from the gold token column into the next prefix. It happens to match the prediction, but its source is still the training data.","我们从标准答案那一列把 like 复制到下一个前缀中。它恰好和预测一致，但它的来源仍然是训练数据。"],[479.68,485.17,56,"In the second training case, the model wrongly predicts love, while the gold token is like.","在第二种训练情况下，模型错误地预测成 love，而标准答案是 like。"],[485.52,492.5,56,"We still copy the gold like into the next prefix, so the next training step still receives, I like.","我们仍然把标准答案 like 复制到下一个前缀中，所以下一步训练收到的仍然是 I like。"],[492.85,498.88,56,"The loss learns from the wrong prediction, but under teacher forcing that prediction is not fed back.","损失会从这个错误预测中学习，但在 teacher forcing 下，这个预测不会被回传作为输入。"],[499.23,504.15,56,"At test time, the model predicts love, and no gold next token is available.","在测试时，模型预测出 love，而此时没有标准答案可用。"],[504.5,514.99,56,"So the prediction love is copied into the prefix, giving, I love. At inference, the model's own outputs become its next inputs.","所以预测出的 love 被复制到前缀中，得到 I love。推理时，模型自己的输出就成了它下一步的输入。"],[515.34,520.48,56,"The same distinction applies to recurrent, convolutional and Transformer decoders.","同样的区别也适用于循环、卷积以及 Transformer 的自回归解码器。"],[520.83,527.49,56,"The scheduled sampling paper by Bengio and colleagues discusses this mismatch between training and inference.","Bengio 等人关于 scheduled sampling 的论文讨论了训练与推理之间的这种不一致。"],[528.74,537.29,57,"Now, the LSTM. Its vector gates, with values between zero and one, control what memory is kept, written and exposed.","现在来看 LSTM。它的向量门的取值在零到一之间，控制着哪些记忆被保留、写入和输出。"],[537.64,542.14,57,"This is the modern forget-gate LSTM, without peepholes.","这是现代带遗忘门的 LSTM，没有窥视孔连接。"],[542.49,549.67,57,"Start with the two state types: c is the cell memory vector, and h is the exposed hidden vector.","先看两种状态：c 是细胞记忆向量，h 是对外输出的隐藏向量。"],[550.02,552.72,57,"The top horizontal route transports memory.","顶部这条水平路径负责传递记忆。"],[553.07,562.47,57,"Each circled dot is an elementwise multiplication, not a matrix multiplication, and a fork copies a vector rather than dividing it.","每个带圈的点都是逐元素相乘，而不是矩阵乘法；分叉则是复制向量，而不是把它分开。"],[562.82,568.24,57,"The three colored cells are a schematic vector, not a claim that the hidden size is three.","这三个彩色小格只是向量的示意，并不是说隐藏维度就是三。"],[568.59,574.28,57,"First, we form q t by concatenating the previous hidden vector and the current input.","首先，把前一个隐藏向量和当前输入拼接起来，得到 q_t。"],[574.63,578.28,57,"The same q t drives four different learned affine transformations.","同一个 q_t 驱动四个不同的可学习仿射变换。"],[578.63,587.26,57,"The sigmoid outputs, f, i and o, are vectors with one value between zero and one for each memory coordinate.","sigmoid 的输出 f、i 和 o 都是向量，每个记忆坐标对应一个零到一之间的值。"],[587.61,592.21,57,"The candidate g is a tanh vector, with values between minus one and one.","候选值 g 是一个 tanh 向量，取值在负一到一之间。"],[592.56,597.81,57,"Gates are computed from the current inputs. They are not hand-selected binary switches.","门是由当前的输入计算出来的，而不是手工设定的二值开关。"],[598.16,604.5,57,"Now follow the forget route. Multiply f and the old memory, coordinate by coordinate.","现在沿着遗忘路线看：把 f 和旧记忆逐坐标相乘。"],[604.85,611.1,57,"A gate value near one preserves that memory component, and a value near zero suppresses it.","门值接近一，就保留这个记忆分量；接近零，就抑制它。"],[611.45,619.76,57,"Next, the write route. The candidate proposes new content, and the input gate controls how much of each component is written.","接下来是写入路线：候选值提出新内容，输入门控制每个分量写入多少。"],[620.11,625.78,57,"This is a state update in the forward pass, not a change to the network's learned weights.","这是前向传播中的状态更新，而不是对网络学习到的权重的修改。"],[626.13,633.64,57,"Then we add the retained and written vectors: c t equals f times the old c, plus i times g.","然后把保留的向量和写入的向量相加：c_t 等于 f 乘旧的 c，再加上 i 乘 g。"],[633.99,636.94,57,"The new cell memory continues to the next time step.","新的细胞记忆继续传到下一个时间步。"],[637.29,644.81,57,"This additive route can support longer gradient paths, but it does not guarantee that gradients never vanish or explode.","这条相加的路径有助于梯度传得更远，但并不能保证梯度永远不会消失或爆炸。"],[645.16,654.43,57,"Finally, a branch copies c t through tanh, and the output gate filters it: h t equals o times tanh of c t.","最后，一个分支把 c_t 复制出来经过 tanh，再由输出门过滤：h_t 等于 o 乘以 tanh(c_t)。"],[654.78,658.59,57,"Both c and h are carried forward, with different roles.","c 和 h 都会被传到下一步，但扮演不同的角色。"],[658.94,664.98,57,"All the W and b parameters are shared across time, while the gate values depend on the current q t.","所有的 W 和 b 参数在时间上都是共享的，而门的具体数值取决于当前的 q_t。"],[665.33,668.3,57,"Next, the GRU uses just one state.","接下来，GRU 只使用一种状态。"],[669.55,680.2,58,"A GRU carries a single hidden-state vector from one time step to the next. Reset controls the candidate, and update blends old and new.","GRU 在时间步之间只传递一个隐藏状态向量。重置门控制候选值，更新门融合新旧信息。"],[680.55,684.92,58,"Follow the upper route for the old state, and the lower route for the candidate.","上面这条路线走的是旧状态，下面这条路线走的是候选值。"],[685.27,693.39,58,"Every group of three cells is a vector, not a scalar, and the circled operators act component by component.","每组三个小格代表一个向量而不是标量，带圈的运算符都是逐分量运算。"],[693.74,702.68,58,"Both gates use the same context q: the previous hidden state concatenated with the current input. Each gate has its own weights and bias.","两个门使用同一个上下文 q：前一个隐藏状态与当前输入的拼接。每个门都有自己的权重和偏置。"],[703.03,708.26,58,"The reset vector r comes from a sigmoid, so its components lie between zero and one.","重置向量 r 来自 sigmoid，所以它的分量都在零到一之间。"],[708.61,717.52,58,"It multiplies the old state before that state enters the candidate. A small reset value suppresses that part of the old information.","它在旧状态进入候选计算之前与之相乘。重置值较小时，就会抑制旧信息中的相应部分。"],[717.87,726.25,58,"The candidate combines W x times x with W h times the reset-filtered old state, adds a bias, and applies tanh.","候选值把 W_x 乘 x 与 W_h 乘以经过重置过滤的旧状态结合起来，加上偏置，再经过 tanh。"],[726.6,733.09,58,"The order is reset first, then W h, as in the original formulation by Cho and colleagues.","顺序是先重置，再乘 W_h，这与 Cho 等人最初的表述一致。"],[733.44,738.55,58,"The update gate computes z from the same q, but with different parameters.","更新门用同一个 q 计算 z，但参数不同。"],[738.9,745.7,58,"Its two outputs are complementary: z for the old-state route, and one minus z for the candidate route.","它的两个输出是互补的：z 用于旧状态路线，一减 z 用于候选值路线。"],[746.05,752.21,58,"Here z means the amount of old state retained. Some descriptions use the opposite naming convention.","这里 z 表示保留多少旧状态，有些资料用的是相反的命名约定。"],[752.56,761.95,58,"A component of z near one mostly keeps its old value, a component near zero mostly uses the candidate, and values in between blend them.","z 的某个分量接近一，主要保留旧值；接近零，主要使用候选值；介于两者之间则是混合。"],[762.3,768.93,58,"So reset controls what informs the candidate, while update controls what enters the final state.","所以，重置门控制什么信息进入候选值，而更新门控制什么进入最终状态。"],[769.28,774.2,58,"Adding the weighted vectors gives h t, which passes to the next time step.","把加权后的向量相加，得到 h_t，并传给下一个时间步。"],[774.55,777.75,58,"There is no separate cell state as in the LSTM.","这里没有像 LSTM 那样单独的细胞状态。"],[778.1,786.15,58,"The additive retention route helps information and gradients flow, but gating does not guarantee against vanishing or exploding gradients.","相加的保留路径有助于信息和梯度的流动，但门控并不能保证避免梯度消失或爆炸。"],[786.5,791.65,58,"Next, a table summarizes how the LSTM and GRU gates differ.","接下来，用一张表总结 LSTM 和 GRU 的门有什么不同。"]]},{"n":6,"title":"Mamba, RWKV and Gradient Flow Through Time","blurb":"Gates compared, depth and direction, the recurrent revival in Mamba and RWKV, then backpropagation through time, vanishing gradients and why residual connections help.","file":"lecture04_part6.mp4","poster":"lecture04_part6.jpg","duration":830.8,"first":59,"last":72,"slides":[{"n":59,"title":"RNN, LSTM and GRU: What the Gates Control","t":0.8},{"n":60,"title":"RNN Depth and Direction","t":74.59},{"n":61,"title":"Mamba: Selective State Updates","t":156.21},{"n":62,"title":"RWKV: Recurrent Inference","t":221.29},{"n":63,"title":"Backpropagation Through Time (BPTT)","t":284.58},{"n":64,"title":"Problems with RNNs: Vanishing and Exploding Gradients","t":388.07},{"n":65,"title":"Vanishing gradient intuition","t":419.94},{"n":66,"title":"chain rule!","t":441.19},{"n":67,"title":"chain rule!","t":462.12},{"n":68,"title":"chain rule!","t":483.36},{"n":69,"title":"What happens if these are small?","t":508.3},{"n":70,"title":"Is vanishing/exploding gradient just an RNN problem?","t":572.42},{"n":71,"title":"Gradient Flow With and Without Residuals","t":639.61},{"n":72,"title":"CNNs and RNNs: Task Comparisons","t":775.89}],"sents":[[0.8,10.57,59,"Now let's compress the previous diagrams into one mechanism table: each gate has one role in retaining, writing or exposing information.","现在我们把前面的几张图压缩成一张机制对照表：每个门在保留、写入或输出信息中各司其职。"],[10.92,21.24,59,"We keep the same GRU convention throughout: z retains the old state. Some libraries name the complement z instead, but the mechanism is equivalent.","我们始终沿用同一个 GRU 约定：z 表示保留旧状态。有些库把它的补数叫作 z，但机制是等价的。"],[21.59,29.21,59,"The plain RNN has one state, h, and no explicit gates for keeping, writing or exposing.","普通 RNN 只有一个状态 h，没有用于保留、写入或输出的显式门。"],[29.56,34.35,59,"It writes its whole candidate, and that candidate becomes its output state.","它会写入整个候选值，而这个候选值就成为它的输出状态。"],[34.7,40.39,59,"The modern LSTM keeps a cell memory c and an exposed hidden state h.","现代 LSTM 保存一个细胞记忆 c 和一个对外输出的隐藏状态 h。"],[40.74,48.89,59,"Its forget, input and output gates have distinct roles: retain history, write content, and expose output.","它的遗忘门、输入门和输出门分工明确：保留历史、写入内容、输出信息。"],[49.24,51.92,59,"The GRU keeps just one state.","GRU 只保存一个状态。"],[52.27,60.94,59,"Its update gate interpolates between old and new content, and its reset gate shapes the candidate. There is no separate output gate.","它的更新门在新旧内容之间插值，重置门则塑造候选值，它没有单独的输出门。"],[61.29,67.61,59,"All these gates are vectors, so different features can behave differently at the same time step.","所有这些门都是向量，所以在同一个时间步，不同的特征可以有不同的行为。"],[67.96,73.19,59,"This way you can map each gate name to its functional role, instead of memorizing acronyms.","这样，你就能把每个门的名字和它的功能对应起来，而不是死记缩写。"],[74.44,83.99,60,"Keep these architectural choices separate from the cell mechanism we just compared: a recurrent cell can be stacked across layers, or run in both directions.","请把这些架构上的选择与刚才比较的单元机制区分开：循环单元可以跨层堆叠，也可以双向运行。"],[84.34,88.45,60,"Both diagrams use the same four-word sentence: The movie was good.","两张图用的都是同一个四个词的句子：The movie was good。"],[88.8,92.79,60,"On the left, we add a second recurrent layer above the first.","在左边，我们在第一层之上再加一个循环层。"],[93.14,101.42,60,"The lower layer emits a sequence of states, and the upper layer reads those states as its inputs, so it can build more abstract features.","下层输出一串状态，上层把这些状态作为输入来读取，因此能构建更抽象的特征。"],[101.77,107.01,60,"The arrows along each row represent time, while the arrows between rows represent network depth.","每一行中的箭头代表时间，而行与行之间的箭头代表网络深度。"],[107.36,110.92,60,"On the right, we add a backward recurrent sequence.","在右边，我们加入一个反向的循环序列。"],[111.27,118.34,60,"At each position, forward states encode earlier context, and backward states encode later context.","在每个位置上，正向状态编码前文，反向状态编码后文。"],[118.69,126.07,60,"Their states are typically concatenated or otherwise combined, so both directions inform each position.","它们的状态通常会被拼接或以其他方式组合，这样两个方向的信息都能作用于每个位置。"],[126.42,132.97,60,"This supports tasks where the full input is known, such as tagging and classification.","这适用于完整输入已知的任务，比如序列标注和分类。"],[133.32,139.52,60,"But it cannot supply future words to a causal language model at generation time.","但在生成时，它无法为因果语言模型提供未来的词。"],[139.87,147.58,60,"Any of these cells may be a vanilla RNN, an LSTM or a GRU, and depth and direction can be combined.","这些单元可以是普通 RNN、LSTM 或 GRU，而且深度和方向也可以结合使用。"],[147.93,154.81,60,"Variants like peephole connections and coupled input-forget gates change the cell internally, not these global paths.","像窥视孔连接、耦合输入遗忘门这样的变体，改变的是单元内部，而不是这些全局路径。"],[156.06,165.02,61,"Recurrence is back in modern form. Mamba keeps a recurrent state, instead of a growing list of token keys and values.","循环结构以现代的形式回归了。Mamba 保留一个循环状态，而不是一个不断增长的词元键值列表。"],[165.37,173.21,61,"This is the original figure from the paper by Gu and Dao. It shows several feature channels and their expanded states.","这是 Gu 和 Dao 论文中的原图，它展示了若干个特征通道及其扩展后的状态。"],[173.56,178.29,61,"Each token selects how the model writes, retains and reads its memory.","每个词元都会选择模型如何写入、保留和读取它的记忆。"],[178.64,183.62,61,"First, the input computes the selective parameters B, C and delta.","第一，输入计算出选择性参数 B、C 和 delta。"],[183.97,188.83,61,"These decide what to write, how strongly to retain history, and what to read.","它们决定写入什么、在多大程度上保留历史，以及读取什么。"],[189.18,193.56,61,"Second, follow the orange history paths into the updated state.","第二，沿着橙色的历史路径进入更新后的状态。"],[193.91,201.71,61,"At fixed model dimensions, the state capacity does not grow with context length, and processing L tokens takes order L work.","在模型维度固定时，状态容量不会随上下文长度增长，处理 L 个词元只需要 L 量级的计算。"],[202.06,205.08,61,"Third, we read the output features through C.","第三，通过 C 读出输出特征。"],[205.43,211.23,61,"This is a compact learned memory, not a verbatim record of every earlier token.","这是一种紧凑的学习式记忆，而不是对之前每个词元的逐字记录。"],[211.58,219.89,61,"The full Mamba block also includes projections, a local convolution and a gate, and training activation memory need not be constant.","完整的 Mamba 模块还包括投影、局部卷积和门控，而且训练时的激活内存不一定是常数。"],[221.14,227.54,62,"Another modern recurrent model is RWKV. Time mixing carries a compact memory from one token to the next.","另一个现代循环模型是 RWKV。时间混合把一份紧凑的记忆从一个词元传到下一个词元。"],[227.89,238.31,62,"Read the original Figure three from bottom to top, then left to right. The inputs are My, name, is, and the predictions are name, is, Bob.","原论文的图 3 要从下往上、再从左往右读。输入是 My、name、is，预测是 name、is、Bob。"],[238.66,243.43,62,"First, the horizontal state connection carries history between the time-mixing blocks.","第一，水平的状态连接在各个时间混合模块之间传递历史信息。"],[243.78,251.27,62,"Second, in RWKV four, keys weight the values, and a learned per-channel decay discounts older contributions.","第二，在 RWKV-4 中，键对值进行加权，而一个按通道学习的衰减系数会削弱较早的贡献。"],[251.62,255.9,62,"Running numerator and denominator statistics allow a recurrent read.","通过累积分子和分母的统计量，就可以实现循环式的读取。"],[256.25,264.68,62,"Third, a sigmoid receptance gate selects the read that is passed on, and channel mixing then transforms the current features.","第三，一个 sigmoid 接收门选择要传下去的读取结果，然后通道混合再对当前特征做变换。"],[265.03,273.1,62,"At fixed model dimensions, recurrent inference keeps a constant-size state in context length, and does linear work over the sequence.","在模型维度固定时，循环推理的状态大小与上下文长度无关，在整个序列上只需线性计算量。"],[273.45,275.39,62,"Parallel training is also possible.","它也支持并行训练。"],[275.74,283.18,62,"This describes the paper's RWKV four formulation. Later RWKV versions change the recurrence.","这里描述的是论文中的 RWKV-4 版本，后来的 RWKV 版本修改了循环的形式。"],[284.43,289.64,63,"So how do we train recurrent networks? With backpropagation through time, or BPTT.","那么循环网络怎么训练？用随时间反向传播，也就是 BPTT。"],[289.99,294.97,63,"BPTT is ordinary backpropagation applied to an RNN unrolled through time.","BPTT 就是把普通的反向传播用在按时间展开的 RNN 上。"],[295.32,302.96,63,"Here the forward pass uses the same recurrent parameters to build h one, h two, h three and h four.","这里，前向传播用同样的循环参数依次构建 h1、h2、h3 和 h4。"],[303.31,312.76,63,"To keep the chain easy to follow, we put a loss only on the final state. With a loss at every step, each state would also get its own local contribution.","为了让链条清晰，这里只在最后一个状态上计算损失。如果每一步都有损失，每个状态还会得到自己的局部贡献。"],[313.11,320.77,63,"J t is the state-transition Jacobian, the partial derivative of h t with respect to h t minus one.","J_t 是状态转移的雅可比矩阵，也就是 h_t 对 h_(t-1) 的偏导。"],[321.12,330.56,63,"It describes how h t changes when the previous state changes. It maps small perturbations forward, and its transpose maps gradients backward.","它描述了前一个状态变化时 h_t 如何变化：它把微小扰动向前传播，而它的转置把梯度向后传播。"],[330.91,341.45,63,"We start with g four, the gradient of the loss with respect to h four. It is a vector of sensitivities, not a state or a new prediction.","我们从 g4 开始，也就是损失对 h4 的梯度。它是一个灵敏度向量，而不是状态，也不是新的预测。"],[341.8,349.75,63,"One step back: g three equals J four transpose times g four. J four belongs to the transition from h three to h four.","往回走一步：g3 等于 J4 的转置乘以 g4。J4 对应的是从 h3 到 h4 的转移。"],[350.1,356.5,63,"Then g two equals J three transpose times g three, and we keep the multiplication order.","接着，g2 等于 J3 的转置乘以 g3，注意保持乘法的顺序。"],[356.85,362.75,63,"Reaching h one, g one equals J two transpose, J three transpose, J four transpose, times g four.","到达 h1 时，g1 等于 J2 转置、J3 转置、J4 转置依次相乘，再乘以 g4。"],[363.1,373.17,63,"These repeated matrix products can shrink some directions and grow others. For tanh, J t is a diagonal of one minus h t squared, times W.","这些反复的矩阵乘积会让某些方向缩小、另一些方向放大。对于 tanh，J_t 等于以 1 减 h_t 平方为对角的矩阵乘以 W。"],[373.52,380.23,63,"Because the recurrent parameters are shared, they receive a sum of gradient contributions from all their uses.","由于循环参数是共享的，它们会收到来自每一次使用的梯度贡献之和。"],[380.58,386.67,63,"BPTT computes these gradients, and an optimizer then updates the parameters.","BPTT 负责计算这些梯度，随后由优化器更新参数。"],[387.92,395.14,64,"We have just seen that backpropagation through time multiplies a chain of state-transition Jacobians.","我们刚刚看到，随时间反向传播会把一串状态转移的雅可比矩阵连乘起来。"],[395.49,399.62,64,"Now let's see why that is a practical problem, and not just algebra.","现在我们来看看，为什么这是一个实际问题，而不只是代数推导。"],[399.97,407.3,64,"Here is a stripped-down picture: four hidden states connected by the same W, and a loss only at step four.","这是一张简化的图：四个隐藏状态由同一个 W 连接，只在第四步有损失。"],[407.65,412.82,64,"The question is simple: how much does the loss at step four care about h one?","问题很简单：第四步的损失在多大程度上关心 h1？"],[413.17,418.54,64,"If the gradient says almost not at all, the model cannot learn that early words matter.","如果梯度告诉我们“几乎不关心”，模型就学不到前面的词其实很重要。"],[419.79,425.79,65,"Try to write it down yourself first: what is the derivative of J four with respect to h one?","大家先自己试着写一下：J4 对 h1 的导数是什么？"],[426.14,429.35,65,"h one does not touch the loss directly.","h1 并不直接影响损失。"],[429.7,435.52,65,"Its only route to J four goes through h two, then h three, then h four.","它通往 J4 的唯一路径是经过 h2，再经过 h3，最后经过 h4。"],[435.87,439.79,65,"So the gradient has to make the same journey, in reverse.","所以梯度必须沿着同一条路径，反方向走一遍。"],[441.04,450.38,66,"First hop, by the chain rule: the gradient at h one equals how h two changes with h one, times the gradient that has already arrived at h two.","第一跳，根据链式法则：h1 处的梯度，等于 h2 随 h1 的变化率，乘以已经到达 h2 的梯度。"],[450.73,456.26,66,"The blue arrow is the backward signal, flowing from the loss toward the past.","蓝色箭头是反向信号，从损失流向过去。"],[456.61,460.72,66,"Keep an eye on how many factors pile up as we keep going.","注意随着我们继续往回走，乘积中的因子会越积越多。"],[461.97,469.35,67,"Expand once more. The gradient at h two is how h three responds to h two, times the gradient at h three.","再展开一次：h2 处的梯度，等于 h3 对 h2 的响应，乘以 h3 处的梯度。"],[469.7,473.51,67,"Every hop backward adds one more local derivative to the product.","每往回走一跳，乘积中就多一个局部导数。"],[473.86,481.96,67,"Notice that each of these factors depends on the same recurrent weight W, because the transition is shared across time.","注意，每一个因子都依赖同一个循环权重 W，因为状态转移在时间上是共享的。"],[483.21,485.57,68,"And the last hop reaches the loss.","最后一跳到达损失。"],[485.92,494.81,68,"Now the whole expression is visible: the gradient at h one is a product of three local factors, times the gradient at h four.","现在整个表达式都出来了：h1 处的梯度是三个局部因子的乘积，再乘以 h4 处的梯度。"],[495.16,501.88,68,"The factors are d h two by d h one, d h three by d h two, and d h four by d h three.","这三个因子分别是 h2 对 h1、h3 对 h2，以及 h4 对 h3 的导数。"],[502.23,506.9,68,"With a longer sentence, that product would have one factor per time step.","如果句子更长，这个乘积中每个时间步就会多一个因子。"],[508.15,510.75,69,"So what happens if those factors are small?","那么，如果这些因子很小，会发生什么？"],[511.1,520.22,69,"For intuition, treat them as numbers: multiply many values below one, and the product shrinks fast, roughly exponentially with distance.","为了直观理解，把它们当成数字：许多小于一的数相乘，乘积会迅速变小，大致随距离呈指数衰减。"],[520.57,523.95,69,"For matrices, the same story holds for their norms.","对于矩阵，同样的道理适用于它们的范数。"],[524.3,535.77,69,"In an RNN, each factor involves the same W and the derivative of the nonlinearity, which for tanh or sigmoid is at most one, and often much smaller.","在 RNN 中，每个因子都涉及同一个 W 和非线性函数的导数，而 tanh 或 sigmoid 的导数最大为一，通常还小得多。"],[536.12,546.02,69,"By the time the gradient reaches distant steps, it is nearly zero, so the parameters barely learn from long-range dependencies.","等梯度传到较远的时间步时，它几乎为零，所以参数几乎学不到长距离依赖。"],[546.37,548.64,69,"This is the vanishing gradient problem.","这就是梯度消失问题。"],[548.99,556.08,69,"Think back to the Chinese long-context examples: the decisive clue was many words back, exactly where the gradient has faded.","回想一下前面的中文长上下文例子：关键线索在很多个词之前，而那里恰恰是梯度已经消失的地方。"],[556.43,564.73,69,"The mirror image is the exploding gradient: if the factors are large, the product blows up and training becomes unstable.","反过来就是梯度爆炸：如果这些因子很大，乘积就会急剧膨胀，训练变得不稳定。"],[565.08,571.02,69,"Clipping handles that one. Vanishing gradients need a change in the information path itself.","梯度裁剪可以解决梯度爆炸，而梯度消失则需要改变信息路径本身。"],[572.27,575.78,70,"Is this just an RNN problem? No!","这只是 RNN 的问题吗？不是！"],[576.13,583.24,70,"It can affect all neural architectures, including feed-forward and convolutional ones, especially very deep ones.","它可能影响所有的神经网络架构，包括前馈网络和卷积网络，尤其是非常深的网络。"],[583.59,591.46,70,"Any deep network applies the chain rule through layer after layer, so it faces the same issue along depth instead of time.","任何深层网络都要一层层地应用链式法则，所以它们会在深度方向上遇到同样的问题，而不是在时间方向上。"],[591.81,594.32,70,"The lower layers end up learning very slowly.","结果是较低的层学习得非常慢。"],[594.67,600.56,70,"The fix that changed deep learning is to add more direct connections, so the gradient can flow.","改变了深度学习的解决办法，是增加更多的直接连接，让梯度能够流过去。"],[600.91,605.01,70,"For example, residual connections, also known as skip connections.","例如残差连接，也叫跳跃连接。"],[605.36,612.73,70,"A residual block computes F of x plus x. The block only has to learn a correction on top of the identity.","残差块计算的是 F(x) 加 x，这个模块只需要在恒等映射的基础上学习一个修正量。"],[613.08,616.36,70,"The identity path preserves information by default.","恒等路径默认就能保留信息。"],[616.71,623.46,70,"That is the ResNet building block from He and colleagues, and it made very deep networks much easier to train.","这就是 He 等人提出的 ResNet 基本模块，它让非常深的网络变得容易训练得多。"],[623.81,629.02,70,"You have already seen a cousin of this idea in time: the LSTM's additive cell update.","你其实已经在时间维度上见过这个思想的“近亲”：LSTM 的相加式细胞更新。"],[629.37,633.83,70,"Remember this block, because the Transformer wraps one around every sublayer.","请记住这个模块，因为 Transformer 的每个子层外面都包着一个这样的残差连接。"],[634.18,638.21,70,"Let's check with actual numbers what the shortcut does to the gradient.","我们用具体的数字来验证一下，这条捷径对梯度有什么作用。"],[639.46,644.78,71,"This page compares the local backward maps of a plain block and a residual block.","这一页比较普通模块和残差模块在局部的反向传播映射。"],[645.13,656.03,71,"We keep everything else the same: the same transformation F at the same input x, the same local Jacobian, and the same incoming gradient.","其他条件都保持相同：同一个输入 x 上的同一个变换 F、同一个局部雅可比矩阵，以及同一个传入的梯度。"],[656.38,662.66,71,"This is a controlled local comparison. It does not claim that the two complete models have the same output or loss.","这是一个受控的局部比较，并不是说两个完整模型的输出或损失相同。"],[663.01,669.38,71,"Read both networks from top to bottom. The plain block computes y equals F of x.","两个网络都从上往下读。普通模块计算 y 等于 F(x)。"],[669.73,679.21,71,"The residual block computes y equals x plus F of x, and its identity shortcut carries the input around F into the addition node.","残差模块计算 y 等于 x 加 F(x)，它的恒等捷径把输入绕过 F，直接送到加法节点。"],[679.56,684.9,71,"Now send the same incoming gradient, one and minus one, into each output.","现在，向两个输出都送入同样的梯度：1 和 -1。"],[685.25,697.34,71,"Here the local Jacobian of F is fixed at zero point one times the identity, so the transformed contribution is zero point one and minus zero point one on both sides.","这里 F 的局部雅可比固定为 0.1 乘以单位矩阵，所以两边经过变换的贡献都是 0.1 和 -0.1。"],[697.69,700.81,71,"The plain block has only this transformed term.","普通模块只有这一项变换后的梯度。"],[701.16,710.95,71,"At the addition node, the derivative of the sum with respect to each input is the identity, so each branch receives the full incoming gradient.","在加法节点处，和对每个输入的导数都是单位矩阵，所以每个分支都会收到完整的传入梯度。"],[711.3,715.05,71,"It is copied into both branches, not divided between them.","梯度是被复制到两个分支，而不是在两者之间平分。"],[715.4,724.03,71,"Follow the green backward path: the gradient travels from the addition node around F directly to x, unchanged, as one and minus one.","沿着绿色的反向路径看：梯度从加法节点绕过 F，原封不动地直接到达 x，仍然是 1 和 -1。"],[724.38,730.03,71,"Adding the two contributions coordinate by coordinate gives one point one and minus one point one.","把两项贡献逐坐标相加，得到 1.1 和 -1.1。"],[730.38,740.8,71,"So without the shortcut, g x equals J F transpose times g y. With it, g x equals g y plus J F transpose times g y.","所以没有捷径时，g_x 等于 J_F 转置乘 g_y；有捷径时，g_x 等于 g_y 加上 J_F 转置乘 g_y。"],[741.15,746.78,71,"The teaching point is that a correction can reach an earlier layer without passing through F.","要点在于：修正信号可以不经过 F 就到达更早的层。"],[747.13,751.33,71,"A larger gradient here does not mean training is always better or more stable.","这里梯度更大，并不意味着训练总是更好或更稳定。"],[751.68,759.21,71,"For example, a branch Jacobian near minus the identity could cancel the direct term, and other branches could amplify it.","例如，若分支的雅可比接近负的单位矩阵，就可能抵消直接项，而其他分支也可能把它放大。"],[759.56,765.17,71,"Nonlinearities, normalization, initialization and the optimizer all still matter.","非线性、归一化、初始化和优化器依然都很重要。"],[765.52,774.49,71,"And the original ResNet paper applies an activation after the sum. Here we isolate the addition, to make the gradient identity exact.","另外，原始的 ResNet 论文在相加之后还有一个激活函数。这里我们只单独看加法，以便让梯度恒等关系严格成立。"],[775.74,783.34,72,"Here is a comparative study of CNNs and RNNs across several NLP tasks, from Yin and colleagues.","这是 Yin 等人对 CNN 和 RNN 在多个 NLP 任务上的比较研究。"],[783.69,788.28,72,"Read each result together with its task, metric and experimental setting.","读每一个结果时，都要结合它的任务、评价指标和实验设置。"],[788.63,795.38,72,"For example, GRU is best on sentiment classification at eighty-six point three two.","例如，在情感分类上 GRU 最好，达到 86.32。"],[795.73,801.18,72,"A CNN is best on question relation matching, at seventy-one point five zero.","而在问题关系匹配任务 QRM 上，CNN 最好，为 71.50。"],[801.53,807.31,72,"And on POS tagging, the bidirectional LSTM reaches ninety-four point three five.","在词性标注上，双向 LSTM 达到 94.35。"],[807.66,813.2,72,"An advantage on one benchmark does not make one architecture universally superior.","在某一个基准上占优，并不意味着某种架构在所有情况下都更强。"],[813.55,819.9,72,"The useful question is which interaction pattern fits the task and the computational constraints.","真正有用的问题是：哪种交互模式适合当前任务和计算条件。"],[820.25,828.94,72,"Having seen both local and recurrent paths, we can now contrast them with the direct, content-dependent interactions of the Transformer.","看过了局部路径和循环路径之后，我们现在可以把它们与 Transformer 中直接、依赖内容的交互进行对比。"]]},{"n":7,"title":"The Transformer Architecture: Encoder and Decoder","blurb":"A walk through the full Transformer: position embeddings, residuals, feed-forward layers, stacked blocks, masked self-attention in the decoder and cross-attention to the encoder.","file":"lecture04_part7.mp4","poster":"lecture04_part7.jpg","duration":529.2,"first":73,"last":89,"slides":[{"n":73,"title":"Lecture Roadmap","t":0.8},{"n":74,"title":"Transformer Components","t":21.88},{"n":75,"title":"The Transformer Architecture","t":53.94},{"n":79,"title":"encoder","t":131.68},{"n":80,"title":"decoder","t":158.18},{"n":81,"title":"Position embeddings are added to each word embedding. Otherwise, since we have no recurrence, our model is unaware of the position of a word","t":180.43},{"n":82,"title":"Residual connections, which mean that we add the input to a particular block to its output, help improve gradient flow","t":225.98},{"n":83,"title":"A feed-forward layer on top of the attention- weighted averaged value vectors allows us to add more parameters / nonlinearity","t":261.12},{"n":84,"title":"We stack as many of these Transformer blocks on top of each other as we can (bigger models are generally better given enough data!)","t":303.25},{"n":85,"title":"Moving on to the decoder, which takes in English sequences that have been shifted to the right (e.g., <START> schools opened their)","t":335.23},{"n":86,"title":"We first have an instance of masked self attention. Since the decoder is responsible for predicting the English words, w","t":374.66},{"n":87,"title":"Why don’t we do masked self-attention in the encoder?","t":420.7},{"n":88,"title":"Now, we have cross attention, which connects the decoder to the encoder by enabling it to attend over the encoder’s final hidden states.","t":460.35},{"n":89,"title":"After stacking a bunch of these decoder blocks, we finally have our familiar Softmax layer to predict the next English word","t":492.5}],"sents":[[0.8,5.37,73,"And now we reach the final architecture in our section: the Transformer.","现在，我们来到这一部分的最后一种架构：Transformer。"],[5.72,13.58,73,"We have compared multilayer perceptrons, convolutional networks and recurrent networks by how they combine token information.","我们已经从整合词元信息的方式出发，比较了多层感知机、卷积网络和循环网络。"],[13.93,20.48,73,"The Transformer gives the most direct answer, and it will lead us to the last part: scaling laws and emergence.","Transformer 给出了最直接的答案，它也将把我们带到最后一部分：规模定律和涌现。"],[21.73,24.75,74,"The original Transformer has several components.","原始的 Transformer 包含若干个组成部分。"],[25.1,35.43,74,"An encoder and a decoder; self-attention and cross-attention; multiple attention heads; position information; and residual and feed-forward layers.","编码器和解码器；自注意力和交叉注意力；多头注意力；位置信息；以及残差连接和前馈层。"],[35.78,38.97,74,"Do not try to memorize the whole diagram at once.","不要试图一下子记住整张结构图。"],[39.32,45.0,74,"We will follow the source and target information flows, and then isolate the individual components.","我们会沿着源端和目标端的信息流走一遍，然后再逐个拆解各个组件。"],[45.35,52.54,74,"By the end, each box should correspond to a computation, and each connection to a source of information.","到最后，每个方框都应该对应一种计算，每条连接都应该对应一个信息来源。"],[53.79,59.55,75,"Here is the Transformer architecture, with an encoder on the left and a decoder on the right.","这就是 Transformer 的架构，左边是编码器，右边是解码器。"],[59.9,63.5,75,"The original Transformer uses post-normalization blocks.","原始的 Transformer 使用的是后归一化的模块。"],[63.85,68.43,75,"First, encode all the observed source words: The students opened their books.","首先，对所有已知的源端词进行编码：The students opened their books。"],[68.78,77.32,75,"Each gray bypass starts before its sublayer and joins Add and Norm. The output after the last encoder normalization is the source memory.","每条灰色旁路从子层之前出发，汇入 Add + Norm。编码器最后一次归一化之后的输出就是源端记忆。"],[77.67,86.73,75,"Second, the shifted target is fed into masked self-attention, whose causal mask blocks access to later target words.","第二，把右移后的目标序列送入掩码自注意力，它的因果掩码会阻止访问后面的目标词。"],[87.08,90.4,75,"Third, trace the two inputs to cross-attention.","第三，追踪交叉注意力的两路输入。"],[90.75,100.34,75,"The query, Q, comes from the decoder stream below, while the keys and values, K and V, come from the final encoder output on the left.","查询 Q 来自下方的解码器数据流，而键和值 K、V 来自左边编码器的最终输出。"],[100.69,106.75,75,"Each decoder block reads the same final encoder memory, through its own projections.","每个解码器模块都通过自己的投影，读取同一份编码器最终记忆。"],[107.1,113.19,75,"So cross-attention asks with the decoder state, and reads from the encoder output.","所以，交叉注意力用解码器状态来提问，从编码器输出中读取信息。"],[113.54,118.81,75,"Finally, apply the decoder feed-forward layer and the output vocabulary head.","最后，经过解码器的前馈层和输出词表头。"],[119.16,125.01,75,"The N markers mean the blocks are repeated. Only one representative block is drawn.","N 标记表示这些模块会重复堆叠，图中只画出了一个代表性的模块。"],[125.36,130.28,75,"This routing will matter when we distinguish self-attention from cross-attention.","当我们区分自注意力和交叉注意力时，这种连接方式会非常重要。"],[131.53,139.29,79,"Now let's map this onto the original diagram from Attention Is All You Need. First, the encoder, in the green box.","现在把它对应到 Attention Is All You Need 的原图上。首先是绿色框中的编码器。"],[139.64,145.34,79,"The encoder stack takes the input sequence and computes contextualized representations.","编码器堆栈接收输入序列，计算出上下文化的表示。"],[145.69,150.92,79,"Its self-attention layers capture dependencies among the input elements.","其中的自注意力层捕捉输入元素之间的依赖关系。"],[151.27,156.78,79,"These representations are then used as context for generating the output sequence.","这些表示随后被用作生成输出序列的上下文。"],[158.03,161.01,80,"Next, the decoder, in the blue box.","接下来是蓝色框中的解码器。"],[161.36,165.54,80,"The decoder stack generates the output sequence step by step.","解码器堆栈一步一步地生成输出序列。"],[165.89,172.82,80,"It attends to the encoder's representations and to the previously generated tokens, to make context-aware predictions.","它同时关注编码器的表示和之前已生成的词元，从而做出结合上下文的预测。"],[173.17,179.03,80,"Its own self-attention captures dependencies within the output sequence.","它自身的自注意力则捕捉输出序列内部的依赖关系。"],[180.28,185.59,81,"Now let's walk through the Transformer piece by piece, starting at the bottom.","现在我们从底部开始，逐块讲解 Transformer。"],[185.94,189.21,81,"Self-attention on its own has no sense of order.","自注意力本身并没有顺序的概念。"],[189.56,196.18,81,"If you shuffle the words, each token still sees the same set of keys and values, and the outputs just get shuffled too.","如果把词的顺序打乱，每个词元看到的仍是同一组键和值，输出也只是跟着被打乱而已。"],[196.53,205.27,81,"An RNN got order for free from recurrence, and a CNN from its windows. The Transformer has neither.","RNN 通过循环天然获得了顺序信息，CNN 则通过窗口获得。而 Transformer 两者都没有。"],[205.62,211.62,81,"So we add a position embedding to each word embedding, before the first layer.","所以我们在第一层之前，给每个词嵌入加上一个位置嵌入。"],[211.97,218.97,81,"Added, not concatenated: the same vector now carries both what the word is, and where it is.","是相加，而不是拼接：同一个向量现在既携带了这个词是什么，也携带了它在哪里。"],[219.32,224.58,81,"We will look at what these position vectors actually look like a bit later.","这些位置向量具体长什么样，我们稍后再看。"],[225.83,229.57,82,"Next, the arrows that skip around each sublayer.","接下来，看看绕过每个子层的那些箭头。"],[229.92,240.28,82,"These are residual connections: the input to a block is added to its output, and then layer normalization is applied. That is what Add and Norm means.","这些就是残差连接：把模块的输入加到它的输出上，然后再做层归一化，这就是 Add & Norm 的含义。"],[240.63,244.5,82,"It is exactly the ResNet trick we just saw for gradient flow.","这正是我们刚刚看到的、用于改善梯度流动的 ResNet 技巧。"],[244.85,254.89,82,"Each attention or feed-forward sublayer only has to learn a refinement of the representation, and the gradient gets a direct path down through the stack.","每个注意力或前馈子层只需学习对表示的一个改进，而梯度则获得了一条贯穿整个堆栈的直达路径。"],[255.24,259.72,82,"Without these shortcuts, stacking many layers would be much harder to train.","如果没有这些捷径，堆叠很多层将会难训练得多。"],[260.97,262.87,83,"Then comes the feed-forward layer.","接下来是前馈层。"],[263.22,268.69,83,"Remember what attention outputs: for each token, a weighted average of value vectors.","回忆一下注意力输出的是什么：对每个词元，是值向量的加权平均。"],[269.04,275.36,83,"That's great for mixing information across positions, but averaging alone is a fairly weak transformation.","这对于在不同位置之间混合信息很有用，但仅靠平均是一种相当弱的变换。"],[275.71,279.86,83,"The feed-forward network adds nonlinearity and a lot of parameters.","前馈网络加入了非线性，也加入了大量参数。"],[280.21,288.77,83,"In the original model, its hidden layer is four times wider than the model dimension: two thousand forty-eight versus five hundred twelve.","在原始模型中，它的隐藏层宽度是模型维度的四倍：2048 对 512。"],[289.12,293.33,83,"And it's applied to each position separately, with shared weights.","而且它对每个位置分别作用，权重是共享的。"],[293.68,301.85,83,"In our language from earlier: attention does composition across tokens, and the feed-forward layer does abstraction within each token.","用我们前面的说法：注意力负责词元之间的组合，前馈层负责每个词元内部的抽象。"],[303.1,308.78,84,"One encoder block is attention plus feed-forward, each wrapped in Add and Norm.","一个编码器块就是注意力加前馈层，每一部分都包裹在 Add and Norm 之中。"],[309.13,315.39,84,"Then we stack N of them; that's the N-times label, and the original paper used six.","然后我们把 N 个这样的块堆叠起来，这就是 N 乘号标记的含义，原论文用了六层。"],[315.74,322.11,84,"The remark on the slide, bigger models are generally better given enough data, is worth underlining.","幻灯片上的这句话，只要数据足够，更大的模型通常更好，值得特别强调。"],[322.46,325.87,84,"It foreshadows the last part of today: scaling laws.","因为它预示了我们今天的最后一部分：规模定律。"],[326.22,333.83,84,"The architecture is simple and regular enough that you can keep stacking and widening it, and that turns out to matter a lot.","这个架构足够简单、规整，你可以不断地加深、加宽它，而这一点后来被证明非常重要。"],[335.08,337.12,85,"Now over to the decoder side.","现在来看解码器这一侧。"],[337.47,348.39,85,"Its input is the target sentence shifted one position to the right: a start token followed by the target words, like START, schools, opened, their.","它的输入是向右移动一位的目标句子：一个起始符，后面跟着目标词，比如 START、schools、opened、their。"],[348.74,354.61,85,"Shifting means that at each position, the model's job is to predict the word that comes next.","右移的意思是，在每个位置上，模型的任务都是预测下一个词。"],[354.96,361.2,85,"During training this is teacher forcing again: we feed the gold prefix and compute all positions at once.","训练时这又是教师强制：我们输入标准答案的前缀，并一次性计算所有位置。"],[361.55,370.15,85,"A small heads-up: in this sequence of slides the decoder produces English, while our earlier architecture slide translated English into French.","提醒一下：在这一组幻灯片里，解码器生成的是英语，而前面的架构图是把英语翻译成法语。"],[370.5,373.26,85,"The direction doesn't matter for the mechanism.","翻译方向对机制本身没有影响。"],[374.51,378.1,86,"The first sublayer in the decoder is masked self-attention.","解码器的第一个子层是带掩码的自注意力。"],[378.45,384.48,86,"Look at the matrix on the left: rows are query positions, and columns are key positions.","看左边这个矩阵：行是查询位置，列是键位置。"],[384.83,388.04,86,"Yellow means allowed, and purple means blocked.","黄色表示允许，紫色表示屏蔽。"],[388.39,393.81,86,"Each position can attend to itself and everything before it, but nothing after it.","每个位置都可以关注它自己和它之前的所有位置，但不能关注之后的位置。"],[394.16,401.52,86,"In practice, we set the blocked scores to minus infinity before the softmax, so they get exactly zero weight.","实际操作中，我们在 softmax 之前把被屏蔽的分数设为负无穷，这样它们的权重正好为零。"],[401.87,407.1,86,"Why do we need it? Because during training, the whole target sentence goes in at once.","为什么需要掩码？因为训练时，整个目标句子是一次性输入的。"],[407.45,412.75,86,"Without the mask, the position predicting word five could simply look at word five.","如果没有掩码，负责预测第五个词的位置就可以直接看到第五个词。"],[413.1,419.3,86,"The mask keeps parallel training honest: every position sees only what it would have at generation time.","掩码让并行训练保持诚实：每个位置只能看到它在生成时本来就能看到的内容。"],[420.55,425.04,87,"Here's a question for you: why don't we mask self-attention in the encoder?","给大家一个问题：为什么编码器里的自注意力不加掩码？"],[425.39,426.83,87,"Think about it for a moment.","先思考一下。"],[427.18,431.48,87,"The encoder's input is the source sentence, which we're given in full.","编码器的输入是源句子，我们一开始就拿到了完整的句子。"],[431.83,435.29,87,"We're not predicting it, so there's nothing to cheat on.","我们并不需要预测它，所以也就不存在作弊的问题。"],[435.64,441.39,87,"And letting every word see both its left and right context gives better representations.","而且让每个词同时看到左右两边的上下文，可以得到更好的表示。"],[441.74,445.66,87,"That's exactly the bidirectional context BERT exploits.","这正是 BERT 所利用的双向上下文。"],[446.01,452.43,87,"Masking is needed only where we generate, which is why GPT-style decoder-only models use it everywhere.","只有在生成的地方才需要掩码，这就是为什么 GPT 风格的纯解码器模型处处都用它。"],[452.78,458.95,87,"It's the same BERT-versus-GPT mask question we asked on the global-interaction slide.","这和我们在全局交互那页提过的 BERT 与 GPT 的掩码问题是同一个问题。"],[460.2,463.93,88,"Next comes cross-attention, the bridge between the two halves.","接下来是交叉注意力，它是两半之间的桥梁。"],[464.28,471.26,88,"The queries come from the decoder's current states, while the keys and values come from the encoder's final hidden states.","查询来自解码器当前的状态，而键和值来自编码器最后的隐藏状态。"],[471.61,478.59,88,"So at every target position, the decoder asks: which parts of the source sentence matter for the word I'm about to produce?","所以在每个目标位置，解码器都会问：源句子的哪些部分，对我将要生成的这个词最重要？"],[478.94,483.77,88,"It's like a translator glancing back at the original text while writing each word.","这就像译者每写一个词，都会回头看一眼原文。"],[484.12,491.1,88,"Every decoder block has its own cross-attention, but they all read the same final encoder output.","每个解码器块都有自己的交叉注意力，但它们读取的都是同一个编码器最终输出。"],[492.35,497.42,89,"After stacking N of these decoder blocks, we end with something familiar.","堆叠了 N 个解码器块之后，最后是我们熟悉的部分。"],[497.77,505.03,89,"A linear layer projects to the vocabulary size, and a softmax gives a distribution over the next English word.","一个线性层把输出投影到词表大小，再由 softmax 给出下一个英文单词的概率分布。"],[505.38,510.94,89,"At inference time, we pick a word, append it to the prefix and run again.","推理时，我们选出一个词，把它接到前缀后面，然后再运行一次。"],[511.29,517.25,89,"It's the same predict-and-append loop we saw for convolutional translation.","这和我们在卷积翻译模型里看到的预测再追加的循环是一样的。"],[517.6,520.58,89,"That completes the tour of the full architecture.","到这里，我们就走完了整个架构。"],[520.93,527.33,89,"Now let's zoom into the most important box, self-attention, and see exactly what it computes.","现在我们放大最重要的那个模块，自注意力，看看它到底在计算什么。"]]},{"n":8,"title":"Self-attention, Multi-head Attention and Positions","blurb":"Queries, keys and values computed step by step, softmax attention weights, multiple heads, and how sinusoidal, rotary and position-free designs inject word order.","file":"lecture04_part8.mp4","poster":"lecture04_part8.jpg","duration":822.8,"first":90,"last":111,"slides":[{"n":90,"title":"Between-token interaction","t":0.8},{"n":91,"title":"Multi-faced token representation (QKV)","t":42.38},{"n":92,"title":"Key-value interaction between tokens","t":88.47},{"n":93,"title":"Normalize the Key-value interaction as attention (a probability distribution)","t":117.34},{"n":94,"title":"Slide 94","t":169.1},{"n":95,"title":"Self-attention (in encoder)","t":207.31},{"n":96,"title":"Self-attention (in encoder)","t":227.82},{"n":97,"title":"Self-attention (in encoder)","t":247.75},{"n":98,"title":"Self-attention (in encoder)","t":272.51},{"n":99,"title":"Self-attention (in encoder)","t":294.99},{"n":100,"title":"Self-attention (in encoder)","t":319.72},{"n":101,"title":"Self-attention (in encoder)","t":337.87},{"n":102,"title":"Self-attention (in encoder)","t":353.43},{"n":103,"title":"Multi-head self-attention","t":373.44},{"n":104,"title":"Multi-head self-attention","t":412.34},{"n":105,"title":"Multi-head self-attention","t":428.87},{"n":106,"title":"Transformer positional encoding","t":463.22},{"n":107,"title":"Intuitive example","t":517.29},{"n":108,"title":"What does this look like? (each row is the pos. emb. of one of 50 positions)","t":555.69},{"n":109,"title":"Sinusoidal Position Vectors","t":592.96},{"n":110,"title":"Rotary Position Embedding","t":675.98},{"n":111,"title":"Kimi Linear Without Explicit Position Embeddings","t":760.67}],"sents":[[0.8,8.95,90,"This picture from Jay Alammar's Illustrated Transformer shows one encoder block on a two-word input, Thinking Machines.","这张图来自 Jay Alammar 的 Illustrated Transformer，展示了一个编码器块处理两个词的输入：Thinking Machines。"],[9.3,12.11,90,"Read it with the framework from the start of the lecture.","用本讲开头的框架来读这张图。"],[12.46,17.5,90,"Self-attention at the bottom is the between-token interaction.","底部的自注意力就是词元之间的交互。"],[17.85,23.95,90,"It's the only place where x1 and x2 exchange information, producing z1 and z2.","这是 x1 和 x2 唯一交换信息的地方，产生 z1 和 z2。"],[24.3,27.47,90,"The feed-forward network on top is token abstraction.","上面的前馈网络就是词元抽象。"],[27.82,33.79,90,"The exact same network is applied to each position separately, with no mixing across tokens.","完全相同的网络分别作用于每个位置，词元之间没有任何混合。"],[34.14,38.35,90,"Composition, then abstraction, repeated layer after layer.","先组合，再抽象，一层又一层地重复。"],[38.7,40.98,90,"Let's open up the self-attention box.","我们来打开自注意力这个盒子。"],[42.23,53.33,91,"Each token embedding is multiplied by three different learned matrices, W Q, W K and W V, to give a query, a key and a value.","每个词元的嵌入都会乘以三个不同的可学习矩阵 W Q、W K 和 W V，得到一个查询、一个键和一个值。"],[53.68,59.17,91,"I like to call this a multi-faced representation, because the same word plays three roles.","我喜欢把它称为多面的表示，因为同一个词扮演了三种角色。"],[59.52,62.48,91,"The query says what this token is looking for.","查询表示这个词元在寻找什么。"],[62.83,66.43,91,"The key says what it offers when others are searching.","键表示当别的词元来搜索时，它能提供什么。"],[66.78,70.27,91,"The value is the content it actually hands over once selected.","值是它被选中后真正交出去的内容。"],[70.62,76.82,91,"On the left, you can see that for the whole sentence, this is just three matrix multiplications with X.","左边可以看到，对整个句子来说，这只是 X 与三个矩阵的三次矩阵乘法。"],[77.17,87.07,91,"Notice the vectors get smaller: here four dimensions become three, and in the original paper, five hundred twelve becomes sixty-four per head.","注意向量变小了：这里四维变成了三维，而在原论文中，每个头从 512 维变成 64 维。"],[88.32,89.72,92,"Now the interaction.","现在来看交互。"],[90.07,96.28,92,"To update Thinking, we take its query q1 and compute a dot product with every key, including its own.","为了更新 Thinking，我们拿它的查询 q1，与每一个键做点积，包括它自己的键。"],[96.63,101.67,92,"q1 dot k1 is one hundred twelve, and q1 dot k2 is ninety-six.","q1 点乘 k1 等于 112，q1 点乘 k2 等于 96。"],[102.02,108.9,92,"A bigger dot product means a better match between what Thinking is looking for and what that token offers.","点积越大，说明 Thinking 想找的东西和那个词元能提供的东西越匹配。"],[109.25,115.94,92,"That's the key-value interaction: a learned, content-based relevance score for every pair of tokens.","这就是键值交互：为每一对词元计算一个可学习的、基于内容的相关性分数。"],[117.19,120.14,93,"Two more steps turn scores into attention.","还需要两步，才能把分数变成注意力。"],[120.49,127.03,93,"First, we divide by the square root of the key dimension, here eight, since d k is sixty-four.","第一步，除以键维度的平方根，这里是 8，因为 d k 等于 64。"],[127.38,131.79,93,"So one hundred twelve and ninety-six become fourteen and twelve.","于是 112 和 96 变成了 14 和 12。"],[132.14,135.5,93,"Why scale? Dot products grow with dimension.","为什么要缩放？因为点积会随着维度增大而变大。"],[135.85,142.13,93,"Very large scores would push the softmax into a nearly one-hot regime with tiny gradients.","分数太大会把 softmax 推向近乎独热的状态，梯度变得非常小。"],[142.48,146.49,93,"Then the softmax gives zero point eight eight and zero point one two.","然后 softmax 给出 0.88 和 0.12。"],[146.84,151.39,93,"And the question at the bottom: why does softmax give a probability distribution?","再看底部的问题：为什么 softmax 能给出一个概率分布？"],[151.74,158.04,93,"Exponentiating makes every score positive, and dividing by the sum makes them add up to one.","取指数让每个分数都变成正数，再除以总和，让它们加起来等于一。"],[158.39,167.7,93,"It also keeps the ranking and exaggerates the gaps: a difference of just two in the scores became zero point eight eight versus zero point one two.","它还保持了排序，并放大了差距：分数只差 2，结果却变成了 0.88 对 0.12。"],[168.95,173.59,94,"Finally, multiply each value vector by its attention weight and add them up.","最后，把每个值向量乘以它的注意力权重，再加起来。"],[173.94,183.21,94,"z1 is zero point eight eight times v1 plus zero point one two times v2, which is why v2 is drawn faded.","z1 等于 0.88 乘 v1 加上 0.12 乘 v2，所以 v2 被画得很淡。"],[183.56,189.87,94,"The new representation of Thinking is mostly its own content, with a bit of Machines mixed in.","Thinking 的新表示主要是它自己的内容，再混入一点 Machines 的信息。"],[190.22,192.34,94,"Every position does this in parallel.","每个位置都在并行地做这件事。"],[192.69,199.66,94,"So in matrix form, the whole layer is softmax of Q K transpose over root d k, times V.","所以写成矩阵形式，整个层就是 Q 乘 K 转置除以根号 d k，取 softmax，再乘以 V。"],[200.01,203.03,94,"That one line is the heart of the Transformer.","这一行公式就是 Transformer 的核心。"],[203.38,205.91,94,"Let's watch it run on a longer sentence.","我们来看看它在一个更长的句子上如何运行。"],[207.16,213.94,95,"Here's the same computation on a real sentence: Nobel committee awards Strickland who advanced optics.","这是同样的计算，作用在一个真实的句子上：Nobel committee awards Strickland who advanced optics。"],[214.29,222.0,95,"Each token's vector at layer p is projected into three vectors: a query in blue, a key in red and a value in green.","每个词元在第 p 层的向量被投影成三个向量：蓝色的查询、红色的键和绿色的值。"],[222.35,226.42,95,"The same three projection matrices are shared by every position.","这三个投影矩阵被所有位置共享。"],[227.67,233.59,96,"Take one token's query, here the first word's, and compare it with every key in the sentence.","拿一个词元的查询，这里是第一个词的查询，和句子中的每一个键进行比较。"],[233.94,238.63,96,"The red keys now stand upright, one per token, ready for the dot products.","红色的键现在竖了起来，每个词元一个，准备好做点积。"],[238.98,246.35,96,"One query against seven keys gives seven scores, one for each word in the sentence, including the word itself.","一个查询对七个键，得到七个分数，句子中每个词一个，包括这个词自己。"],[247.6,254.69,97,"The scores go through a softmax, giving an attention distribution over all seven words: the purple column.","这些分数经过 softmax，得到在全部七个词上的注意力分布，也就是这个紫色的列。"],[255.04,257.17,97,"Darker circles mean more weight.","颜色越深的圆圈表示权重越大。"],[257.52,262.78,97,"Every token gets its own column, because every token issues its own query.","每个词元都有自己的一列，因为每个词元都会发出自己的查询。"],[263.13,271.11,97,"The shading is illustrative, but you can imagine, for example, who putting a lot of weight on Strickland, the person it refers to.","这里的深浅只是示意，但你可以想象，比如 who 会把很多权重放在 Strickland 上，也就是它所指代的人。"],[272.36,276.06,98,"Here all seven attention distributions are labeled A.","这里，七个注意力分布都被标记为 A。"],[276.41,280.07,98,"They're computed at the same time, not one after another.","它们是同时计算出来的，而不是一个接一个地算。"],[280.42,287.27,98,"And that's a big practical advantage over an RNN: within a layer, there's no sequential dependency between positions.","这是相对 RNN 的一个很大的实际优势：在同一层内，各位置之间没有顺序依赖。"],[287.62,293.59,98,"On a GPU, the whole set is essentially one matrix multiplication followed by a softmax.","在 GPU 上，这一整套计算本质上就是一次矩阵乘法加一次 softmax。"],[294.84,296.5,99,"Now we use the weights.","现在我们来使用这些权重。"],[296.85,303.14,99,"For the first word, each entry in its attention column scales the value vector of the corresponding token.","对于第一个词，它注意力列中的每一项都会缩放对应词元的值向量。"],[303.49,306.29,99,"The lines show those weighted values being gathered.","这些连线表示加权后的值被汇集起来。"],[306.64,313.08,99,"Any word can pull information directly from any other word in a single step, however far apart they are.","任何一个词都可以一步就直接从其他任何词那里获取信息，不管它们相距多远。"],[313.43,318.32,99,"Compare that with the long chain of transitions in the RNN.","对比一下 RNN 中那条长长的状态转移链。"],[319.57,323.66,100,"The weighted values are summed into a single vector for that position.","加权后的值被求和成该位置上的一个向量。"],[324.01,331.01,100,"That's one output: a new representation of the first word that now carries information from the rest of the sentence.","这就是一个输出：第一个词的新表示，现在携带了句子其余部分的信息。"],[331.36,336.47,100,"Its own value is in there too, mixed with whatever the attention weights pulled in.","它自己的值也在其中，和注意力权重拉进来的信息混合在一起。"],[337.72,343.89,101,"Do the same for every position, and you get the new row of vectors labeled M, one per token.","对每个位置都这样做，就得到了新的一行向量，标记为 M，每个词元一个。"],[344.24,352.03,101,"Same length as the input, but each vector is now contextual: it reflects the whole sentence, weighted by relevance.","长度和输入相同，但每个向量现在都是上下文相关的：它按相关性加权，反映了整个句子。"],[353.28,357.23,102,"Compared with the previous build, the attention columns here are softer.","和前一页相比，这里的注意力列更柔和。"],[357.58,365.2,102,"Attention is a distribution, not a hard choice: most words get at least a little weight, and a few get most of it.","注意力是一个分布，而不是硬性选择：大多数词至少会得到一点权重，少数几个词得到大部分权重。"],[365.55,372.04,102,"That softness is what keeps the whole operation differentiable and trainable by gradient descent.","正是这种柔和性，让整个操作可微，可以用梯度下降来训练。"],[373.29,376.97,103,"So far, that's one attention pattern per word.","到目前为止，每个词只有一种注意力模式。"],[377.32,385.83,103,"Multi-head attention runs several of them in parallel, M1 up to MH, each with its own query, key and value projections.","多头注意力并行地运行好几个这样的模式，从 M1 到 MH，每个头都有自己的查询、键和值投影。"],[386.18,390.4,103,"Why bother? A word may need different kinds of information at once.","为什么要这样做？因为一个词可能同时需要不同种类的信息。"],[390.75,397.25,103,"One head might track who did what, another nearby words, another the referent of who.","一个头可能追踪谁做了什么，另一个关注相邻的词，还有一个关注 who 指代的是谁。"],[397.6,403.11,103,"Each head works with smaller vectors, so the total cost is similar to a single big head.","每个头处理的向量更小，所以总成本和一个大的单头差不多。"],[403.46,410.94,103,"Those head roles are just illustrations; what a head actually learns comes from training, not from our design.","这些头的角色只是举例；一个头实际学到什么，来自训练，而不是我们的设计。"],[412.19,418.66,104,"The H head outputs for each token are concatenated and passed through a learned output projection.","每个词元的 H 个头的输出被拼接起来，再经过一个可学习的输出投影。"],[419.01,422.32,104,"That gives one vector per token again: the brown row.","这样每个词元又只剩一个向量：就是这一行棕色的向量。"],[422.67,427.47,104,"That keeps the model width fixed, so the next layer sees vectors of the same size.","这让模型宽度保持不变，下一层看到的向量大小也一样。"],[428.72,433.24,105,"Finally, each position goes through the feed-forward network independently.","最后，每个位置独立地通过前馈网络。"],[433.59,437.96,105,"And the residual connection on the left adds the layer's input back in.","左边的残差连接把这一层的输入加回来。"],[438.31,442.17,105,"The result is the representation at layer p plus one.","结果就是第 p 加 1 层的表示。"],[442.52,449.42,105,"That's one full encoder layer: composition by multi-head attention, abstraction by the feed-forward network.","这就是一个完整的编码器层：多头注意力负责组合，前馈网络负责抽象。"],[449.77,453.65,105,"And residual connections and normalization hold it together.","残差连接和归一化把它们连成一个整体。"],[454.0,457.23,105,"Stack it N times, and you have the encoder.","把它堆叠 N 次，就得到了编码器。"],[457.58,461.82,105,"One piece we promised to revisit is still open: position.","还有一块我们说过要回头再讲的内容：位置。"],[463.07,465.32,106,"Here's the original positional encoding.","这是原始的位置编码。"],[465.67,471.82,106,"For position pos, the even dimensions use a sine, and the odd dimensions use a cosine.","对于位置 pos，偶数维用正弦，奇数维用余弦。"],[472.17,477.55,106,"The frequency depends on the dimension, through ten thousand to the power of two i over d model.","频率通过 10000 的 2i 除以 d model 次方，与维度相关。"],[477.9,485.04,106,"So the first dimension pairs oscillate quickly as you move along the sentence, and the last ones change very slowly.","所以沿着句子移动时，前面几对维度振荡得很快，后面几对变化得非常慢。"],[485.39,492.48,106,"To be precise: pos is the word's position in the sequence, and i indexes the sine-cosine pair.","准确地说：pos 是词在序列中的位置，i 是正弦余弦对的编号。"],[492.83,499.31,106,"So every position gets a five-hundred-twelve-dimensional vector when d model is five hundred twelve.","所以当 d model 等于 512 时，每个位置都会得到一个 512 维的向量。"],[499.66,505.35,106,"Why sinusoids? They're fixed rather than learned, and defined for any position.","为什么用正弦函数？因为它们是固定的而不是学出来的，并且对任何位置都有定义。"],[505.7,515.89,106,"And the authors point out that shifting by a fixed offset is a linear function of the encoding, which may help the model reason about relative positions.","作者还指出，平移一个固定偏移量后的编码，是原编码的线性函数，这可能有助于模型推理相对位置。"],[517.14,520.01,107,"Here's an intuition from Kazemnejad's blog.","这里有一个来自 Kazemnejad 博客的直观例子。"],[520.36,523.85,107,"Write the positions zero to fifteen in binary.","把位置 0 到 15 写成二进制。"],[524.2,533.28,107,"The red, rightmost bit flips at every step, the blue one every two steps, green every four, and orange every eight.","最右边红色的位每一步都翻转，蓝色的每两步翻转一次，绿色每四步，橙色每八步。"],[533.63,538.42,107,"Each position gets a unique code, built from bits that change at different rates.","每个位置都得到一个唯一的编码，由变化速率不同的位组成。"],[538.77,543.2,107,"The sinusoidal encoding is a smooth, continuous version of this.","正弦位置编码就是它的一个平滑、连续的版本。"],[543.55,549.56,107,"Fast-oscillating dimensions play the role of the low bits, and slowly changing ones the role of the high bits.","振荡快的维度扮演低位的角色，变化慢的维度扮演高位的角色。"],[549.91,554.29,107,"And because it's continuous, nearby positions get similar vectors.","而且因为它是连续的，相邻的位置会得到相似的向量。"],[555.54,557.97,108,"And here's what the real thing looks like.","这是真实的位置编码的样子。"],[558.32,565.96,108,"Each row is one position, from zero to fifty, and each column is one of one hundred twenty-eight dimensions.","每一行是一个位置，从 0 到 50，每一列是 128 个维度中的一个。"],[566.31,571.9,108,"On the left, the high-frequency dimensions change from row to row, giving that checkerboard.","左边是高频维度，逐行变化，形成了这种棋盘格图案。"],[572.25,575.35,108,"Moving right, the waves get slower and slower.","往右走，波动变得越来越慢。"],[575.7,584.05,108,"The far-right columns barely change over fifty positions, and look like plain stripes, just like the high bits of the binary counter.","最右边的那些列在 50 个位置内几乎不变，看起来就像普通的条纹，正如二进制计数器的高位。"],[584.4,591.56,108,"To make this concrete, the next slide shrinks the vector to eight dimensions, so you can read every number.","为了更具体，下一页把向量缩小到八维，这样你能读出每一个数字。"],[592.81,597.06,109,"Here the vector has just eight dimensions, so every value is readable.","这里向量只有八维，所以每个数值都能看清。"],[597.41,602.53,109,"The table shows the position vectors for positions zero through seven, all at once.","表格同时展示了位置 0 到 7 的位置向量。"],[602.88,612.68,109,"Even dimensions use sine and odd dimensions use cosine, with rates given by ten thousand to the power of minus twice the pair index divided by the dimension.","偶数维用正弦，奇数维用余弦，速率由 10000 的负的两倍维度对编号除以总维数次方决定。"],[613.03,617.68,109,"The displayed numbers are rounded to one decimal, including values that round to zero.","显示的数字都四舍五入到一位小数，包括那些四舍五入后为零的值。"],[618.03,622.04,109,"On the right, we keep one word fixed throughout: books.","右边，我们始终固定同一个词：books。"],[622.39,628.86,109,"Its word embedding stays the same, and we add the row for one position to it, component by component.","它的词嵌入保持不变，我们把某一个位置对应的那一行逐个分量地加上去。"],[629.21,633.17,109,"Here it's position seven, giving the combined representation at the bottom.","这里是位置 7，相加后得到下方的组合表示。"],[633.52,639.44,109,"Compare the rows: the fast sine-cosine pair on the left changes a lot from position to position.","比较一下各行：左边快速变化的正弦余弦对，在不同位置之间变化很大。"],[639.79,644.97,109,"The low-frequency pairs on the right change only slightly over these eight positions.","右边的低频维度对，在这八个位置之间只变化了一点点。"],[645.32,650.97,109,"That slow change is caused by the low sinusoidal frequency, not by those channels being unimportant.","这种缓慢变化是由于正弦频率低造成的，并不是因为这些通道不重要。"],[651.32,654.71,109,"Word embeddings still carry content in those channels.","词嵌入在这些通道里依然承载着内容信息。"],[655.06,664.08,109,"If the words changed along a real sentence, their content embeddings would also change, and may dominate variation in the slow channels over a short span.","如果在真实句子中词在变化，它们的内容嵌入也会变化，在短距离内，可能主导慢速通道上的变化。"],[664.43,669.17,109,"The output width stays eight: this is additive positional encoding.","输出宽度仍然是八：这就是加法式的位置编码。"],[669.52,674.58,109,"That motivates comparing it with the next idea: rotating the queries and keys instead.","这引出了与下一个思路的比较：改为旋转查询和键。"],[675.83,679.56,110,"Rotary position embedding, or RoPE, takes a different route.","旋转位置编码，也就是 RoPE，走的是另一条路。"],[679.91,683.95,110,"Position rotates query and key feature pairs around the same origin.","位置会让查询和键的特征对绕着同一个原点旋转。"],[684.3,694.12,110,"Here, one feature pair uses an illustrative angular rate of fifteen degrees per position, and the content directions start at ten and forty degrees.","这里，一个特征对使用示意性的角速率：每个位置 15 度，内容方向分别从 10 度和 40 度开始。"],[694.47,697.83,110,"Put q at position two and k at position five.","把 q 放在位置 2，k 放在位置 5。"],[698.18,705.49,110,"They rotate by thirty and seventy-five degrees, so their final directions are forty and one hundred fifteen degrees.","它们分别旋转 30 度和 75 度，所以最终方向是 40 度和 115 度。"],[705.84,709.1,110,"The total angle between them is seventy-five degrees.","它们之间的总夹角是 75 度。"],[709.45,717.3,110,"It contains both the original content angle, thirty degrees, and the relative position contribution, forty-five degrees.","它同时包含原本的内容夹角 30 度，和相对位置贡献的 45 度。"],[717.65,722.68,110,"Now shift both positions by two: q at four and k at seven.","现在把两个位置都平移 2：q 在位置 4，k 在位置 7。"],[723.03,730.2,110,"Both vectors rotate another thirty degrees, preserving the relative angle, the norms and the dot product.","两个向量都再旋转 30 度，相对夹角、模长和点积都保持不变。"],[730.55,741.72,110,"That's the identity here: R m q, transposed, times R n k, equals q transposed times R of n minus m, times k.","这就是这个恒等式：R m 乘 q 的转置，乘以 R n 乘 k，等于 q 的转置乘以 R 的 n 减 m，再乘以 k。"],[742.07,746.97,110,"Same content plus the same offset gives the same dot product.","相同的内容加上相同的偏移，就得到相同的点积。"],[747.32,751.03,110,"The full model uses many feature pairs with different rates.","完整的模型会使用许多具有不同速率的特征对。"],[751.38,759.27,110,"And notice that RoPE rotates Q and K instead of adding a position vector to the input; values need not rotate.","注意，RoPE 旋转的是 Q 和 K，而不是给输入加一个位置向量；值向量不需要旋转。"],[760.52,767.64,111,"Here's a recent architecture that drops explicit position embeddings in its attention layers: Kimi Linear.","这是一个最近的架构，它的注意力层里去掉了显式的位置编码：Kimi Linear。"],[767.99,772.71,111,"Jianlin Su, the author of RoPE, also contributed to this paper.","RoPE 的作者苏剑林也参与了这篇论文。"],[773.06,779.4,111,"The original architecture diagram places three KDA layers between full MLA layers.","原始架构图中，在完整的 MLA 层之间放置了三个 KDA 层。"],[779.75,787.02,111,"First, KDA updates a recurrent state in sequence order, so permuting the inputs generally changes the result.","第一，KDA 按序列顺序更新一个循环状态，所以打乱输入通常会改变结果。"],[787.37,792.8,111,"Second, input-dependent channel decay and state transformations carry recency information.","第二，依赖输入的通道衰减和状态变换携带了时间远近的信息。"],[793.15,800.0,111,"The paper interprets these cumulative transformations as learned, multiplicative positional structure.","论文把这些累积的变换解释为一种学习得到的、乘法形式的位置结构。"],[800.35,811.38,111,"Third, the hybrid uses no position encoding in its full-attention MLA layers, relying on the KDA layers for order information.","第三，这个混合模型在完整注意力的 MLA 层中不使用位置编码，而是依靠 KDA 层提供顺序信息。"],[811.73,816.23,111,"This relocates the position mechanism; it does not make order irrelevant.","这只是把位置机制挪了个地方，并不意味着顺序变得无关紧要。"],[816.58,820.99,111,"And the hybrid still has caches in its full-attention layers.","而且这个混合模型的完整注意力层里依然有缓存。"]]},{"n":9,"title":"Transformer Variants, Applications and Ablations","blurb":"Quadratic cost and sparse attention, Transformers for images, diffusion, robot actions and music, and ablations that test which components really matter.","file":"lecture04_part9.mp4","poster":"lecture04_part9.jpg","duration":974.6,"first":112,"last":133,"slides":[{"n":112,"title":"Transformer Variants","t":0.8},{"n":113,"title":"The Cost of Full Attention","t":19.29},{"n":114,"title":"Quadratic Attention Complexity","t":51.89},{"n":115,"title":"Sequence length / batch size","t":100.28},{"n":116,"title":"Beltagy et al. (2020), Longformer: The Long-Document Transformer","t":138.82},{"n":117,"title":"Attention Cost in the Full Model","t":183.85},{"n":118,"title":"Do Transformer Modifications Transfer?","t":225.71},{"n":119,"title":"Dosovitskiy et al. (2021), An Image Is Worth 16 × 16 Words: Transformers for Image Recognition at Scale Yuan et al. (202","t":264.98},{"n":120,"title":"Peebles et al. (2022), Scalable Diffusion Models with Transformers DiT replaces the U-Net backbone with a Transformer in","t":309.87},{"n":121,"title":"π₀: Continuous Action Generation","t":349.21},{"n":122,"title":"Huang et al. (2019), Music Transformer: Generating Music with Long-Term Structure","t":408.13},{"n":123,"title":"Why Pretraining + Transformers","t":443.6},{"n":124,"title":"Why Pretraining + Transformers","t":527.46},{"n":125,"title":"Understanding Transformer Components","t":606.19},{"n":126,"title":"What changes if we remove or replace: - Self-attention - Feed-forward layers - Position embeddings - Other architectural","t":627.16},{"n":127,"title":"Pure Attention Without Feed-forward Layers","t":659.87},{"n":128,"title":"Token Mixing Without Self-attention","t":711.74},{"n":129,"title":"FNet: Fourier Token Mixing","t":750.43},{"n":130,"title":"Ordering Attention and Feed-forward Layers","t":789.01},{"n":131,"title":"Changing Position Embeddings","t":838.02},{"n":132,"title":"DeepNorm and Deep Transformers","t":889.71},{"n":133,"title":"Wider or Deeper Models?","t":934.8}],"sents":[[0.8,5.57,112,"We have assembled the standard Transformer and its position information.","我们已经搭好了标准的 Transformer 以及它的位置信息。"],[5.92,17.89,112,"Next, we examine the cost of long sequences, alternative attention patterns, applications to other input types, and experiments that test whether individual components are necessary.","接下来，我们将考察长序列的代价、其他注意力模式、对其他类型输入的应用，以及检验各个组件是否必要的实验。"],[19.14,24.01,113,"Full self-attention compares every query position with every key position.","完整的自注意力会把每一个查询位置和每一个键位置进行比较。"],[24.36,28.79,113,"Consequently, its score matrix grows quadratically with sequence length.","因此，它的分数矩阵随序列长度呈平方增长。"],[29.14,36.51,113,"Look at the figure: as the context becomes longer, the orange attention part grows much faster than the blue feed-forward part.","看这张图：随着上下文变长，橙色的注意力部分比蓝色的前馈部分增长得快得多。"],[36.86,44.27,113,"This can create a serious memory and computation cost, although attention need not dominate every model configuration.","这可能带来严重的内存和计算开销，不过注意力并不一定在每种模型配置下都占主导。"],[44.62,50.49,113,"The next slide makes the all-pairs relationship explicit before we discuss possible reductions.","下一页先把这种两两比较的关系讲清楚，然后再讨论可能的削减方法。"],[51.74,57.07,114,"A sequence of length n produces n by n query-key scores.","一个长度为 n 的序列，会产生 n 乘 n 个查询键分数。"],[57.42,64.27,114,"With feature dimension d, the core dense attention computation is roughly big O of n squared d.","特征维度为 d 时，核心的稠密注意力计算量大约是 n 平方乘 d 的量级。"],[64.62,70.75,114,"Doubling the sequence length therefore has a different effect from merely doubling a linear token-processing cost.","所以，序列长度翻倍，与线性的逐词处理成本翻倍，效果是不一样的。"],[71.1,78.39,114,"With d around one thousand, a short sentence of up to thirty tokens has at most nine hundred token pairs.","取 d 约为一千，一个最多 30 个词元的短句子，最多只有 900 个词元对。"],[78.74,87.76,114,"A context limit such as five hundred twelve keeps the matrix manageable, but a long document with fifty thousand tokens or more needs far more pairwise work.","像 512 这样的上下文限制可以让矩阵保持可控，但五万个词元以上的长文档需要多得多的两两计算。"],[88.11,94.62,114,"For short inputs, other model components may dominate; long contexts make this term much more consequential.","对于短输入，其他模型组件可能占主导；长上下文会让这一项变得重要得多。"],[94.97,98.88,114,"We will compare compression and sparsity as two ways to reduce it.","我们会比较压缩和稀疏这两种降低它的方法。"],[100.13,103.08,115,"Can we reduce the all-pairs attention cost?","我们能降低这种两两注意力的代价吗？"],[103.43,109.0,115,"Linformer compresses keys and values along the sequence dimension before attention.","Linformer 在做注意力之前，沿着序列维度压缩键和值。"],[109.35,116.31,115,"The query can then interact with a smaller representation, instead of an unrestricted set of original positions.","这样，查询只需要与一个更小的表示交互，而不是与所有原始位置交互。"],[116.66,125.57,115,"On the right, the standard Transformer's inference time climbs steeply as sequences get longer, while the Linformer curves stay much flatter.","右边，随着序列变长，标准 Transformer 的推理时间急剧上升，而 Linformer 的曲线则平缓得多。"],[125.92,129.27,115,"These curves should be read under their reported settings.","这些曲线应该结合它们报告的实验设置来解读。"],[129.62,137.42,115,"And reduced computation is valuable only when the resulting approximation preserves enough task quality.","而且，只有当这种近似保留了足够的任务质量时，减少计算才有价值。"],[138.67,146.66,116,"Longformer and Big Bird take a different route: they reduce the number of directly connected token pairs through sparse attention patterns.","Longformer 和 Big Bird 走的是另一条路：它们用稀疏注意力模式，减少直接相连的词元对的数量。"],[147.01,151.45,116,"Compare full n-squared attention with these sparse patterns.","对比一下完整的 n 平方注意力和这些稀疏模式。"],[151.8,157.34,116,"Local windows capture nearby information, and global positions create longer routes.","局部窗口捕捉邻近的信息，全局位置则建立更长的通路。"],[157.69,163.34,116,"Big Bird also includes random connections, combining random, window and global attention.","Big Bird 还加入了随机连接，把随机注意力、窗口注意力和全局注意力结合起来。"],[163.69,170.86,116,"These patterns change the connectivity graph, whereas Linformer changes the representation used in the attention calculation.","这些模式改变的是连接图，而 Linformer 改变的是注意力计算中所用的表示。"],[171.21,176.81,116,"Follow a distant dependency through the sparse links, and you'll see why path structure still matters.","沿着稀疏连接追踪一个远距离依赖，你就会明白为什么路径结构依然重要。"],[177.16,182.45,116,"Next, we place these attention savings within the cost of a complete model.","接下来，我们把这些注意力上的节省放到整个模型的成本中来看。"],[183.7,189.35,117,"The total runtime depends on model width, sequence length, implementation and hardware.","总运行时间取决于模型宽度、序列长度、实现方式和硬件。"],[189.7,195.87,117,"A quadratic attention term does not necessarily dominate a short-sequence or very wide model.","对于短序列或非常宽的模型，平方级的注意力项不一定占主导。"],[196.22,202.46,117,"Likewise, fewer theoretical operations may not translate directly into faster execution.","同样，理论运算量更少，也不一定能直接转化为更快的执行速度。"],[202.81,209.51,117,"So evaluate an attention modification using end-to-end cost and task quality together.","所以，评估一种注意力改进时，要同时看端到端的成本和任务质量。"],[209.86,214.73,117,"Still, long contexts make efficient alternatives increasingly relevant.","不过，长上下文确实让高效的替代方案越来越重要。"],[215.08,224.31,117,"This prepares us to read comparative studies of Transformer modifications, without assuming that every promising local change will generalize.","这为我们阅读 Transformer 改进的对比研究做好准备，不要假设每个看起来有希望的局部改动都能推广。"],[225.56,231.31,118,"This study tested a large number of Transformer modifications under shared implementations.","这项研究在统一的实现下，测试了大量的 Transformer 改进方案。"],[231.66,240.38,118,"It found that many modifications did not consistently improve performance across its evaluated settings.","它发现，在所评估的设置中，许多改进并没有带来一致的性能提升。"],[240.73,249.0,118,"That conclusion is about transfer across particular implementations and tasks, not a proof that architectural innovation cannot help.","这个结论讨论的是在特定实现和任务之间能否迁移，并不能证明架构创新没有用。"],[249.35,254.39,118,"When reading the table, look for controlled comparisons and reproducible gains.","阅读这张表时，要关注受控的对比和可复现的提升。"],[254.74,263.58,118,"We will now temporarily leave the efficiency question and see how the Transformer computation can be reused with different kinds of input sequences.","现在我们暂时离开效率问题，看看 Transformer 的计算如何复用到不同类型的输入序列上。"],[264.83,271.36,119,"A Vision Transformer divides an image into patches and projects each patch into a token representation.","视觉 Transformer 把一张图像切成小块，再把每个小块投影成一个词元表示。"],[271.71,275.51,119,"Position information preserves where those patches came from.","位置信息保留了这些图像块来自哪里。"],[275.86,281.33,119,"The encoder then processes the sequence using the familiar attention and feed-forward blocks.","然后编码器用我们熟悉的注意力和前馈模块来处理这个序列。"],[281.68,285.46,119,"The key adaptation is the interface from image to tokens.","关键的改动在于从图像到词元的这个接口。"],[285.81,292.01,119,"So ask yourself: which parts differ from text, and which remain structurally similar?","所以请思考：哪些部分与文本不同，哪些在结构上仍然相似？"],[292.36,302.26,119,"The plot on the right compares ViT, Tokens-to-Token ViT and ResNet in accuracy against computation and model size.","右边的图比较了 ViT、Tokens-to-Token ViT 和 ResNet 在准确率与计算量、模型大小之间的关系。"],[302.61,308.47,119,"This leads to another use of Transformers, within a different training objective: diffusion.","这引出了 Transformer 在另一种训练目标下的应用：扩散模型。"],[309.72,317.05,120,"DiT places a Transformer backbone inside a diffusion model, replacing the U-Net backbone in the design shown here.","DiT 把 Transformer 作为扩散模型的主干网络，替换了这里所示设计中的 U-Net 主干。"],[317.4,326.81,120,"The network processes image or latent patches together with conditioning information, such as the timestep and label, to support denoising.","网络把图像或潜变量的小块与条件信息一起处理，比如时间步和标签，以支持去噪。"],[327.16,333.63,120,"Inside each block, you can still recognize multi-head self-attention and a pointwise feed-forward layer.","在每个模块里，你仍然能认出多头自注意力和逐点前馈层。"],[333.98,342.45,120,"The purpose of this example is architectural transfer: an attention-based block can be trained for an objective other than next-word prediction.","这个例子的目的在于架构迁移：基于注意力的模块可以用于训练下一个词预测之外的目标。"],[342.8,347.81,120,"We will make a similar connection for robot actions and musical sequences next.","接下来，我们会对机器人动作和音乐序列建立类似的联系。"],[349.06,351.99,121,"Transformers can even generate robot actions.","Transformer 甚至可以生成机器人动作。"],[352.34,355.71,121,"The left diagram is the original pi-zero architecture.","左边是原始的 pi-zero 架构图。"],[356.06,364.17,121,"Images and an instruction, such as fold shirt, provide context through the pre-trained vision-language model.","图像和一条指令，比如“叠衬衫”，通过预训练的视觉语言模型提供上下文。"],[364.52,369.26,121,"The robot state and a noisy action chunk enter the action expert.","机器人状态和一段带噪声的动作块进入动作专家模块。"],[369.61,373.56,121,"Each future action is a vector of continuous control values.","每一个未来动作都是一个由连续控制量组成的向量。"],[373.91,381.59,121,"The expert predicts a velocity field, and repeated flow-matching integration refines the whole chunk jointly.","动作专家预测一个速度场，通过反复的流匹配积分，对整个动作块进行联合细化。"],[381.94,387.21,121,"The small plot shows only one action coordinate at eight illustrative times.","右边的小图只展示了一个动作坐标在八个示意时刻上的取值。"],[387.56,393.08,121,"It is a teaching schematic, not measured robot data or the actual learned velocity field.","它只是教学示意图，不是实测的机器人数据，也不是真正学到的速度场。"],[393.43,401.58,121,"Distinguish the two axes of time: the paper uses fifty future control actions per chunk, and ten numerical flow-integration steps.","要区分两种时间轴：论文中每个动作块有 50 个未来控制动作，并使用 10 步数值流积分。"],[401.93,406.73,121,"Flow matching is the specific continuous generative method used by pi-zero.","流匹配是 pi-zero 所采用的具体的连续生成方法。"],[407.98,415.72,122,"Music contains both local transitions and long-range structure, such as recurring motifs and dependencies across measures.","音乐既包含局部的过渡，也包含长程结构，比如反复出现的动机，以及跨小节的依赖关系。"],[416.07,421.36,122,"Music Transformer uses attention to model relationships among musical events.","Music Transformer 用注意力来建模音乐事件之间的关系。"],[421.71,428.18,122,"Follow the long-distance links in the figure, and relate them to a repeated or structurally connected passage.","沿着图中的长距离连线看，把它们与重复出现或结构上相关联的乐段对应起来。"],[428.53,434.87,122,"The analogy with language is about sequence relationships, not identical data semantics.","与语言的类比，是关于序列关系的类比，而不是说两者数据语义相同。"],[435.22,442.2,122,"Having seen several application areas, we return to the question of why Transformers became so widely useful.","看过几个应用领域之后，我们回到这个问题：为什么 Transformer 变得如此广泛有用？"],[443.45,446.54,123,"So why did pretraining plus Transformers take over?","那么，为什么预训练加 Transformer 能够一统天下？"],[446.89,452.26,123,"Here are four proposed explanations, each with a pushback from the original discussion.","这里有四种可能的解释，每一种在最初的讨论中都受到了反驳。"],[452.61,455.91,123,"First, because Transformers are more efficient?","第一，因为 Transformer 更高效？"],[456.26,463.14,123,"The original lecture challenges this: it says Transformers are slower than LSTMs with the same number of parameters.","最初的讲义对此提出质疑：它说在参数量相同的情况下，Transformer 比 LSTM 更慢。"],[463.49,468.12,123,"That is a comparison in a particular setting, not a universal speed ordering.","这是在特定设置下的比较，并不是普遍的速度排序。"],[468.47,475.6,123,"Throughput and latency depend on sequence length, batching, hardware, parallelism and implementation.","吞吐量和延迟取决于序列长度、批处理、硬件、并行方式和实现。"],[475.95,479.91,123,"Second, because Transformers are better at machine translation?","第二，因为 Transformer 更擅长机器翻译？"],[480.26,489.78,123,"Strong recurrent and convolutional translation systems also existed, so the claim of equal quality here is rhetorical and setting-dependent.","强大的循环网络和卷积网络翻译系统也存在，所以这里说效果一样好，是一种修辞，取决于具体设置。"],[490.13,494.15,123,"Third, because Transformers use nothing but attention? So what?","第三，因为 Transformer 只用了注意力？那又怎样？"],[494.5,503.98,123,"Saying that a model uses attention does not by itself explain why it is trainable, or why performance improves with scale.","说一个模型用了注意力，本身并不能解释它为什么可训练，也不能解释为什么性能随规模提升。"],[504.33,506.45,123,"We need to look for a mechanism.","我们需要去寻找背后的机制。"],[506.8,511.27,123,"Fourth, because Transformers learn contextualized word embeddings?","第四，因为 Transformer 学到了上下文相关的词嵌入？"],[511.62,516.62,123,"But RNNs can learn them too: ELMo uses a deep bidirectional language model.","但 RNN 也能学到：ELMo 用的就是一个深层双向语言模型。"],[516.97,522.99,123,"These points come from the original lecture discussion, credited to Zhilin Yang of Recurrent AI.","这些观点来自最初的课程讨论，出自循环智能的杨植麟。"],[523.34,526.06,123,"The next slide gives the actual argument.","下一页给出真正的论点。"],[527.31,532.5,124,"Here's the answer the original lecture gives, and it's a combination rather than one trick.","这是最初讲义给出的答案，它是多个因素的组合，而不是某一个技巧。"],[532.85,539.29,124,"Capacity: attention plus wide feed-forward layers can express very rich functions.","容量：注意力加上宽的前馈层，可以表达非常丰富的函数。"],[539.64,548.18,124,"Optimization: with residual connections, normalization and parallel training, we can actually find good solutions in that huge space.","优化：借助残差连接、归一化和并行训练，我们真的能在这个巨大的空间里找到好的解。"],[548.53,551.6,124,"And any two tokens are only one step apart.","而且任意两个词元之间只隔一步。"],[551.95,555.33,124,"Generalization: those solutions hold up on test data.","泛化：这些解在测试数据上依然成立。"],[555.68,559.64,124,"And then scalability, which is the punchline.","然后是可扩展性，这才是重点。"],[559.99,572.47,124,"Look at the box. For two very large LSTMs, going from one point eight to three point three billion parameters made perplexity slightly worse: thirty point six to thirty-two point two.","看这个框。两个非常大的 LSTM，参数从 18 亿增加到 33 亿，困惑度反而略微变差：从 30.6 到 32.2。"],[572.82,578.82,124,"Transformer-XL with only zero point four six billion parameters reaches twenty-three point five.","而只有 4.6 亿参数的 Transformer-XL 就达到了 23.5。"],[579.17,584.35,124,"Growing it to zero point eight billion improves that to twenty-one point eight; and lower is better.","把它增大到 8 亿参数，困惑度改进到 21.8；困惑度越低越好。"],[584.7,589.76,124,"These numbers come from different papers and setups, so don't over-read the exact gap.","这些数字来自不同的论文和设置，所以不要过度解读具体的差距。"],[590.11,595.95,124,"But the trend is the point: Transformers keep paying off as you add parameters.","但趋势才是重点：随着参数增加，Transformer 能持续带来回报。"],[596.3,599.63,124,"That's why pretraining plus Transformers took over.","这就是为什么预训练加 Transformer 能一统天下。"],[599.98,604.79,124,"Knowing that it works, though, isn't the same as knowing which parts matter.","不过，知道它有效，并不等于知道哪些部分才是关键。"],[606.04,611.44,125,"A successful architecture does not automatically reveal which ingredients are essential.","一个成功的架构，并不会自动告诉我们哪些成分才是关键。"],[611.79,620.46,125,"In this section, we use component ablations to test the roles of attention, feed-forward transformations and positional information.","在这一部分，我们用组件消融实验来检验注意力、前馈变换和位置信息各自的作用。"],[620.81,625.76,125,"These experiments connect the design back to our composition-and-abstraction framework.","这些实验把架构设计和我们的组合与抽象框架重新联系起来。"],[627.01,634.75,126,"Consider three interventions: remove or replace self-attention, remove feed-forward layers, and change position information.","考虑三种干预：去掉或替换自注意力，去掉前馈层，以及改变位置信息。"],[635.1,641.88,126,"Each tests a different hypothesis: about token interaction, feature transformation, or sequence order.","每一种都在检验一个不同的假设：关于词元交互、特征变换，或者序列顺序。"],[642.23,649.09,126,"A useful ablation keeps other factors as comparable as possible, and evaluates the tasks relevant to the claim.","一个有用的消融实验，要尽量让其他因素保持可比，并在与结论相关的任务上进行评估。"],[649.44,653.61,126,"The following papers provide examples of these experiments.","接下来的几篇论文提供了这类实验的例子。"],[653.96,658.47,126,"We begin with what can go wrong in a network built from pure attention.","我们先来看，一个只由纯注意力构成的网络会出什么问题。"],[659.72,664.4,127,"What happens if we keep only attention, with no feed-forward layers?","如果只保留注意力、去掉前馈层，会发生什么？"],[664.75,672.13,127,"The figure decomposes such a network into paths through individual attention heads, across layers one to L.","这张图把这样的网络分解成穿过各个注意力头、从第 1 层到第 L 层的路径。"],[672.48,682.48,127,"The cited analysis shows that pure attention loses rank rapidly with depth: doubly exponentially, under particular architectural assumptions.","所引用的分析表明，在特定的架构假设下，纯注意力的表示秩会随深度迅速退化：呈双指数速度。"],[682.83,690.16,127,"This is a reason to study feed-forward layers, residual paths and other components separately.","这就是为什么要分别研究前馈层、残差通路和其他组件。"],[690.51,695.68,127,"We shouldn't attribute every benefit of a standard Transformer to attention alone.","我们不应该把标准 Transformer 的所有好处都归功于注意力。"],[696.03,702.78,127,"But be careful about the scope: the result does not say that every practical Transformer collapses in this way.","但要注意适用范围：这个结果并不是说每个实际的 Transformer 都会这样崩塌。"],[703.13,710.34,127,"Next, we examine an architecture that keeps token mixing, while replacing attention with MLPs.","接下来，我们看一个保留了词元混合、但用 MLP 替代注意力的架构。"],[711.59,714.74,128,"MLP-Mixer alternates two kinds of operations.","MLP-Mixer 交替使用两种操作。"],[715.09,722.5,128,"One mixes information across tokens, the patches, and the other mixes channels within each token representation.","一种在词元，也就是图像块之间混合信息，另一种在每个词元表示的内部混合通道。"],[722.85,730.39,128,"It therefore preserves our conceptual separation of composition and abstraction, while changing the implementation.","因此，它保留了我们关于组合与抽象的概念区分，只是换了实现方式。"],[730.74,735.36,128,"The work shown here concerns vision; at least it works for computer vision.","这里展示的工作针对的是视觉；至少在计算机视觉上它是有效的。"],[735.71,741.11,128,"Its success there should not be assumed to transfer unchanged to every language task.","不能假设它在视觉上的成功，可以原封不动地迁移到每一个语言任务上。"],[741.46,749.03,128,"The broader lesson is that useful token interaction need not always be implemented through content-dependent attention.","更广泛的启示是：有用的词元交互，不一定总要通过依赖内容的注意力来实现。"],[750.28,756.22,129,"FNet uses a Fourier transform as a fixed linear mechanism for mixing information across the sequence.","FNet 用傅里叶变换作为一种固定的线性机制，在整个序列上混合信息。"],[756.57,763.3,129,"Notice that the Fourier block simply takes the place of the attention sublayer, with the feed-forward layer kept on top.","注意，傅里叶模块直接取代了注意力子层的位置，上面仍然保留前馈层。"],[763.65,771.41,129,"This explores whether a cheaper global interaction can support useful representations without standard self-attention.","这探索的是：在没有标准自注意力的情况下，一种更便宜的全局交互能否支撑起有用的表示。"],[771.76,780.26,129,"The reported text-classification results motivate that question, but do not establish equal performance for all generative tasks.","报告的文本分类结果激发了这个问题，但并不能证明它在所有生成任务上表现同样好。"],[780.61,787.61,129,"Next, we keep the familiar attention and feed-forward components, and instead ask whether their ordering matters.","接下来，我们保留熟悉的注意力和前馈组件，转而问：它们的排列顺序重要吗？"],[788.86,795.36,130,"The standard Transformer alternates attention and feed-forward sublayers, but other orderings are possible.","标准的 Transformer 交替排列注意力和前馈子层，但也可以有其他排列方式。"],[795.71,801.28,130,"Here, s in green is self-attention, and f in purple is feed-forward.","这里，绿色的 s 是自注意力，紫色的 f 是前馈层。"],[801.63,807.11,130,"The sandwich Transformer puts more attention at the bottom and more feed-forward at the top.","三明治 Transformer 把更多的注意力放在底部，把更多的前馈层放在顶部。"],[807.46,817.3,130,"Compare the arrangements with the reported perplexities on the right, which range from about twenty point seven down to eighteen point two; lower is better.","把这些排列方式和右边报告的困惑度对比，困惑度大约从 20.7 到 18.2；越低越好。"],[817.65,826.41,130,"Having the same number of components does not imply the same computation: each component receives representations shaped by the layers before it.","组件数量相同，并不意味着计算相同：每个组件接收到的表示，都由它前面的层塑造。"],[826.76,832.18,130,"This is another way to test the interaction between token mixing and feature transformation.","这是检验词元混合与特征变换之间相互作用的另一种方式。"],[832.53,836.62,130,"Next, we revisit the role of positional information.","接下来，我们重新审视位置信息的作用。"],[837.87,842.27,131,"Changing or removing position embeddings probes how the model uses order.","改变或去掉位置编码，可以探查模型是如何利用顺序的。"],[842.62,849.34,131,"This table comes from one of my own papers, On Position Embeddings in BERT, at ICLR.","这张表来自我自己的一篇论文，On Position Embeddings in BERT，发表在 ICLR。"],[849.69,858.28,131,"Without any position embedding, BERT's mean score drops to seventy-six point six, compared with around eighty-two with position embeddings.","没有任何位置编码时，BERT 的平均分降到 76.6，而有位置编码时大约是 82。"],[858.63,867.62,131,"But read the results task by task: CoLA falls sharply, from sixty point two to thirty-nine, while SST-2 drops much less.","但要逐个任务地看：CoLA 大幅下降，从 60.2 降到 39，而 SST-2 下降得少得多。"],[867.97,875.1,131,"Different tasks depend on word order in different ways, so an average alone may hide important effects.","不同任务对词序的依赖方式不同，所以只看平均值可能会掩盖重要的影响。"],[875.45,882.46,131,"Relate this to our earlier sinusoidal and rotary examples, which introduce position through different mechanisms.","把这一点和我们前面讲的正弦编码与旋转编码的例子联系起来，它们通过不同的机制引入位置。"],[882.81,888.31,131,"The next study turns from order information to the challenge of training much deeper Transformer stacks.","下一项研究从顺序信息转向另一个挑战：训练更深的 Transformer 堆叠。"],[889.56,892.7,132,"DeepNet scales Transformers to one thousand layers.","DeepNet 把 Transformer 扩展到了一千层。"],[893.05,901.32,132,"Its DeepNorm adjusts the scaling of the residual connection, and pairs that change with a corresponding initialization scheme.","它的 DeepNorm 调整了残差连接的缩放，并配合一个相应的初始化方案。"],[901.67,910.42,132,"Compare the standard LayerNorm of x plus F of x with the modified version, LayerNorm of alpha x plus F of x.","对比标准的 LayerNorm 作用于 x 加 F of x，和修改后的版本：LayerNorm 作用于 alpha 乘 x 加 F of x。"],[910.77,918.1,132,"In the formula, alpha rescales the residual input before normalization; it is not simply a replacement name for LayerNorm.","在公式中，alpha 在归一化之前对残差输入做缩放；它并不只是 LayerNorm 的另一个名字。"],[918.45,925.45,132,"The goal is to make very deep Transformers train more stably, while retaining useful performance.","目标是让非常深的 Transformer 训练得更稳定，同时保持良好的性能。"],[925.8,933.4,132,"This example shows that increasing depth requires attention to both architectural structure and optimization.","这个例子说明，增加深度需要同时关注架构结构和优化。"],[934.65,939.09,133,"Capacity can grow through depth, width or additional experts.","模型容量可以通过深度、宽度或增加专家来增长。"],[939.44,943.84,133,"WideNet explores a different allocation of parameters and computation.","WideNet 探索了一种不同的参数与计算分配方式。"],[944.19,953.24,133,"It shares parameters across blocks, and expands capacity through a mixture of experts, where a router sends each token to some of the feed-forward experts.","它在各个模块之间共享参数，并通过混合专家扩展容量，由路由器把每个词元分配给其中一些前馈专家。"],[953.59,958.24,133,"Compare total parameter capacity with the amount of computation activated for an input.","要比较总的参数容量，和对一个输入实际激活的计算量。"],[958.59,964.18,133,"Also consider whether each expert receives enough training tokens to learn effectively.","还要考虑每个专家是否能获得足够的训练词元，从而有效学习。"],[964.53,972.71,133,"We have now seen several ways to alter the architecture; next, we study empirical relationships between scale and performance.","我们已经看到了几种修改架构的方式；接下来，我们研究规模与性能之间的经验关系。"]]},{"n":10,"title":"Scaling Laws and Emergent Abilities","blurb":"How loss scales with model size, data and compute, compute-optimal training, test-time and agent scaling, and whether emergent abilities depend on the chosen metric.","file":"lecture04_part10.mp4","poster":"lecture04_part10.jpg","duration":696.8,"first":134,"last":149,"slides":[{"n":134,"title":"Lecture Roadmap","t":0.8},{"n":135,"title":"Scaling Laws","t":39.0},{"n":136,"title":"Scaling Model, Data and Compute","t":57.32},{"n":137,"title":"Predicting Performance at Scale","t":102.35},{"n":138,"title":"Model Capacity and Training Budget","t":165.52},{"n":139,"title":"Scaling Curves and Learning-rate Schedules","t":201.83},{"n":140,"title":"Comparing Models at Fixed Compute","t":236.44},{"n":141,"title":"New Dimensions of Scaling","t":271.47},{"n":142,"title":"Training-time and Test-time Compute","t":314.64},{"n":143,"title":"Scaling Agent Systems","t":351.58},{"n":144,"title":"New Scaling Directions","t":395.1},{"n":145,"title":"Emergent Abilities","t":459.78},{"n":146,"title":"Emergent Abilities in Language Models","t":481.43},{"n":147,"title":"Emergence and the Choice of Metric","t":536.35},{"n":148,"title":"Acknowledgements","t":595.84},{"n":149,"title":"Course Project Discussion","t":631.89}],"sents":[[0.8,3.1,134,"Let's pause and look at the roadmap again.","我们停下来，再看一下路线图。"],[3.45,11.75,134,"We started with NLP tasks and representations, and the inductive bias of semantic abstraction and composition.","我们从 NLP 任务与表示讲起，然后是语义抽象与组合这一归纳偏置。"],[12.1,22.6,134,"Then, under one heading, we compared four architecture families: multilayer perceptrons, convolutional networks, recurrent networks and the Transformer.","接着，在同一个标题下，我们比较了四类架构：多层感知机、卷积网络、循环网络和 Transformer。"],[22.95,25.9,134,"Each family combines token information in its own way.","每一类架构都有自己组合词元信息的方式。"],[26.25,31.6,134,"Now we move to the bold item, the last part of today: scaling laws and emergence.","现在我们进入加粗的这一项，也是今天的最后一部分：规模定律与涌现。"],[31.95,37.6,134,"Keep the mechanisms we just studied in mind, because they are what gets scaled up.","请记住我们刚刚学过的这些机制，因为被放大规模的，正是它们。"],[38.85,44.7,135,"A scaling law describes an empirical relationship between resource scale and a performance measure.","规模定律描述的是资源规模与某个性能指标之间的经验关系。"],[45.05,55.92,135,"Before interpreting any curve, identify the resource on the horizontal axis, the metric on the vertical axis, and the experimental regime in which the relationship was measured.","在解读任何曲线之前，先弄清横轴上的资源、纵轴上的指标，以及测量这种关系时所处的实验范围。"],[57.17,65.74,136,"The classic language-model scaling experiments, by Kaplan and colleagues, found relatively smooth, predictable trends in loss.","Kaplan 等人经典的语言模型规模实验发现，损失呈现出相对平滑、可预测的趋势。"],[66.09,72.44,136,"Loss decreased as compute, dataset size and parameters increased, within the studied ranges.","在所研究的范围内，随着计算量、数据集规模和参数量的增加，损失不断下降。"],[72.79,77.63,136,"On these log-log axes, each trend looks like a straight line: a power law.","在这些双对数坐标轴上，每一种趋势看起来都像一条直线，也就是幂律。"],[77.98,85.88,136,"Each family of curves answers a question under particular constraints, so read the axes carefully before comparing them.","每一组曲线都是在特定约束下回答某个问题，所以在比较之前要仔细看清坐标轴。"],[86.23,93.39,136,"And a predictable language-model loss curve does not imply that every downstream task improves at the same rate.","而且，语言模型损失曲线可预测，并不意味着每个下游任务都以同样的速度提升。"],[93.74,100.95,136,"The next example uses smaller-scale experiments to forecast a larger model's performance on a specific metric.","下一个例子用更小规模的实验，来预测一个更大模型在某个具体指标上的表现。"],[102.2,110.66,137,"Here's how you predict performance at scale: measure smaller runs, fit a trend, then test a prediction at a larger scale.","这就是如何预测大规模下的性能：先测量小规模的运行，拟合趋势，再在更大规模上检验预测。"],[111.01,114.44,137,"First, observe the gray points from smaller training runs.","第一步，观察这些来自较小训练运行的灰色点。"],[114.79,121.4,137,"The horizontal axis is logarithmic, and normalized so that the final run equals one.","横轴是对数刻度，并做了归一化，使最终那次运行等于一。"],[121.75,127.33,137,"Second, fit a power law with an irreducible loss term to those smaller runs.","第二步，用一个带不可约损失项的幂律去拟合这些小规模运行。"],[127.68,132.75,137,"The fitted curve summarizes a trend, rather than literally joining every observation.","拟合的曲线概括的是趋势，而不是把每个观测点都连起来。"],[133.1,138.19,137,"Third, extrapolate to predict the large run, before seeing its result.","第三步，在看到结果之前，外推预测大规模运行的结果。"],[138.54,142.2,137,"Fourth, compare the observed green point with the prediction.","第四步，把观测到的绿色点和预测进行比较。"],[142.55,150.25,137,"The GPT-4 report describes predicting held-out code loss without using partial results from the large run.","GPT-4 技术报告描述了在不使用大规模运行部分结果的情况下，预测留出代码数据上的损失。"],[150.6,157.62,137,"This figure is an approximate reconstruction, so use the paper for exact evidence, not the plotted coordinates here.","这张图是近似的重绘，所以请以论文为准，而不是这里画出的坐标。"],[157.97,164.12,137,"And predictability for this metric does not guarantee predictability of every capability.","而且，这个指标可预测，并不保证每一种能力都可预测。"],[165.37,171.85,138,"Choosing a model under a fixed training budget is different from training a given model for as long as possible.","在固定的训练预算下选择模型，和把一个给定模型训练得尽可能久，是两回事。"],[172.2,177.25,138,"Look at the training-loss curves for models from seventy-five million to ten billion parameters.","看这些训练损失曲线，模型规模从 7500 万到 100 亿参数不等。"],[177.6,185.53,138,"A smaller model may improve quickly early on, while a larger model may achieve lower loss when given substantially more computation.","小模型可能在早期进步很快，而大模型在得到多得多的计算量时，可能达到更低的损失。"],[185.88,190.4,138,"The best choice therefore depends on the budget and the assumptions.","因此，最佳选择取决于预算和假设。"],[190.75,195.73,138,"Treat the discussion around Chinchilla as a question about those regimes.","关于 Chinchilla 的讨论，应该被看作是关于这些不同情形的问题。"],[196.08,200.43,138,"We will first compare progress by tokens, then by computational cost.","我们先按词元数比较进展，再按计算成本比较。"],[201.68,207.96,139,"Here the loss curves for four LLaMA models are plotted against the number of training tokens.","这里四个 LLaMA 模型的损失曲线，是对照训练词元数量画出来的。"],[208.31,213.26,139,"Notice that the slope changes over training, rather than remaining constant.","注意，斜率在训练过程中不断变化，而不是保持不变。"],[213.61,219.68,139,"A flatter endpoint can partly reflect the learning-rate schedule, such as cosine decay.","曲线末端变平，部分原因可能是学习率调度，比如余弦衰减。"],[220.03,224.7,139,"So it should not automatically be interpreted as a hard capacity limit.","所以不应该自动地把它理解为一个硬性的容量上限。"],[225.05,227.67,139,"Read optimization choices alongside the curve.","要结合优化设置来解读曲线。"],[228.02,235.04,139,"The next slide changes the comparison axis, to ask how much improvement each model buys with the same computation.","下一页换了一个比较的坐标轴，问的是：用同样的计算量，每个模型能换来多少提升。"],[236.29,243.0,140,"At fixed compute, the relevant question is how much each model learns within an equal resource budget.","在固定计算量下，相关的问题是：在同样的资源预算内，每个模型能学到多少。"],[243.35,247.79,140,"Now the horizontal axis is GPU-hours instead of tokens.","现在横轴是 GPU 小时数，而不是词元数。"],[248.14,255.14,140,"A larger model generally spends more computation per token, so matching tokens and matching compute are different comparisons.","更大的模型通常在每个词元上花费更多计算量，所以按词元对齐和按计算量对齐是两种不同的比较。"],[255.49,259.56,140,"Curves can cross, and continued training may change the ranking.","曲线可能会交叉，继续训练也可能改变排名。"],[259.91,264.02,140,"Extrapolation beyond the observed range remains uncertain.","超出观测范围的外推仍然是不确定的。"],[264.37,270.07,140,"We will now broaden the notion of scaling to include computation spent during inference.","接下来，我们把规模的概念扩展到推理时所花的计算。"],[271.32,274.94,141,"Test-time computation can be expanded in different ways.","测试时的计算可以通过不同的方式来扩展。"],[275.29,281.41,141,"Parallel scaling samples multiple candidates and uses a verifier or another selection mechanism.","并行扩展会采样多个候选答案，再用验证器或其他选择机制挑选。"],[281.76,290.52,141,"Sequential scaling produces additional intermediate reasoning steps within a trajectory, as in OpenAI o1 and DeepSeek R1.","顺序扩展则在一条推理轨迹中生成更多的中间推理步骤，比如 OpenAI o1 和 DeepSeek R1。"],[290.87,298.5,141,"These designs have different costs and failure modes; simply spending more computation does not guarantee continued improvement.","这些设计有不同的成本和失效模式；单纯花更多计算，并不能保证持续提升。"],[298.85,306.2,141,"Our own study on verifier-guided search in mathematical reasoning highlights how much the selection signal matters.","我们自己关于数学推理中验证器引导搜索的研究，突出了选择信号有多么重要。"],[306.55,313.24,141,"Next, we separate reasoning-related training compute from reasoning compute used at test time.","接下来，我们把与推理相关的训练计算，和测试时用于推理的计算区分开。"],[314.49,318.61,142,"The o1 example distinguishes two budgets.","o1 这个例子区分了两种预算。"],[318.96,326.08,142,"One plot shows AIME accuracy as reinforcement-learning computation during training increases.","一张图展示的是随着训练期间强化学习计算量的增加，AIME 准确率的变化。"],[326.43,331.79,142,"The other shows accuracy as more computation is spent reasoning at test time.","另一张图展示的是随着测试时用于推理的计算量增加，准确率的变化。"],[332.14,335.86,142,"In both, performance improves smoothly on a log scale of compute.","在两张图中，性能都随着对数刻度下的计算量平滑提升。"],[336.21,341.63,142,"But these are not the same variable, and neither should be silently equated with pre-training scale.","但它们不是同一个变量，也都不应该被默认为等同于预训练的规模。"],[341.98,350.18,142,"The broader point is that resource allocation extends beyond a model's parameter count and pre-training dataset size.","更广泛的观点是：资源分配不仅仅是模型的参数量和预训练数据规模。"],[351.43,354.38,143,"What about scaling the number of agents?","那么，扩展智能体的数量又如何呢？"],[354.73,362.72,143,"Increasing the number of agents does not by itself establish a reliable scaling law: more agents alone may offer limited gains.","增加智能体的数量本身，并不能建立一个可靠的规模定律：只增加智能体可能收益有限。"],[363.07,371.73,143,"The benefit depends on how agents coordinate, what feedback the environment provides, and whether that feedback can identify useful behavior.","收益取决于智能体之间如何协作、环境提供什么样的反馈，以及这些反馈能否识别出有用的行为。"],[372.08,383.04,143,"The figure, from CAMEL-AI, presents environment interaction as a promising research direction, rather than a guaranteed outcome.","这张来自 CAMEL-AI 的图，把环境交互呈现为一个有前景的研究方向，而不是一个必然的结果。"],[383.39,388.5,143,"So always ask: what measurable improvement would demonstrate success?","所以要始终追问：什么样的可测量提升才能证明它成功了？"],[388.85,393.7,143,"Let's collect these different scaling dimensions before turning to emergent abilities.","在讨论涌现能力之前，我们先把这些不同的扩展维度汇总一下。"],[394.95,401.83,144,"This is a set of research questions, not a claim that every proposed axis follows a power law.","这是一组研究问题，而不是断言每一个提出的维度都遵循幂律。"],[402.18,407.41,144,"A useful scaling proposal names both the resource and the measurable return.","一个有用的扩展方案，要同时说明投入的资源和可测量的回报。"],[407.76,413.06,144,"Data can increase in coverage and verified experience, not only in token count.","数据的增长可以体现在覆盖面和经过验证的经验上，而不只是词元数量。"],[413.41,425.86,144,"Test-time computation can increase through longer reasoning, candidate generation or search; its return depends on how useful steps and final choices are selected.","测试时计算可以通过更长的推理、生成候选或搜索来增加；回报取决于如何挑选有用的步骤和最终答案。"],[426.21,432.57,144,"External memory and tools can increase accessible knowledge, but retrieval quality and errors matter.","外部记忆和工具可以增加可获取的知识，但检索质量和错误同样重要。"],[432.92,438.31,144,"Architecture can change how effectively parameters and computation are used.","架构可以改变参数和计算被利用的效率。"],[438.66,444.23,144,"Additional agents can divide work, while also adding communication and coordination costs.","更多的智能体可以分工，但也会增加沟通和协调的成本。"],[444.58,452.83,144,"Ask for controlled measurements: hold the cost and evaluation protocol fixed, then estimate the marginal gain and where it saturates.","要求受控的测量：固定成本和评估协议，然后估计边际收益，以及它在哪里饱和。"],[453.18,458.38,144,"Try to propose one experiment that could reject your own preferred hypothesis.","试着提出一个可能推翻你自己所偏爱假设的实验。"],[459.63,461.98,145,"Now, emergent abilities.","现在来看涌现能力。"],[462.33,470.68,145,"An emergent ability describes a pattern where small models stay near a baseline, while larger models show a clearly measurable capability.","涌现能力描述的是这样一种模式：小模型停留在基线附近，而大模型表现出明显可测量的能力。"],[471.03,474.5,145,"Its interpretation depends on the task and the metric.","对它的解读取决于任务和指标。"],[474.85,480.03,145,"We will compare examples of the pattern with a measurement-based alternative explanation.","我们会把这种模式的例子，和一种基于测量方式的替代解释进行比较。"],[481.28,483.78,146,"Here is the setting: few-shot prompting.","这是实验设置：少样本提示。"],[484.13,491.45,146,"The model sees a couple of labeled examples in the prompt, like reviews with their sentiment, and then must complete a new one.","模型在提示中看到几个带标签的例子，比如评论及其情感，然后要补全一个新的例子。"],[491.8,499.95,146,"On some few-shot tasks, performance stays near a random baseline at smaller scales, and rises markedly at larger scales.","在一些少样本任务上，小规模时性能停留在随机基线附近，到大规模时显著上升。"],[500.3,511.19,146,"These panels plot tasks like modular arithmetic and word unscrambling against training compute, for models such as GPT-3, Gopher, Chinchilla and PaLM.","这些面板把模运算、单词还原等任务的表现，对照训练计算量画出来，模型包括 GPT-3、Gopher、Chinchilla 和 PaLM。"],[511.54,514.6,146,"This motivates the term emergent ability.","这就引出了“涌现能力”这个术语。"],[514.95,521.9,146,"However, the observation belongs to a particular combination of models, prompts, tasks and evaluation rules.","然而，这一观察结果属于模型、提示、任务和评估规则的一个特定组合。"],[522.25,527.79,146,"The apparent onset depends on the task, the baseline and the evaluation metric.","表面上的出现时机取决于任务、基线和评估指标。"],[528.14,534.95,146,"The next slide asks whether an abrupt-looking curve can arise even when the underlying improvement is smoother.","下一页要问的是：即使底层的提升更平滑，是否也可能出现一条看起来很突然的曲线？"],[536.2,541.73,147,"A nonlinear or discontinuous metric can make gradual improvements appear sudden.","非线性或不连续的指标，可能让渐进的提升看起来像是突然出现的。"],[542.08,551.15,147,"Panel A shows per-token loss falling smoothly with model size, and panel B turns it into a smoothly rising probability of a correct token.","图 A 显示每个词元的损失随模型规模平滑下降，图 B 把它转换成正确词元概率的平滑上升。"],[551.5,560.69,147,"Score the outputs with a nonlinear metric like exact accuracy, or a discontinuous one like multiple-choice grade, and you see emergence.","如果用非线性指标，比如完全正确率，或不连续指标，比如多选题评分，你就会看到涌现。"],[561.04,568.46,147,"Score them linearly or continuously, and the same models show no emergent abilities.","如果用线性或连续的指标来评分，同样的模型就看不到涌现能力。"],[568.81,575.61,147,"For example, a measure that gives credit only when a complete answer is correct may hide partial progress.","比如，只有当整个答案完全正确才给分的指标，可能会掩盖部分的进步。"],[575.96,584.09,147,"Re-evaluating with alternative metrics helps distinguish a change in the model from a change in how we summarize its behavior.","用其他指标重新评估，可以帮助区分是模型本身发生了变化，还是我们概括其行为的方式发生了变化。"],[584.44,587.44,147,"This discussion does not deny that models improve.","这一讨论并不否认模型在进步。"],[587.79,594.44,147,"It asks us to interpret capability curves with the same care we applied to scaling loss curves.","它要求我们像解读规模损失曲线那样，同样谨慎地解读能力曲线。"],[595.69,600.28,148,"This lecture draws on several public courses and teaching resources.","本讲参考了多门公开课程和教学资源。"],[600.63,615.66,148,"They include Princeton's COS four eighty-four, Illinois's CS four forty-seven, Stanford's CS231n, a Medium summary by Gautam Karmakar, and Mohit Iyyer's CS six eighty-five at UMass Amherst.","包括普林斯顿的 COS 484、伊利诺伊的 CS 447、斯坦福的 CS231n、Gautam Karmakar 在 Medium 上的总结，以及 Mohit Iyyer 在麻省大学阿默斯特分校的 CS 685。"],[616.01,621.77,148,"They provide additional explanations, exercises and original examples for follow-up study.","它们提供了更多的讲解、练习和原始例子，供大家课后学习。"],[622.12,630.49,148,"The detailed references on individual slides identify the papers behind specific architectures and empirical results.","各页幻灯片上的详细参考文献，标明了具体架构和实验结果背后的论文。"],[631.74,634.14,149,"Finally, a few words on your course projects.","最后，说几句关于课程项目的话。"],[634.49,641.31,149,"For research projects, sharpen the question into a hypothesis that can be tested with a clear evaluation.","对于研究型项目，要把问题打磨成一个可以用清晰评估来检验的假设。"],[641.66,649.45,149,"For application projects, identify the intended users, their needs, and evidence that the system provides value.","对于应用型项目，要明确目标用户、他们的需求，以及系统能提供价值的证据。"],[649.8,655.18,149,"Discuss scope alongside ambition, so that the work remains achievable.","在谈抱负的同时也要讨论范围，让工作保持可完成。"],[655.53,662.46,149,"And for the assignments, collect your current obstacles, and connect them to the relevant architecture or training concepts.","至于作业，请把你目前遇到的困难整理出来，并把它们和相关的架构或训练概念联系起来。"],[662.81,664.72,149,"So, let's wrap up today.","好，我们来总结一下今天的内容。"],[665.07,675.25,149,"We built the Transformer piece by piece: self-attention, multi-head attention, feed-forward layers, residual connections and position encodings.","我们一步步搭建了 Transformer：自注意力、多头注意力、前馈层、残差连接和位置编码。"],[675.6,681.61,149,"We looked at its variants and ablations, and at how loss, compute and abilities scale.","我们还看了它的各种变体与消融实验，以及损失、计算量和能力是如何随规模变化的。"],[681.96,688.24,149,"Next time, in Lecture five, we put these pieces together at scale: Large Language Models.","下一次，在第五讲中，我们会把这些部件放到大规模下组合起来：大语言模型。"],[688.59,694.93,149,"Before we finish, the appendix gives a closer look at backpropagation, with worked numerical examples.","在结束之前，附录会用具体的数值例子，更仔细地讲解反向传播。"]]},{"n":11,"title":"Appendix: Backpropagation Worked Examples","blurb":"The chain rule as local rules on a computation graph, sigmoid modules in PyTorch, saturation, dying ReLUs and exploding gradients in RNNs.","file":"lecture04_part11.mp4","poster":"lecture04_part11.jpg","duration":686.7,"first":150,"last":161,"slides":[{"n":150,"title":"Backpropagation: Worked Examples","t":0.8},{"n":151,"title":"Backpropagation","t":21.64},{"n":152,"title":"Backpropagation on a Computation Graph","t":172.06},{"n":153,"title":"The Local Rule for Backpropagation","t":235.56},{"n":154,"title":"A Sigmoid Computation Graph","t":275.27},{"n":155,"title":"Backpropagation Through Elementary Operations","t":309.24},{"n":156,"title":"The Sigmoid Module and Its Derivative","t":374.3},{"n":157,"title":"Forward and Backward Module Interfaces","t":425.09},{"n":158,"title":"Sigmoid in PyTorch","t":468.85},{"n":159,"title":"Saturated sigmoid or tanh units have very small derivatives. Initialization should keep activations in a region with use","t":510.97},{"n":160,"title":"Dying ReLU Units","t":551.78},{"n":161,"title":"Exploding Gradients in RNNs","t":625.87}],"sents":[[0.8,5.55,150,"Welcome to the appendix: backpropagation, through worked examples.","欢迎来到附录：通过具体例子来理解反向传播。"],[5.9,9.27,150,"Here we turn the chain rule into small numerical calculations.","在这里，我们把链式法则变成一些小的数值计算。"],[9.62,13.17,150,"Keep a separate record of forward values and backward gradients.","请把前向的数值和反向的梯度分开记录。"],[13.52,20.24,150,"We will first work through a simple network, then connect the same local rules to modular automatic differentiation.","我们先算一个简单的网络，再把同样的局部规则和模块化的自动微分联系起来。"],[21.49,31.75,151,"Here's a small feed-forward classifier: a four-dimensional input, a linear layer with ReLU, three hidden features, and a second linear layer giving two logits.","这是一个小的前馈分类器：四维输入，一个带 ReLU 的线性层，三个隐藏特征，再经过第二个线性层得到两个 logit。"],[32.1,33.87,151,"The target class is positive.","目标类别是“正面”。"],[34.22,42.92,151,"With the initial weights, the model gives the correct class only thirty-nine point five percent, and the cross-entropy loss is zero point nine two eight.","在初始权重下，模型给正确类别的概率只有 39.5%，交叉熵损失是 0.928。"],[43.27,47.38,151,"How should each weight change to make this example less wrong?","每个权重应该怎样变化，才能让这个例子错得少一点？"],[47.73,60.54,151,"Start at the output: for softmax followed by cross-entropy, the derivative with respect to the logits is p minus y, which is plus zero point six zero five and minus zero point six zero five.","从输出开始：对于 softmax 加交叉熵，关于 logit 的导数就是 p 减 y，也就是正 0.605 和负 0.605。"],[60.89,67.19,151,"A positive derivative on the negative score says that increasing that score would increase the loss.","负面类分数上的导数为正，说明增大这个分数会增大损失。"],[67.54,73.19,151,"A negative derivative on the positive score says that increasing it would decrease the loss.","正面类分数上的导数为负，说明增大它会减小损失。"],[73.54,84.41,151,"Now zoom into one output weight in the second matrix: it connects hidden feature h2, which is zero point five, to the positive score, and starts at zero point five.","现在聚焦第二个矩阵中的一个输出权重：它把值为 0.5 的隐藏特征 h2 连接到正面类分数，初始值是 0.5。"],[84.76,93.1,151,"Its gradient is minus zero point six zero five times zero point five, which is about minus zero point three zero two.","它的梯度是负 0.605 乘以 0.5，约等于负 0.302。"],[93.45,99.0,151,"That's the chain rule in a single connection: downstream sensitivity times local sensitivity.","这就是单个连接上的链式法则：下游的敏感度乘以局部的敏感度。"],[99.35,108.17,151,"The whole output matrix follows the same rule: its gradient is the outer product of delta and h transposed, a two by three matrix.","整个输出矩阵遵循同样的规则：它的梯度是 delta 与 h 转置的外积，是一个 2 乘 3 的矩阵。"],[108.52,115.8,151,"Every weight receives an error signal scaled by the feature it used, with no need to perturb each weight experimentally.","每个权重收到的误差信号，都按它所用的特征进行缩放，不需要逐个去扰动权重做实验。"],[116.15,127.67,151,"Next, W2 transposed passes the error back to the three hidden features, giving about plus zero point three zero two, minus zero point five four four, and plus zero point one eight one.","接着，W2 的转置把误差传回三个隐藏特征，大约是正 0.302、负 0.544 和正 0.181。"],[128.02,135.16,151,"All three ReLU pre-activations are positive here, so ReLU passes the gradient through; a zeroed ReLU would block it.","这里三个 ReLU 的预激活值都是正的，所以 ReLU 让梯度通过；如果 ReLU 输出为零，就会阻断梯度。"],[135.51,140.46,151,"Then update every parameter at once, with step size zero point two.","然后用 0.2 的步长，同时更新所有参数。"],[140.81,146.25,151,"The highlighted weight goes from zero point five to about zero point five six.","被高亮的那个权重从 0.5 变成约 0.56。"],[146.6,157.17,151,"Run a fresh forward pass: the positive class now gets eighty-one point one percent, and the loss falls from zero point nine two eight to zero point two one.","重新做一次前向传播：正面类现在得到 81.1% 的概率，损失从 0.928 降到 0.21。"],[157.52,161.39,151,"Forward makes a prediction; backward computes responsibility.","前向负责做预测；反向负责计算“责任”。"],[161.74,170.66,151,"Responsibility here is a sensitivity analogy, not a claim that individual weights have independent semantic roles.","这里的“责任”只是对敏感度的类比，并不是说单个权重有独立的语义角色。"],[171.91,178.97,152,"This example isolates the local derivative rule, on the function f equals x plus y, times z.","这个例子单独拿出局部求导规则，用的函数是 f 等于 x 加 y，再乘以 z。"],[179.32,184.39,152,"The inputs are x equals minus two, y equals five and z equals minus four.","输入是 x 等于负 2，y 等于 5，z 等于负 4。"],[184.74,192.32,152,"Run forward: q equals x plus y, which is three, and f equals q times z, which is minus twelve.","先做前向：q 等于 x 加 y，也就是 3；f 等于 q 乘 z，也就是负 12。"],[192.67,198.21,152,"Seed the output gradient: the derivative of f with respect to itself is one.","设定输出的梯度：f 对它自身的导数是 1。"],[198.56,205.66,152,"At the multiplication, the local derivatives are z for q, which is minus four, and q for z, which is three.","在乘法节点，局部导数分别是：对 q 是 z，即负 4；对 z 是 q，即 3。"],[206.01,215.18,152,"At the addition, both local derivatives are one, so x and y each receive minus four times one, which is minus four.","在加法节点，两个局部导数都是 1，所以 x 和 y 各自得到负 4 乘以 1，也就是负 4。"],[215.53,220.78,152,"So a small increase in either x or y decreases f at this point.","所以在这一点上，稍微增大 x 或 y，都会让 f 减小。"],[221.13,228.16,152,"Note that these are derivatives of f, not of a training loss; a learning objective would add a loss node before gradient descent.","注意，这些是 f 的导数，而不是训练损失的导数；学习目标会在梯度下降之前再加一个损失节点。"],[228.51,234.16,152,"The vector network we just saw applies exactly this local rule to matrix operations.","我们刚才看到的向量网络，正是把这个局部规则应用到了矩阵运算上。"],[235.41,241.07,153,"The general local rule: a node receives the gradient of the loss with respect to its output.","通用的局部规则是：一个节点接收损失对它输出的梯度。"],[241.42,246.5,153,"Each input gradient is the upstream gradient multiplied by the local derivative.","每个输入的梯度，等于上游梯度乘以局部导数。"],[246.85,253.81,153,"A large computational graph can be differentiated by repeatedly applying that rule at each node.","一个大的计算图，可以通过在每个节点反复应用这条规则来求导。"],[254.16,260.05,153,"If a variable influences the loss along multiple paths, the gradient contributions must be added.","如果一个变量通过多条路径影响损失，各条路径的梯度贡献必须相加。"],[260.4,265.07,153,"This local organization is what makes modular automatic differentiation possible.","正是这种局部的组织方式，让模块化的自动微分成为可能。"],[265.42,273.87,153,"Next, we build a more complicated expression from elementary operations, and then group some of them into a reusable module.","接下来，我们用基本运算搭一个更复杂的表达式，然后把其中一些运算组合成一个可复用的模块。"],[275.12,280.84,154,"This example applies a sigmoid to a weighted sum of two inputs and a bias.","这个例子把 sigmoid 作用在两个输入的加权和再加一个偏置上。"],[281.19,290.8,154,"Follow the forward graph: multiplication, addition, adding w2, negation, exponentiation, adding one, and the reciprocal.","沿着前向图走：乘法、加法、加上 w2、取负、取指数、加一，再取倒数。"],[291.15,295.28,154,"Store the intermediate values, because the backward pass will need them.","要把中间值保存下来，因为反向传播会用到它们。"],[295.63,302.24,154,"The expression looks more complicated than the previous example, but every node has a simple local derivative.","这个表达式看起来比前一个例子复杂，但每个节点都有一个简单的局部导数。"],[302.59,307.84,154,"The next slide traces how those derivatives combine during backpropagation.","下一页追踪这些导数在反向传播中是如何组合起来的。"],[309.09,318.83,155,"Here are the values: w0 is two, x0 is minus one, w1 is minus three, x1 is minus two, and w2 is minus three.","这些是取值：w0 是 2，x0 是负 1，w1 是负 3，x1 是负 2，w2 是负 3。"],[319.18,328.43,155,"Going forward, the products are minus two and six, the sum is one, and the sigmoid output is zero point seven three one.","前向计算中，两个乘积是负 2 和 6，加权和是 1，sigmoid 的输出是 0.731。"],[328.78,337.71,155,"Now work backward through the reciprocal, exponential and arithmetic nodes, multiplying by the local derivative at each step.","现在反向经过倒数、指数和算术节点，每一步都乘以局部导数。"],[338.06,340.79,155,"The local rules are listed at the bottom right.","局部求导规则列在右下角。"],[341.14,344.64,155,"The gradient reaching the weighted-sum part is approximately zero point two.","到达加权和部分的梯度大约是 0.2。"],[344.99,352.28,155,"At each multiplication, the gradient for one input is scaled by the other input's forward value.","在每个乘法节点，一个输入的梯度会被另一个输入的前向值缩放。"],[352.63,363.61,155,"So the gradient for w0 is zero point two times minus one, which is minus zero point two, and for x0 it is zero point two times two, which is zero point four.","所以 w0 的梯度是 0.2 乘以负 1，即负 0.2；x0 的梯度是 0.2 乘以 2，即 0.4。"],[363.96,366.62,155,"The procedure is still the same chain rule.","这个过程依然是同一个链式法则。"],[366.97,372.9,155,"We can simplify the implementation by treating the sigmoid subgraph as a single differentiable module.","我们可以把 sigmoid 这部分子图当作一个可微的模块，从而简化实现。"],[374.15,379.17,156,"The graph already showed sigmoid as a sequence of elementary operations.","前面的图已经把 sigmoid 表示成了一串基本运算。"],[379.52,384.7,156,"But a computation graph is not unique: we can group operations into different modules.","但计算图并不是唯一的：我们可以把运算组合成不同的模块。"],[385.05,390.08,156,"Here, sigma of x is one over one plus e to the minus x.","这里，sigma of x 等于 1 除以 1 加 e 的负 x 次方。"],[390.43,397.37,156,"Its derivative is sigma times one minus sigma, which can be calculated directly from the forward output.","它的导数是 sigma 乘以 1 减 sigma，可以直接由前向输出算出来。"],[397.72,403.43,156,"The sigmoid module takes an input of one and outputs zero point seven three one.","sigmoid 模块的输入是 1，输出是 0.731。"],[403.78,413.01,156,"Multiply the upstream gradient of one by zero point seven three one, times one minus zero point seven three one, and you get about zero point two.","用上游梯度 1 乘以 0.731，再乘以 1 减 0.731，大约得到 0.2。"],[413.36,419.42,156,"We have reached the same result with a larger local module, so choose modules with simple local gradients.","我们用一个更大的局部模块得到了同样的结果，所以要选择局部梯度简单的模块。"],[419.77,423.69,156,"This motivates the forward and backward interfaces on the next slide.","这引出了下一页的前向和反向接口。"],[424.94,430.76,157,"A module's forward operation computes its output and caches values that will be needed later.","一个模块的前向操作计算输出，并缓存之后会用到的值。"],[431.11,439.87,157,"Its backward operation receives an upstream gradient, and returns gradients for the inputs, and for parameters when appropriate.","它的反向操作接收上游梯度，并返回输入的梯度，必要时还返回参数的梯度。"],[440.22,447.77,157,"This custom multiplication makes the interface concrete: forward saves x and y and returns x times y.","这个自定义乘法让接口变得具体：前向保存 x 和 y，并返回 x 乘 y。"],[448.12,452.65,157,"Backward gives each input the upstream gradient multiplied by the other input.","反向则让每个输入得到上游梯度乘以另一个输入。"],[453.0,457.4,157,"The cached other input is exactly what the local derivative requires.","缓存下来的另一个输入，正是局部导数所需要的。"],[457.75,462.39,157,"This organization allows a network to be composed from reusable parts.","这种组织方式让网络可以由可复用的部件组合而成。"],[462.74,467.45,157,"We now connect that interface to a historical sigmoid implementation.","现在我们把这个接口和一个历史上的 sigmoid 实现联系起来。"],[468.7,475.23,158,"The forward sigmoid computation returns one over one plus the exponential of minus a.","前向的 sigmoid 计算返回 1 除以 1 加 e 的负 a 次方。"],[475.58,484.47,158,"The backward computation reuses that output z, and multiplies the incoming gradient by one minus z, times z.","反向计算复用那个输出 z，把传入的梯度乘以 1 减 z，再乘以 z。"],[484.82,489.45,158,"That's sigma times one minus sigma, times the upstream gradient.","这就是 sigma 乘以 1 减 sigma，再乘以上游梯度。"],[489.8,495.56,158,"Match the mathematical expression to the two code regions, rather than memorizing the file path.","要把数学表达式和这两段代码对应起来，而不是去记文件路径。"],[495.91,500.95,158,"This is a historical PyTorch implementation, useful for understanding the interface.","这是一个历史上的 PyTorch 实现，有助于理解这个接口。"],[501.3,509.57,158,"We finish with three training problems that arise when local derivatives repeatedly become too small, zero, or too large.","最后，我们来看三个训练问题，分别出现在局部导数反复变得太小、为零或太大的时候。"],[510.82,517.3,159,"Sigmoid derivatives become very small when the input lies far into either saturated region.","当输入深入任一饱和区时，sigmoid 的导数会变得非常小。"],[517.65,523.9,159,"The derivative peaks at only zero point two five, at zero, and approaches zero on both sides.","导数最大值只有 0.25，出现在零点，两侧都趋近于零。"],[524.25,527.08,159,"Tanh has a similar saturation issue.","tanh 也有类似的饱和问题。"],[527.43,532.78,159,"In a deep chain, multiplying many small derivatives can severely weaken the learning signal.","在很深的链条中，许多很小的导数相乘，会严重削弱学习信号。"],[533.13,540.13,159,"Initialization matters, because it influences whether many units begin in these regions.","初始化很重要，因为它决定了是否有很多单元一开始就处在这些区域。"],[540.48,545.62,159,"Inspecting activation and gradient distributions can help diagnose the problem.","检查激活值和梯度的分布，可以帮助诊断这个问题。"],[545.97,550.38,159,"The next slide shows a different way a unit can lose its gradient signal.","下一页展示单元失去梯度信号的另一种方式。"],[551.63,556.17,160,"A ReLU computes the maximum of zero and its pre-activation.","ReLU 计算的是零和它的预激活值中的较大者。"],[556.52,564.2,160,"A positive pre-activation has local derivative one, so the loss can send a gradient through the unit.","预激活值为正时，局部导数是 1，所以损失可以把梯度传过这个单元。"],[564.55,569.59,160,"But a parameter update can move all the training examples to negative pre-activations.","但一次参数更新可能会把所有训练样本都推到负的预激活区域。"],[569.94,577.71,160,"The two red points represent examples after that update, and the green point illustrates the earlier active condition.","两个红点代表更新之后的样本，绿点表示之前处于激活状态的情况。"],[578.06,583.88,160,"The diagram compares these two conditions, rather than tracking individual measurements.","这张图比较的是这两种情况，而不是追踪具体的测量值。"],[584.23,593.15,160,"On the negative branch, the local derivative is zero, so the chain rule gives zero gradient to this unit's incoming weight through this path.","在负半轴上，局部导数是零，所以链式法则沿这条路径给这个单元的输入权重的梯度为零。"],[593.5,598.3,160,"A unit that stays negative across the training data can remain inactive.","一个在整个训练数据上都保持为负的单元，可能会一直处于不激活状态。"],[598.65,603.94,160,"A negative response for only one example is normal, and is not sufficient to call the unit dead.","只对某一个样本输出为负是正常的，不足以说这个单元已经“死亡”。"],[604.29,609.34,160,"Smaller learning rates and appropriate initialization can reduce this risk.","更小的学习率和合适的初始化可以降低这种风险。"],[609.69,619.75,160,"A leaky rectifier gives the negative branch a nonzero slope, so it supplies a gradient there, but it does not guarantee better performance on every task.","Leaky ReLU 让负半轴有一个非零斜率，从而在那里提供梯度，但它并不保证在每个任务上都表现更好。"],[620.1,624.47,160,"Changes elsewhere in a network can also change the unit's input distribution.","网络其他地方的变化，也可能改变这个单元的输入分布。"],[625.72,633.72,161,"Finally, across time, an RNN's gradient contains repeated state transformations and activation derivatives.","最后，在时间维度上，RNN 的梯度包含反复出现的状态变换和激活函数导数。"],[634.07,640.1,161,"In this code, the forward pass applies the shared matrix and then ReLU, fifty times.","在这段代码中，前向传播先应用共享矩阵再应用 ReLU，重复 50 次。"],[640.45,645.51,161,"The backward pass applies the ReLU mask and then the transposed matrix, at every step.","反向传播在每一步都先应用 ReLU 掩码，再应用转置矩阵。"],[645.86,653.41,161,"Some directions can be amplified through this product, causing unstable gradients; small products weaken them instead.","某些方向会在这个连乘中被放大，导致梯度不稳定；而连乘较小时，梯度则会被削弱。"],[653.76,657.49,161,"Gradient clipping limits gradient magnitude before an update.","梯度裁剪在更新之前限制梯度的大小。"],[657.84,664.12,161,"Gating changes how information travels, but does not remove the need to diagnose training behavior.","门控改变了信息传递的方式，但并不能免去诊断训练行为的需要。"],[664.47,670.34,161,"This closes the loop between our numerical chain-rule examples and the lecture's architecture discussion.","这把我们的链式法则数值例子和本讲的架构讨论联系了起来。"],[670.69,678.88,161,"Information paths, residual connections and long-range dependencies matter both in the forward computation and in learning.","信息通路、残差连接和长程依赖，无论在前向计算还是在学习中都很重要。"],[679.23,684.81,161,"That's all for today. Thank you, and see you in Lecture five on large language models!","今天就到这里。谢谢大家，我们第五讲大语言模型再见！"]]}]};
